&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Manager Business Audit | French Market to lead and support the internal audit activities of the N26 Group, with a focus on the French market and topics such as AML/AFC/KYC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Internal Audit team manages the full audit cycle to ensure operational effectiveness, reliability, and compliance with all applicable policies and regulations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will have the opportunity to participate in strategic projects, develop detailed risk-based audit plans, and ensure compliance with professional and regulatory standards at the highest level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and support all internal business audit activities across the N26 Group, including external service providers and subsidiaries, with a primary focus on the N26 French branch and AML/AFC/KYC topics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and manage the full audit cycle, including risk and control management regarding the effectiveness, reliability, and compliance of business operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and update a comprehensive, risk-based annual audit plan across various business functions (such as Product, Customer Operations, Sales, Marketing, and Partnerships).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft detailed written internal audit reports and present findings and agreed action plans to the Executive Board and relevant committees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and follow up on the timely remediation of audit findings and identified deficiencies within agreed timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to key strategic projects, maintain internal audit policies, and supervise and review the work of junior team members to ensure successful delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you need to be successful:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Background:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Bachelor&#39;s degree or a comparable successfully completed degree in accounting, finance, business administration, economics, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 7 years of solid professional experience as an Internal Auditor in an international, regulated environment, preferably in a bank, another financial institution, or an audit firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience in risk controlling and in the validation of financial and non-financial risks, as well as profound knowledge of French banking, anti-money laundering (AML), and consumer protection regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Skills:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English and French language skills; any other European language is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep understanding of operational and financial controls, online banking processes, retail products, european/french/german regulatory standards (e.g. DORA, EBA, MaRisk, CMF, Arrêté du 3 novembre 2014 relatif au contrôle interne) as well as banking IT systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, organizational talent, and pronounced communication and stakeholder management skills for cross-functional collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strategic mindset combined with a high degree of integrity, independence in executing audit tasks, and a strong bias for action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident use of audit tools, data analytics, and reporting systems; familiarity with agile methodologies is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
