&lt;h1&gt;Anti-Money Laundering Analyst II&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; São Paulo, Brazil&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Team description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Anti-Money Laundering Analyst in our AML Brazil team, you&#39;ll work on the front line of transaction monitoring, reviewing the alerts that tell us when something in a financial pattern doesn&#39;t look right. Your investigations help SumUp spot money laundering and other financial or reputational risks early, and your findings can become reports submitted to regulatory authorities, so your judgement has a real impact on how we meet our obligations in Brazil. You&#39;ll be part of a global AML structure, working with international colleagues every day, which means you&#39;ll share knowledge, learn how financial crime is tackled in other markets and build skills that go well beyond your local team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8LwAYCUtfXQ&quot;&gt;Take a tour of our São Paulo office&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate alerts generated by monitoring systems, review the transactions behind them and document clearly what the evidence shows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare detailed case files and suspicious activity or transaction reports for submission to regulatory authorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot patterns and anomalies that may point to money laundering or other reputational and financial risks, and raise them early&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet the agreed service levels for alert reviews and case turnaround set by team leadership, balancing speed with quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share guidance and support teammates with their investigations, helping the team keep a consistent standard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience in anti-money laundering, ideally within a payment institution, with a track record of investigating alerts and documenting findings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid knowledge of AML regulations and the legal requirements of the financial market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced English for reading technical material and working with international colleagues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A sharp analytical mindset and close attention to detail when assessing whether a pattern points to real risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work under time pressure and to resolve disagreements constructively as part of a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
