&lt;p&gt;Self-employed | Commission-only | Local field sales territory | €100K + potential&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for experienced field salespeople who are comfortable walking into a business, starting a conversation with the owner and winning a new merchant..&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a self-employed Field Sales Consultant, you’ll sell SumUp’s payment, POS and software solutions to small and medium-sized businesses in your local area. You’ll find your own prospects, manage your pipeline and support customers as they get started.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll need experience in cold prospecting and the commitment to spend time out in your territory each week. You’ll manage your own activity, with training and support from SumUp.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll be doing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find new customers through face-to-face visits, door-to-door prospecting and direct outreach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focus on local businesses with strong payment volumes that would benefit from SumUp’s products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ask questions about how each business works and recommend suitable payment, card-processing, hardware, POS and software solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the sale from the first conversation through product demonstrations, objections and closing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help customers get set up and start using their SumUp products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with business owners and ask satisfied customers for referrals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan your visits and follow-ups to make good use of your time in the territory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep your CRM records up to date and track your activity, pipeline and sales results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review progress with your Territory Manager and put feedback into practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Essential&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least one year of field sales experience within sectors such as telecoms, energy, business technology, waste management, security systems or food and beverage supply&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cold prospecting experience, including approaching businesses face to face and finding your own leads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling to small and medium sized businesses and dealing directly with owners or decision makers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of winning new customers and meeting sales targets. We’ll ask you for examples of what you’ve achieved and how.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to manage a sale from the first approach to closing, including handling questions and objections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good organisation and consistent follow up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to handle rejection, learn from feedback and keep going.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An understanding of self employment and a willingness to commit the time needed to build your customer base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A base location within easy reach of your agreed territory so you can meet prospects and customers regularly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Desirable&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An existing network of local business owners who could benefit from SumUp’s products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, merchant services, POS or EPOS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Phone sales experience is useful, but you must also have sold face to face in the field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Earnings&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a self-employed, commission-only opportunity with no basic salary. Earnings are uncapped and depend on your individual sales performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The commission package supplied for this draft includes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payments: 50% of annualised payments net revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hardware: 50% of hardware revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software: 50% of annual software revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Residual income: 25% of SumUp net revenue, paid monthly for up to five years.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New-partner incentive: three times the usual residual earnings during the first three months.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional milestone bonuses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Training and support&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ll help you get to know the products and how to sell them, with onboarding and ongoing support covering prospecting, sales conversations, demonstrations, objections and customer onboarding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your Territory Manager will also support you with territory planning, pipeline reviews and coaching in the field.&lt;/p&gt;
