&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Group Financial Controller&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team: Finance, Reporting &amp;amp; Controlling | &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: Sofia, Bulgaria (office first)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Group Reporting and Controlling team is the backbone of SumUp&#39;s financial integrity, and as the business scales, its role in strengthening governance and reporting standards is becoming more critical than ever. This position gives an experienced controller real ownership over a portfolio of legal entities, direct influence on how SumUp standardises controls and reporting across regions, and a front row seat to the audit and governance work that comes with holding ourselves to the highest financial standards. It&#39;s a chance to shape how a fast growing fintech gets its financial house in order, working closely with the Head of Controlling and coordinating directly with external auditors at PwC.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Take a look inside our&lt;a href=&quot;https://youtu.be/gqtjm5NUXs0?si=t7YARvQWQHHidD_z&quot;&gt; Sofia office&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own statutory audits and reporting compliance for a set of legal entities, including regular financial and balance sheet health checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review accounting entries and reconciliations critically, with a focus on accuracy in high impact areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead month end closing activities in complex, high judgement areas such as transfer pricing and chargebacks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the annual closing process for designated entities and financial areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate directly with our external auditors and other stakeholders on audit and technical matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare ad hoc reports on legal entity performance and jurisdictional requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of financial reporting principles under IFRS and GAAP underpins the way you approach controlling work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning a legal entity end to end, from balance sheet reviews to statutory compliance, comes naturally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with stakeholders across tax, accounting, FP&amp;amp;A, and audit teams to resolve complex issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to break down ambiguous problems, spot the real blockers, and drive them to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A qualified accounting background (ACCA or CIMA are a big plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
