&lt;p&gt;SumUp is preparing to build a CRR (Capital Requirements Regulation) licensed bank in Germany—an important next chapter in our journey to help small businesses thrive. As Managing Director, Front Office, you’ll be part of the team that shapes how this bank serves customers: the proposition we bring to market, the products we build, and the standards by which we grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a rare opportunity to take an executive management role in a new, digitally native bank. You’ll combine commercial leadership with direct accountability for customer-facing governance, and represent the market perspective in dialogue with supervisors. We’re looking for a leader who sees customer trust and sustainable growth as inseparable—and who can build with the pace of a technology company and the discipline of a bank.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Together with the other members of the executive management team contribute to the strategic and corporate development of the bank.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the market facing part for the German banking licence application. Represent the bank in supervisory dialogue on commercial strategy, products, distribution and customer treatment, including with BaFin, Deutsche Bundesbank and the European Central Bank where relevant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support building&amp;nbsp; the go to market operating model and ensure it is integrated into the bank’s governance, risk and control framework. Work closely with the Managing Director, Back Office (Geschäftsleiter Marktfolge) to ensure product, conduct and outsourcing risks are understood and managed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the wider SumUp and bank leadership teams—including Finance, Global Banking, Product and Engineering—to turn the strategy into a viable, well-governed business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach the next generation of SumUp leaders on their path to a §25c Abs 1 KWG qualification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll be great for this role if…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring 15 - 20+ years of senior leadership experience in credit institutions, including the qualification according to §25c Abs. 1 KWG.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have led commercial, product or customer activity in a regulated bank and can show how you balanced business performance with customer outcomes, conduct requirements and effective controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a practical understanding of German and European banking regulation, including the requirements relevant to governance, product oversight, market conduct and customer protection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re fluent in German and have excellent English skills. You can engage credibly with supervisors, communicate complex issues clearly and raise difficult topics early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring sound judgement, integrity and the independence of mind expected of a bank executive, and can meet the applicable fitness and propriety requirements for the appointment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable building in a fast-moving environment where there may be limited precedent. You can establish the right foundations without slowing the business down with unnecessary processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in merchant or SME banking, payments, lending, embedded finance, digital banking or API-led products would be especially valuable. So would experience building a new regulated entity or scaling a fintech, specialist lender or digital bank.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ll need to commit the capacity expected of a full-time executive board role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ll help shape a new bank for the businesses that keep local economies moving.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ll have the influence to define its commercial direction and customer proposition, while building the governance and trust that let it grow for the long term.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It’s a chance to bring together your banking experience and your builder mindset at a defining moment for SumUp.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Application Tip&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
