&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Financial Analyst – Revenue Streams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Finance, FGL – Financial General Ledger | Sofia, Bulgaria (office first)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Financial General Ledger (FGL) team sits at the strategic core of SumUp&#39;s financial operations. We&#39;re not your typical accounting team , we own the financial integrity of SumUp&#39;s core business, ensuring every euro of revenue and cost from our lending, payments, and merchant banking products is accurately captured and analyzed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As SumUp scales exponentially, lending volumes growing, our work has evolved into a highly analytical, data-driven function. We combine deep accounting knowledge with SQL queries, AI-assisted reconciliation tools, and advanced data analytics to understand not just what was recorded, but why and how our business operates financially. This is analytical accounting at its core you&#39;ll analyze product mechanics, trace complex payment flows, and use technology to automate routine work, freeing you to focus on the analytical challenges that matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This senior role is the technical anchor of the FGL team: you&#39;ll drive reconciliation quality, solve the toughest accounting puzzles, mentor junior teammates, and shape how we scale our processes intelligently, from our modern&lt;a href=&quot;https://youtu.be/gqtjm5NUXs0?si=t7YARvQWQHHidD_z&quot;&gt; Sofia office&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of complex reconciliations within one of SumUp&#39;s revenue streams such as lending, e-money or merchant banking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate mismatches and data gaps between backoffice systems, ledgers and cash flows, and resolve them at the root cause rather than case by case&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review postings and reconciliations completed by junior colleagues, checking for accuracy, completeness and audit ready documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Post complex accrual, impairment and revenue recognition entries, and support month-end close within tight deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with Product, Controlling and other teams to understand how systems and data connect, and where improvements are needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build structured tracking and documentation for open reconciling items and controls, supporting SumUp&#39;s move towards a stronger control environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong accounting background gained in an international company or audit firm, comfortable with financial reporting, GL entries and revenue recognition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience investigating and resolving reconciliation mismatches across high-volume, complex data sets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort reviewing colleagues&#39; work and giving clear, constructive feedback, without needing to be in a formal leadership role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine curiosity about how systems and processes connect, with the confidence to ask questions and dig into unfamiliar territory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to reach out proactively to teams like Product and Controlling to get to the bottom of an issue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌍 Opportunity to work with SumUppers globally on large-scale fintech products used by millions of businesses worldwide, from our modern Sofia office. This involves an office-first setup&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone&#39;s perspectives are respected and embraced&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚀 Enrolment onto our Virtual Stock Option programme: you&#39;ll own a stake in SumUp&#39;s future success&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 A dedicated annual L&amp;amp;D budget of €2000 and 10 paid days of educational leave, which can be used to attend conferences and/or advance your career through further education&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏖 Generous time off: 25 days of paid leave, plus one extra day per year of service (up to 35), along with public holidays and special leave options&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏥 Peace of mind: additional health insurance and life insurance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💪 Stay active: on-site yoga and a co-sponsored Multisport card offering access to hundreds of sports facilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🍽 Meal support: benefit from a tax-free food voucher program plus flexibility via our Re:Benefits platform&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚌 Easy commute: free shuttle buses connecting directly to Joliot-Curie metro station&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌴 Break4me: 1-month sabbatical after 3 years of service&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🔗 Referral Bonus: earn additional rewards by referring talented individuals to join the SumUp team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
