&lt;li&gt;Over 2,800 Tideans globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognised with Great Place to Work certification three years in a row, and among India’s Top 50 Best Workplaces in Banking, Financial Services, and Insurance in 2026&lt;br&gt;We have offices in Central London, with a member support and technology centre in Sofia, Bulgaria, technology centres in Serbia, Romania, Lithuania and Hyderabad and offices in Gurugram, New Delhi, Berlin, Paris and Luxembourg&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE TEAM:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Company Formation (CoFo) team manages business registration and incorporation across multiple countries and jurisdictions by integrating with local government and third-party providers, and collaborating with strategic partners to utilize market-specific capabilities. Beyond registration, CoFo oversees the complete member onboarding lifecycle, ensuring cross-domain functionality and operability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To support our expansion into registering existing businesses and incorporating new ones in countries like Germany and France, the team is restructuring into two specialized focus areas:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established Markets: Dedicated to core operations in the UK.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New Markets: A newly established team focused on scaling operations across Germany (DE) and France (FR).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position is critical to our growth and receives strong visibility from executive leadership. Because company formation is directly tied to new member onboarding, any friction in the process risks permanently losing prospective members. Consequently, building resilient, observable, and gracefully degradable services is essential for acquiring new members and successfully scaling into new markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and own the end-to-end delivery of company formation and business registration within the New Markets team, ensuring full compliance with local regulatory requirements and market-specific nuances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, build, and maintain scalable distributed systems for seamless member onboarding with sustainable long-term strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Established Markets team to extend a reusable core onboarding platform utilizing flexible state machines and market-specific adapters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with product, compliance, and internal operations to define system architecture, execute key deliveries, and ensure all services are highly accurate, supportable, and fully compliant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional engagement across domains to gain a complete understanding of their systems and optimise existing flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and develop team members through active hands-on technical delivery and leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
