&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Tide leverages AI to enhance our hiring experience. You can read more about how we use AI in our recruitment process in our &lt;a href=&quot;https://assets.ctfassets.net/3h69mkdgxn20/5MFtWSdG8YLKq3jZkK52NY/3f18633073e6cdbd03bba4b9791c64f4/Using_AI_throughout_the_Hiring_Process.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AI Policy&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Your personal data will be processed by Tide for recruitment purposes and in accordance with &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://assets.ctfassets.net/3h69mkdgxn20/30JAUcDJMlaCwUKt4zoW0j/dd541981a67b6838d6e54537704bc8aa/Tide_Recruitment_Privacy_Notice_Job_Post_Version.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://assets.ctfassets.net/3h69mkdgxn20/1MYf6q4ZMWugpeaROVETBN/526e9c160a2de03576413c81657c6466/Recruitment_Privacy_Notice__Final_Draft__Sep_2024_.pdf&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Tide&#39;s Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BOUT TIDE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tide, we help SMEs save time and money in the running of their businesses by not only offering business accounts and related banking services, but also a comprehensive set of highly usable and connected administrative solutions, from invoicing to accounting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tide is transforming the small business banking market and now supports over 2 million members globally across the UK, Germany and France.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Using advanced technology, all solutions are designed with SMEs in mind. With quick onboarding, low fees and innovative features, we thrive on making data driven decisions to serve our mission: to help SMEs save time and money so they can get back to doing what they love.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tide facts:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tide is available for UK, German and French SMEs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Over 2 million members globally and rapidly growing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Over $300 million raised in funding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3,000 Tideans globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have offices in Central London, with a member support and technology centre in Sofia, Bulgaria, technology centres in Serbia, Romania, Lithuania and Hyderabad and offices in Gurugram, New Delhi, Berlin, Paris and Luxembourg&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT THE TEAM:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Commercial Finance and FP&amp;amp;A team plays a pivotal role in shaping the future of Tide — enabling data-driven decisions that accelerate growth and optimise performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a strategic partner to the business, we combine deep financial expertise with strong commercial acumen to deliver impactful support across all functions. From analysing complex data to influencing high-stakes decisions, we are at the forefront of driving value in one of the most exciting and dynamic sectors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a highly analytical, commercially minded FP&amp;amp;A Manager to own key parts of our planning, forecasting and performance reporting cycle. You will be a trusted finance partner to senior leaders, turning numbers into clear insights that shape decisions. This is a high-impact role: you will make sure our investments, including people, line up with our strategic and financial goals. You’ll need strong financial modelling skills, a rigorous approach to process and automation, and the confidence to challenge and influence stakeholders across the business. You thrive on ambiguity and take full ownership of a process or workflow from start to finish, building the structure and policies yourself without waiting for direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate in this role will be focused on the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own key parts of the annual budget, quarterly reforecast and long-range planning cycles, from setting assumptions to final sign-off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead month-end performance reporting, including detailed variance analysis against budget and previous forecasts, with a clear explanation of what drove each variance and the outlook for the rest of the year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, maintain and improve driver-based financial models in our planning system (Aleph) that link operational drivers to P&amp;amp;L, EBITDA and cash outcomes. Act as a subject matter expert for the system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run scenario and sensitivity analysis and provide financial modelling and decision support on major initiatives, including organisational design, location strategy and large-scale investments, testing the impact of different growth, cost and investment options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a Finance Business Partner to budget holders. Analyse spend and assumptions, support investment cases, and help leaders make informed trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the forecasting of people costs, including headcount, compensation, bonus and equity. Work with the People and Total Rewards teams so these costs are fully and accurately reflected in the plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain financial control over headcount and hiring approvals so that open roles stay in line with approved budgets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flag risks and opportunities to the forecast early, using real-time operational data from source systems such as Workday and Greenhouse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare insight-led reporting and investor/board materials for senior leadership, leading with conclusions supported by data. Build and automate the reports and dashboards behind them to cut manual effort and speed up decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and analyse key business and cost-efficiency metrics, translating operational data into a financial story.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and launch new FP&amp;amp;A processes and policies independently, from scoping requirements through to adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement in FP&amp;amp;A processes, data quality and tooling, including integrations between Aleph and our core finance and operational systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of progressive experience in FP&amp;amp;A, corporate finance or a similar role, ideally in a fast-growth tech or scale-up business. Experience with headcount or people-cost planning is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of owning core FP&amp;amp;A processes from start to finish, including budgeting, re-forecasting, long-range planning and month-end reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build and maintain driver-based financial models, including people-cost and compensation drivers, that connect operating activity to financial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated end-to-end ownership of an ambiguous process. This means taking a loosely defined problem, scoping the requirements yourself, designing the process, getting stakeholders to adopt it, and keeping it running over time with minimal direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent business partnering skills with budget holders and senior leaders, with the confidence to challenge assumptions and influence decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel/Google Sheets skills and hands-on experience with dedicated FP&amp;amp;A planning tools (e.g. Aleph, Anaplan, Adaptive, Pigment).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data skills, including hands-on SQL for pulling and analysing complex datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A systems mindset, with experience managing data flows between the planning tool and source systems such as the ERP/GL, HRIS (e.g. Workday) or ATS (e.g. Greenhouse).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional ability to turn complex financial analysis into clear, actionable insight for both finance and non-finance audiences, including the Executive Team and the Board.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;WHAT YOU’LL GET IN RETURN:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our location-specific employee benefits are designed to cater to the unique needs of Tideans:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive Compensation -&amp;nbsp; Competitive salary and share options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time Off – Generous annual leave on top of bank holidays.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental Leave – Paid maternity, paternity, and adoption leave to support your family journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sabbatical – Extended unpaid and paid leave options after completing milestone years with Tide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health Insurance – Private family insurance with additional OPD coverage and top-up options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life &amp;amp; Accident Cover – Comprehensive accidental and life insurance protection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental Wellbeing – Access to therapy sessions, courses, meditations, and workshops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteering &amp;amp; Development Days – Paid days annually for volunteering or personal growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning &amp;amp; Development – Annual budget for books, courses, coaching, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;WOO (Work Outside the Office) – Work from abroad for up to 90 days annually.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home Office Setup – Contribution towards setting up your home office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Laptop Ownership – Keep your old laptop and get a new one when it’s time for a replacement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Snacks &amp;amp; Meals – Office perks with snacks, coffee, tea, and lunch (location dependent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;TIDEAN WAYS OF WORKING&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tide, we champion a &lt;strong&gt;flexible workplace &lt;/strong&gt;model that&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;supports both in-person and remote work to cater to the specific needs of our different teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While remote work is supported, we believe in the power of face-to-face interactions to foster team spirit and collaboration. Our offices are designed as hubs for innovation and team-building, where we encourage regular in-person gatherings to foster a strong sense of community.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
