&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BOUT TIDE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tide, we help SMEs save time and money in the running of their businesses by not only offering business accounts and related banking services, but also a comprehensive set of highly usable and connected administrative solutions, from invoicing to accounting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tide is transforming the small business banking market and now supports over 2 million members globally across the UK, Germany and France.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Using advanced technology, all solutions are designed with SMEs in mind. With quick onboarding, low fees and innovative features, we thrive on making data driven decisions to serve our mission: to help SMEs save time and money so they can get back to doing what they love.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tide facts:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tide is available for UK, German and French SMEs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Over 2 million members globally and rapidly growing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Over $300 million raised in funding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3,000 Tideans globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have offices in Central London, with a member support and technology centre in Sofia, Bulgaria, technology centres in Serbia, Romania, Lithuania and Hyderabad and offices in Gurugram, New Delhi, Berlin, Paris and Luxembourg&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here at Tide, we are looking for a seasoned Manager who&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;has a good understanding of the Trust and Safety domain with expertise in an e-commerce environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to operate in a fast paced growing product line within Tide called Commercial Services that primarily focus on enabling Small and Medium Enterprises (SME Businesses) to sell their products online&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;has understanding on Financial Crime Typologies including money laundering, fraud, online safety, trust and safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is passionate and proactive, who will help ensure Tide is taking all relevant steps to detect and prevent all aspects of fraud, financial crime.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;understands Trust and Safety in the context of financial crime in a global financial set up with specific focus towards UK and Europe geography.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;has exceptional communication skills in English (both Written and Speaking).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;can motivate the team and work in an extremely fast paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;can use expert judgement to recommend articulating risks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Manager Commercial Services (AML&amp;amp;PA), you’ll be:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Leadership and Operational Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, scale, and empower a high-performing team of Trust and Safety Specialists who also will work on AML Transaction Monitoring and Payment Sanctions Screening&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Primary focus will be towards Trust &amp;amp; Safety operations but the role scope will cover AML Transaction Monitoring and Payment Sanctions Screening.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive operational excellence across ongoing monitoring, alert review, and risk assessment workflows to maintain strict SLA compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define performance metrics, oversee talent development, and champion continuous training in Trust and Safety Risks and financial crime typologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish resource allocation strategies to efficiently balance operational workload and backlogs across financial services oversight.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Risk Governance and Quality Assurance:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the final internal escalation authority for complex Trust &amp;amp; Safety investigations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure robust control mechanisms are in place to address evolving financial crime and trust threats specific to Commercial Services product offerings (online listings)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extreme ownership in leading conversations with cross functional stakeholders such as Product Development team, engineering teams, policy and procedures to drive a rapidly growing product line&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and prioritize alert backlogs to mitigate risk and ensure timely resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Subject Matter Expertise and Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain deep domain expertise in financial services, Online safety Act, international sanctions screening regimes, and AML risks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic oversight on emerging Trust and Safety standards, financial crime typologies, and illegal transaction pattern detection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a subject matter expert (SME) on complex cases, offering guidance on investigation strategies and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Optimization and System Enhancements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Engineering, and Analytics teams to optimize automated rules to detect risks related to Trust and Safety standards and financial crime typologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage data analytics to identify risk trends, eliminate operational bottlenecks, and minimize false positives in payments sanctions screening.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze data to identify trends, patterns, and inefficiencies, and recommend solutions to reduce false positives and improve detection effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Management and Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present strategic KPI metrics, risk assessments, and performance dashboards to senior executive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as key liaison across 2nd Line of Defence, Legal, Regulatory Compliance, and external financial partners for UK and EU markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in preparing for internal and external audits and regulatory examinations where applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with employees of partner banks (other than Tide)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;br&gt;WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 8+ years of experience in a Trust and Safety Domain. Any experience within Transaction monitoring, Financial Crime risk related role in financial services will be a great advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 5+ years of managerial experience leading teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuinely curious mindset, asking the right questions at the right times, with a problem solving attitude.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a keen eye for process improvements, looking how we can work leaner and more robustly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have an analytical mind and are able to digest large data sets and spot patterns and trends with ease&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a quick learner, explorer and multitasker&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have exceptional communication skills, written and verbal. Are able to communicate with our members, internal stakeholders &amp;amp; regulatory bodies if required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have C1/C2 level of spoken and written English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CAMS, ICA (or similar industry certifications) will be considered as an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;br&gt;WHAT YOU’LL GET IN RETURN:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days paid annual leave&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3 paid days off for volunteering or L&amp;amp;D activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal L&amp;amp;D budget&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional health &amp;amp; dental insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental wellbeing platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Snacks, light food, drinks in the office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;WFH equipment allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;TIDE IS A PLACE FOR EVERYONE&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tide, we believe that we can only succeed if we let our differences enrich our culture. Our Tideans come from a variety of backgrounds and experience levels. We consider everyone irrespective of their ethnicity, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, family or parental status, national origin, veteran, neurodiversity or differently-abled status. We celebrate diversity in our workforce as a cornerstone of our success. Our commitment to a broad spectrum of ideas and backgrounds is what enables us to build products that resonate with our members’ diverse needs and lives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are One Team and foster a transparent and inclusive environment, where everyone’s voice is heard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
