&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BOUT TIDE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tide, we help SMEs save time and money in the running of their businesses by not only offering business accounts and related banking services, but also a comprehensive set of highly usable and connected administrative solutions, from invoicing to accounting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tide is transforming the small business banking market and now supports over 2 million members globally across the UK, Germany and France.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Using advanced technology, all solutions are designed with SMEs in mind. With quick onboarding, low fees and innovative features, we thrive on making data driven decisions to serve our mission: to help SMEs save time and money so they can get back to doing what they love.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tide facts:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tide is available for UK, German and French SMEs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Over 2 million members globally and rapidly growing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Over $300 million raised in funding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3,000 Tideans globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have offices in Central London, with a member support and technology centre in Sofia, Bulgaria, technology centres in Serbia, Romania, Lithuania and Hyderabad and offices in Gurugram, New Delhi, Berlin, Paris and Luxembourg&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT THE TEAM:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Platform Engineering team builds the tools, infrastructure and ‘golden paths’ that let Tide’s engineers ship safely and quickly. We own everything from CI/CD pipelines and developer tooling to Tide’s service catalogue, including the Developer Productivity function, and our mission is to make the right way the easy way for every engineer at Tide — human or AI agent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;br&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Engineering Manager, Developer Experience / Head of Developer Experience, you will report directly to the Director of Platform Engineering and be responsible for how every engineer at Tide builds, tests and ships software. You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Developer Experience strategy for Tide, setting the vision and roadmap for developer tooling, CI/CD and the internal platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design, build and continuous improvement of CI/CD pipelines and developer tooling, reducing friction and lead time across the software delivery lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, track and report on DevEx and engineering productivity metrics (e.g. DORA, SPACE), using data to identify bottlenecks and prioritise investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve Tide’s service catalogue (Backstage), establishing it as the single source of truth for the ICT Asset Register and driving adoption across engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the Developer Productivity function, responsible for building and maintaining Java/Spring and Python ‘paved road’ templates that give product teams a fast, secure and consistent way to start new services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the internally developed libraries for authentication and other common functionality, ensuring they are well documented, kept up to date, and widely adopted across product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, lead and mentor a team of platform, developer experience and developer productivity engineers, fostering a culture of ownership, craftsmanship and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare Tide’s engineering platform for agentic development, ensuring our tooling, paved roads and guardrails allow AI coding agents (e.g. Claude Code) to contribute safely and effectively alongside human engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the platform, tooling and operating model for running AI-developed applications in production, covering observability, security, testing and governance for agent-authored code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineering leaders, security and compliance stakeholders across Tide’s product and platform teams to identify friction points and shape the platform roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;br&gt;WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tide is seeking an experienced Head of Developer Experience to lead our efforts in making our engineers as productive and effective as possible. The ideal candidate will have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record leading Developer Experience, Platform Engineering or DevOps/SRE teams at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building and operating CI/CD pipelines and developer tooling in a modern cloud environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Backstage, or a comparable internal developer portal / service catalogue tool, including rollout and adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running a developer productivity or paved-road function, including building and maintaining project templates (e.g. Java/Spring, Python) and shared libraries (e.g. authentication, common functionality) used by product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of engineering productivity frameworks such as DORA metrics or SPACE, and experience using them to drive improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with agentic and AI-assisted development tools (e.g. Claude Code, GitHub Copilot), and a point of view on the guardrails, governance and infrastructure needed to run AI-developed applications safely in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong people leadership skills, with a track record of building, growing and developing high-performing engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, able to influence engineering leaders across multiple teams and locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in financial services or another regulated, technology-driven scale-up environment is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;OUR TECH STACK&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
