&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Product Analyst ( Member Acquisition Marketing )&lt;/strong&gt;, you’ll be responsible for managing insights projects related to member growth &amp;amp; acquisition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;As a Product Analyst you’ll be:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Presenting insights to stakeholders &amp;amp; senior management, translating analysis into the &#39;so what?&#39; and identifying possible actions to take as a result&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using your SQL/Python expertise to interrogate our data to solve key business problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focusing on improving performance marketing and growth initiatives by providing full stack descriptive to prescriptive analytics via cutting edge technologies to support business objectives&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to deal with ambiguity &amp;amp; form ambiguous questions into defined solutions to improve the business area&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support to build analytics roadmap for customer strategy, acquisition efficiency, customer lifetime value enhancement and budget optimization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Analytical engineering and Martech to create a holistic view of the members by ensuring seamless integration of various data sources from 3rd party platforms like Google Ads, Facebook Ads, etc.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advising and Support performance marketing stakeholders to provide an accurate view of the member attribution by various channels&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measuring and report performance of all marketing campaigns, and assess ROI and other key KPIs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting Analytics leadership in prioritisation and identification of various business cases&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Refine work items with the business to the point where they can be worked upon and ensure timely and quality deliverables&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion powerful storytelling, prioritisation, commercial and growth mindset&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Presenting insights to stakeholders &amp;amp; senior management, translating analysis into the &#39;so what?&#39; and identifying possible actions to take as a result&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What makes you a great fit:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience working in the analytics team of a digital product. Experience working in fintech firms preferred ( not mandatory)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience in Performance Marketing is mandatory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a sound understanding of how the different digital Marketing tools work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a good understanding of digital marketing, A/B testing, Google Analytics, Appsflyer, etc.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a good understanding of Multi touch attribution, Marketing Mix Modelling, Cohort Analysis, Customer Lifetime Value.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have excellent leadership skills - you can drive and influence team of analysts, engineers and data scientists without any formal reporting&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong skills on SQL and Visualization tools ( Looker, Tableau, Qlikview etc.)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have great Storytelling skills and the ability to explain complex analytical concepts to business users&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
