&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BOUT TIDE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tide, we help SMEs save time and money in the running of their businesses by not only offering business accounts and related banking services, but also a comprehensive set of highly usable and connected administrative solutions, from invoicing to accounting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tide is transforming the small business banking market and now supports over 2 million members globally across the UK, Germany and France.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Using advanced technology, all solutions are designed with SMEs in mind. With quick onboarding, low fees and innovative features, we thrive on making data driven decisions to serve our mission: to help SMEs save time and money so they can get back to doing what they love.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tide facts:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tide is available for UK, German and French SMEs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Over 2 million members globally and rapidly growing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Over $300 million raised in funding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3,000 Tideans globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have offices in Central London, with a member support and technology centre in Sofia, Bulgaria, technology centres in Serbia, Romania, Lithuania and Hyderabad and offices in Gurugram, New Delhi, Berlin, Paris and Luxembourg&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE TEAM:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The SRE team is part of Platform Engineering. Its mission is to own the reliability system: the standards, tooling, and platform services that determine how reliable Tide is by default. We measure success by SLO attainment and the reliability our members experience.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Tide is hiring an Engineering Manager to lead the SRE team that owns our reliability system.&lt;br&gt;As an Engineering Manager, SRE, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead: Hire, coach, and set clear goals for the SRE team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define SLOs: Agree SLOs with service owners and run the error budget policy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own observability: Run the observability platform 24/7 in production, including SLOs and platform alerting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Release safely: Build deployment guardrails such as canary rollouts and auto-rollback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build resilience: Detect partner degradation early with synthetic monitoring and vendor scorecards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remove toil: Automate manual incident work, such as recording incident timelines and drafting status updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fix systemically: Turn post-mortem findings and incident patterns into cross-cutting platform fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure outcomes: Track SLO attainment and member-facing reliability metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support: Advise product engineering teams on reliability.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An Engineering Leader with a strong engineering mindset who simplifies problems and looks for optimal solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Professional who wants to own real systems in production and be measured on outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in software engineering or infrastructure engineering roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years in engineering leadership roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of SLIs, SLOs, SLAs, and error budgets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience instrumenting Java, Python, and Go services with OpenTelemetry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Terraform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Kubernetes, AWS, and Java&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with canary rollouts, auto-rollback, and auto-scaling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of reliability patterns such as retries, backoffs, DLQs, the transactional outbox, and feature flags&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to plan, prioritise, and manage expectations, particularly during incidents and retrospectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running blameless retrospectives that uncover the root cause of complex issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OUR TECH STACK:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud: AWS and Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infrastructure as code: Terraform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Observability: OpenTelemetry and Coralogix&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Service catalogue: Backstage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backend: Java, Python, and Go&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivery: Canary rollouts, auto-rollback, auto-scaling, and feature flags&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL GET IN RETURN:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote first&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The gross annual salary for this position ranges from 94,000 to 100,000 EUR but we are also open to discussing the salary further, taking into account your expertise and contributions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days of paid annual leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3 paid days off for volunteering or L&amp;amp;D activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private Health Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental Health Support Platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FitPass&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family and friendly leave (according to statutory)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal L&amp;amp;D budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TIDEAN WAYS OF WORKING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tide, we champion a flexible workplace model that supports both in-person and remote work to cater to the specific needs of our different teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While remote work is supported, we believe in the power of face-to-face interactions to foster team spirit and collaboration. Our offices are designed as hubs for innovation and team-building, where we encourage regular in-person gatherings to foster a strong sense of community.&lt;/p&gt;
