&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Your personal data will be processed by Tide for recruitment purposes and in accordance with &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://assets.ctfassets.net/3h69mkdgxn20/30JAUcDJMlaCwUKt4zoW0j/dd541981a67b6838d6e54537704bc8aa/Tide_Recruitment_Privacy_Notice_Job_Post_Version.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://assets.ctfassets.net/3h69mkdgxn20/1MYf6q4ZMWugpeaROVETBN/526e9c160a2de03576413c81657c6466/Recruitment_Privacy_Notice__Final_Draft__Sep_2024_.pdf&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Tide&#39;s Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BOUT TIDE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tide, we help SMEs save time and money in the running of their businesses by not only offering business accounts and related banking services, but also a comprehensive set of highly usable and connected administrative solutions, from invoicing to accounting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tide is transforming the small business banking market and now supports over 2 million members globally across the UK, Germany and France.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Using advanced technology, all solutions are designed with SMEs in mind. With quick onboarding, low fees and innovative features, we thrive on making data driven decisions to serve our mission: to help SMEs save time and money so they can get back to doing what they love.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tide facts:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tide is available for UK, German and French SMEs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Over 2 million members globally and rapidly growing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Over $300 million raised in funding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3,000 Tideans globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have offices in Central London, with a member support and technology centre in Sofia, Bulgaria, technology centres in Serbia, Romania, Lithuania and Hyderabad and offices in Gurugram, New Delhi, Berlin, Paris and Luxembourg&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE TEAM&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;The Ledger team owns the core ledger. It&#39;s the system of record behind every account, balance and payment at Tide. Payments, cards and lending all sit on top of it. If it&#39;s slow or wrong, members can&#39;t pay people, and that hits their business directly. The team works on this one problem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Tide is growing into new markets and new products, and the ledger has to scale with that. We&#39;re rewriting it and migrating to the new version. The goals are better performance for members and a foundation that keeps up as volumes and products grow. You&#39;ll help design it and deliver it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role in one team, working on one problem. You&#39;ll do architecture, system design, coding and mentoring. You won&#39;t have direct reports, but you&#39;ll own the technical direction of the ledger. You&#39;ll partner closely with the team&#39;s Engineering Manager and Product Manager, and lead by example.&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re also changing how we build and test. The team uses AI and agentic tools to deliver working software. We&#39;re applying the same approach to functional and performance testing, so we can deliver this work in a fraction of the time it would have taken before. You&#39;ll help shape how that works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL BE DOING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and own the architecture of the new ledger, and make the trade-off calls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write production code and review the team&#39;s, so the quality bar is clear&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and lead the migration from the current ledger: staged rollouts, parallel running, reconciliation and rollback, with a small blast radius for every change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI and agentic tools to deliver faster, and help build AI-assisted functional and performance testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own performance and reliability: latency budgets, SLOs and capacity as volumes grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and coach engineers at every level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Engineering Manager and Product Manager, and with the teams that build on the ledger&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to our Communities of Practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience and background:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve built and run high-volume, real-time distributed systems with hard constraints, such as the time allowed to authorise a transaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve worked on systems that are too important to fail, where an outage stops customers doing business. That could be in payments, FX, trading, gambling, finance or similar. Payments or banking experience is a bonus, not a requirement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve changed critical systems safely: rewrites, migrations and rollouts where you kept the blast radius small&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve used agentic AI tools such as Claude to deliver working software, and changed how you work to get the best out of them. You believe in this approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve mentored other engineers and set technical direction for a team, without being their line manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical depth:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong backend engineering in a strongly typed language. Java is preferred, but design and architecture skills matter more than the language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Distributed systems: consistency, idempotency, concurrency, ordering and failure modes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relational databases at scale, ideally PostgreSQL: transactions, locking, and data modelling for correctness and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance engineering: profiling, latency budgets and load testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Event-driven and asynchronous design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Running services in a cloud-native environment (we are AWS-heavy)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Testing: functional, performance and resilience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you work:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You make pragmatic trade-offs and can explain them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You lead by example&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You coach and develop the engineers around you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You use your authority well: you explain your decisions and bring people with you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can talk to non-technical stakeholders without losing precision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our tech stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Java and PostgreSQL, running on AWS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Event-driven architecture with messaging over SNS and SQS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Observability with Coralogix&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GitHub for CI/CD with automated testing and security scanning. New joiners typically have something in production within their first two weeks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI coding and agentic tools, including Claude, as part of everyday engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL GET IN RETURN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days paid annual leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3 paid days off for volunteering or L&amp;amp;D activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The gross annual salary for this position ranges from 90,000 to 101,250 EUR but we are also open to discussing the salary further, taking into account your expertise and contributions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended maternity and paternity leave covered by the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal L&amp;amp;D budget in the amount of 500 EUR per year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional health &amp;amp; dental insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental wellbeing platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully covered Multisports card&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Food vouchers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Snacks, light food, drinks in the office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;WFH equipment allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working from home&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sabbatical Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TIDEAN WAYS OF WORKING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Tide, we champion a flexible workplace model that supports both in-person and remote work to cater to the specific needs of our different teams. While remote work is supported, we believe in the power of face-to-face interactions to foster team spirit and collaboration. Our offices are designed as hubs for innovation and team-building, where we encourage regular in-person gatherings to foster a strong sense of community.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;TIDE IS A PLACE FOR EVERYONE&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tide, we believe that we can only succeed if we let our differences enrich our culture. Our Tideans come from a variety of backgrounds and experience levels. We consider everyone irrespective of their ethnicity, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, family or parental status, national origin, veteran, neurodiversity or differently-abled status. We celebrate diversity in our workforce as a cornerstone of our success. Our commitment to a broad spectrum of ideas and backgrounds is what enables us to build products that resonate with our members’ diverse needs and lives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are One Team and foster a transparent and inclusive environment, where everyone’s voice is heard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Tide, we thrive on diversity, embracing various backgrounds and experiences. We welcome all individuals regardless of ethnicity, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability. Our inclusive culture is key to our success, helping us build products that meet our members&#39; diverse needs. We are One Team, committed to transparency and ensuring everyone’s voice is heard.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
