&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TransferGo&lt;/strong&gt; is a growing fintech scale-up on a mission to champion financial freedom with care. We strive to provide tailored, more affordable financial services that make people&#39;s hard-earned money go further. Now in our 14th year, with close to 400 employees in offices across Europe and the UK, we’re crafting a brilliant, relevant product that makes a difference in people&#39;s lives and the well-being of their families.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ve come this far by building a talented, diverse workforce on a fair culture and our strong values. Having this strong team of employees, we can serve those who really need our product to make their lives better.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;sec&quot;&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;sec&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The TransferGo Card is a Visa debit card, virtual and physical, and it works with Apple Pay and Google Pay. It&#39;s live in the UK, and more countries are coming.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work between product, engineering, our card partners and the rest of the business, and pick up the work that falls between them. You&#39;ll agree priorities with our PM for cards and subscriptions, then run with them. One month you might be working out why cardholders don&#39;t activate and what would change that. The next you might be running a country launch with Engineering, Legal, Marketing, Compliance and our partners. When the same job comes round a second time, you&#39;ll build the tracker, dashboard or automation so it doesn&#39;t need a person the third time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cards also come with rules we don&#39;t write. Card schemes set deadlines, Apple and Google certify every wallet launch, and partners have their own requirements. You&#39;ll make sure none of it gets missed, and that as little of it as possible is done by hand.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our PM for cards and subscriptions decides what we build and launch. Engineering owns how it gets built. You run card operations day to day: the projects you take on, from the first question to a shipped and measured result, and the systems that keep cards running without extra meetings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;sec&quot;&gt;&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;sec&quot;&gt;&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like after six months&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve shipped two or three projects that moved card activation, active cardholders or spend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scheme deadlines, partner requests and launch tasks all live in one system you built, and nobody hears about one late.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least one weekly manual job in Cards is now done by an automation or tool you built.
&lt;section class=&quot;sec&quot;&gt;&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
