&lt;div class=&quot;group&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own problems end to end&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a problem from a vague question to a shipped, measured result. Scope it, bring in the right people, run it and close it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use SQL and Amplitude to find where cardholders drop off between ordering, activating and spending, and work out what a fix is worth. Come with a recommendation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read support contacts and partner reports, rank what&#39;s hurting customers, and make sure each item has an owner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build with AI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build what the team needs yourself. For example, a tool that turns each new scheme bulletin into a short summary with draft tasks and deadlines, or a weekly card dashboard leadership reads instead of asking for updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype product ideas before engineering commits to them, so the PM can decide with something real in front of them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep cards running&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run card launches and wallet certifications with Engineering, Legal, Marketing, Compliance and our partners, from one tracker with one readiness date and an owner for every item.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep our scheme mandate tracker up to date, and turn each bulletin or partner notice into tasks with owners and dates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work through operational issues with our card partners. When something needs escalating, write it in three lines: what we need, by when, and what it blocks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
