&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Bridge team helps businesses build and scale stablecoin-powered financial products and global money movement through a single API. Our virtual accounts let international consumers and businesses access, store, and spend US dollars, while our payouts infrastructure helps platforms disburse funds globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We collaborate across product, compliance, legal, and operations as we develop Stripe Crypto’s go-to-market approach and build a durable sales culture. Our team has built financial infrastructure at Coinbase, Square, Brex, Upstart, DoorDash, and Airbnb, and we’re focused on making stablecoins a practical foundation for global payments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Executive (New Business), you’ll help grow Bridge by turning qualified demand and outbound prospecting into successful customer relationships. You’ll own the commercial journey from first conversation through launch, translating business and technical needs into practical solutions and working with internal partners to deliver strong outcomes. You’ll also use data and field insights to improve how the team sells and how Stripe Crypto scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close qualified inbound leads and develop outbound opportunities through networking, cold calling, and lead follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead discovery conversations to understand prospects’ business needs and identify relevant Bridge solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full sales cycle, from identifying opportunities through negotiation and close, and partner with customers and internal teams to get them live&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain client relationships that support satisfaction, repeat business, and account growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet or exceed monthly, quarterly, and annual sales targets while providing detailed and accurate sales forecasts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product, risk, operations, and other internal teams to deliver effective solutions for clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and contribute to team projects that develop and refine the sales process and help shape the Bridge and Stripe sales culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-8 years of sales experience managing the full sales cycle for new accounts at a high-growth payments, financial technology, crypto, or technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of exceeding sales quotas, closing net-new and upsell opportunities, and managing complex pricing or commercial negotiations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using data to prioritize accounts, build business cases, and track outcomes, including familiarity with customer relationship management tools, Excel, and basic SQL, or demonstrated comfort with comparable data tools and analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand technical product requirements, explain solutions across multiple technology products, and work with product, risk, and operations teams to deliver customer outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication, negotiation, and relationship-building skills, with the ability to prioritize a high-volume territory and work persistently through ambiguity in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise AEs&lt;/strong&gt; must be in their current role for a minimum of &lt;strong&gt;24 months &lt;/strong&gt;at the time of application.&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Sales AE’s&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;must be in their current role for a minimum of &lt;strong&gt;24 months &lt;/strong&gt;at the time of application.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Velocity AEs&lt;/strong&gt; must be in their current role for a minimum of &lt;strong&gt;18 months &lt;/strong&gt;at the time of application.&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a large book of accounts or a high-velocity sales motion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-office Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an in-office role. Office-assigned Stripes in most of our locations are currently expected to spend at least 50% of the time in a given month in their local office or with users. This expectation may vary depending on role, team and location. This approach helps strike a balance between bringing people together for in-person collaboration and learning from each other, while supporting flexibility when possible.&lt;/p&gt;
