&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work cross-functionally and with different cultures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience with internal controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to be flexible and comfortable with changing requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPA/ CA or similar qualification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical expertise with US GAAP, specifically ASC 606/IFRS 15&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of (or experience in) the technology or payments industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Oracle Suite, SalesForce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Hubble and SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Analytical Tools like- Power BI, Tableau, KNIME, Python, Alteryx&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Finance Operations (FinOps) team provides and enhances core business services that are the backbone for Stripe. FinOps uses data and operational excellence to deliver technology solutions, procurement, billing and payroll services, strategic sourcing, and supplier relationship management to Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced finance professional to join the Accounts Payable team within Finance Operations at the Stripe Delivery Center (SDC). You’ll support accounts payable operations across Stripe’s US and international entities and build expertise in the end-to-end procure-to-pay process. Your work will include processing supplier invoices in Oracle, managing invoice backlogs, and resolving queries from suppliers and internal teams. You’ll partner with Procurement, Vendor Management, Payments, and Accounting to resolve issues and keep payments on track.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll also lead cross-functional automation and process improvement projects to reduce manual work, improve invoice accuracy, shorten processing times, and make it easier for teams to track invoices and queries. As workflows change, you’ll update standard operating procedures and communicate those changes to the teams that rely on them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own invoice processing and AP query management for US and international entities. Become a subject matter expert in the end-to-end procure-to-pay process and related activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process a high volume of supplier invoices in Oracle. Validate invoice details and accounting coding, prioritize invoices by due date and urgency, and meet accuracy and turnaround targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own supplier and internal AP queries from intake through resolution. Investigate invoice discrepancies, holds, potential duplicates, approval delays, and payment-status questions. Keep stakeholders informed and follow up until each issue is resolved.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor aging invoices and backlogs. Escalate invoices at risk of missing payment deadlines and coordinate with Procurement, Vendor Management, and Payments to resolve issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional teams to resolve issues and support accounting and operational activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional automation and process improvement projects that reduce manual work, improve invoice processing accuracy and turnaround times, and give teams better visibility into invoice and query status.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep invoice processing and AP query workflows and standard operating procedures (SOPs) up to date. Document changes and communicate them to the teams that use them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You understand the end-to-end procure-to-pay process and have hands-on experience processing a high volume of supplier invoices in Oracle or a comparable ERP. You manage competing deadlines and invoice backlogs without sacrificing accuracy, and you’ve owned supplier and internal AP queries from intake through resolution. You bring a strong accounting foundation, including general ledger processes, the chart of accounts, account coding, reconciliations, and month-end close. You exercise sound judgment and discretion, apply internal controls and compliance policies consistently, and know when to escalate an issue. You work independently in a fast-changing environment, communicate clearly in writing and in conversation, and collaborate effectively across teams. You take a hands-on approach to solving problems, can lead automation and process improvement projects, and keep standard operating procedures up to date as workflows change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6–8 years of relevant accounts payable experience, preferably at a large multinational or global company, with hands-on experience processing high volumes of supplier invoices and resolving AP queries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of accounting concepts, including accruals, prepayments, and the chart of accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Excel or Google Sheets, with experience analyzing large datasets to investigate discrepancies and make sound decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills and the ability to stay organized while managing competing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to partner with cross-functional teams and follow issues through to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently, take initiative, and deliver accurate results with minimal supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, detail-oriented approach to solving problems and improving processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will also likely have (not required):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working at a high-growth technology or financial services company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Oracle, Zip, or similar enterprise resource planning (ERP), accounting, or procurement systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;knowledge on India TDS/GST/e-invoicing would be an add on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Finance Operations (FinOps) team provides and enhances core business services that are the backbone for Stripe. FinOps uses data and operational excellence to deliver technology solutions, procurement, billing and payroll services, strategic sourcing, and supplier relationship management to Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an Accounts Receivable (AR) Specialist to join our growing team. The AR Specialist will own billing and collections programs for Stripe’s growing mix of products that are invoiced. This role is responsible for projects within the end‑to‑end billing cycle, reconciliation of billing outputs to Finance reporting, and supporting AR collections strategy and improvement. The role works closely with Finance, Sales/GTM, Product, Data/Engineering, and Accounting to ensure invoices are accurate, timely, and collected.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and execute defined Accounts Receivable (AR) programs and projects from planning through delivery, establishing scope, milestones, success measures, and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain project plans, track dependencies, and coordinate cross-functional execution to deliver agreed outcomes on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate AR business priorities into actionable workstreams, aligning stakeholders on requirements, deliverables, and ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify project risks, resolve execution blockers, and escalate decisions or trade-offs with clear recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze AR performance and financial trends to identify gaps, investigate root causes, and recommend targeted improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance, Sales/GTM, Engineering, and other stakeholders to deliver initiatives that improve receivables performance and the customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead process improvement projects that standardize and simplify AR workflows, reduce manual effort, and strengthen controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather business requirements and coordinate the prioritization, testing, and rollout of enhancements in partnership with technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive change management for assigned initiatives, including stakeholder communications, documentation, adoption planning, and post-launch measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and monitor program metrics and leading indicators to measure business performance, delivery progress, and realized benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide concise updates to AR and Finance leadership on program health, milestones, risks, decisions, and results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain program documentation, decision logs, and ownership handoffs to support sustainable outcomes and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and execute subsidiary AR integration projects, aligning stakeholders on requirements, milestones, and dependencies while driving process improvements to standardize workflows, strengthen controls, and improve scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant experience in billing/accounts receivable with usage-based billing platforms or complex SaaS billing systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Excel/Sheets and SQL literacy; comfortable reading billing query outputs and reconciling to invoices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with APIs, simple python scripts, or Retool automations preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with payment methods (ACH, wires, crypto/USDC, Stripe payment links) and cash application best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent attention to detail, organized, and able to manage a heavy month‑end cadence and ad hoc adjustments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and ability to partner cross‑functionally (Sales, Finance, Data, Product, Legal).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to build strong collaborative working relationships with business partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to be a self starter capable of driving business results without significant supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to maintain high performance under tight timelines and a “roll up your sleeves” mindset to get any job done&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to bring structure to ambiguous areas of opportunity and thrive in an unstructured, fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills and demonstrated ability to work independently, analyze problems and data sets to make complex investigation decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated history of taking on various types of challenging projects and producing results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solution-oriented mindset with enthusiasm for establishing best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-disciplined, diligent, proactive and detail oriented&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working at a high-growth technology or financial services company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior exposure to charge-through and pass‑through third‑party fees and complex fee constructs (platform fees, per txn, bps/% pricing, minimums).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working at or supporting fintech or payments companies, especially crypto/stablecoin or cross‑border FX rails&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Databricks, Snowflake, or similar data stacks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Stripe, our Mexico City office is a vibrant hub at the forefront of our mission to reshape the financial landscape for businesses worldwide. Our team prioritizes collaboration, innovation, and excellence. As a member of the Mexico City team, you&#39;ll be part of a mission-driven community dedicated to enhancing the global economy and increasing the GDP of the internet. We strive for excellence by creating with craft and beauty, while having fun and celebrating our successes together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We cultivate a culture of collaboration, inclusivity and support where every team member’s voice matters. Our commitment shines through as we handle over a million support cases each year, empowering our users not just to solve problems but to achieve their goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bridge, a Stripe company, is a rapidly growing business and the number of developers integrating our APIs is growing quickly. We partner with developers to understand their use cases and guide them in integrating with our APIs. We’re a small but mighty team that’s expanding global coverage and is looking to make our first Activation Specialists hires in Mexico City.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll work directly with developers as they integrate with Bridge APIs, guiding them through the onboarding process and helping them go live successfully. You’ll play a key role in resolving early-stage technical challenges, ensuring a smooth activation experience, and accelerating time-to-value for our customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Activation Specialist, you’ll collaborate across Product, Solutions Engineering, and Support teams to unblock customers, improve onboarding workflows, and ensure high-quality handoffs. Beyond day-to-day activation support, you’ll contribute to the growth of our onboarding operation- enhancing areas such as workflow optimization, documentation, tooling, metrics, and reporting. This is a high-impact role with visibility across the business, ideal for someone who enjoys solving technical problems, working with developers, and improving processes at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A few key features include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Specialized experts: Activation specialists provide experience helping customers integrate Bridge technology in various use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project management consists of a kick off call, regular check-ins, Slack Q&amp;amp;A to help unblock your team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product workshops and training for Bridge’s dashboard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively providing technical guidance and support to users during their onboarding journey with Bridge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver pre-built technical workshops and kick off calls to users.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide light touch project management for ongoing Bridge implementations and timely escalate any delays with planned go-live dates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshooting technical issues and providing timely solutions to ensure a smooth onboarding process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with cross-functional teams to address user queries and concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintaining accurate records of user interactions, issues, and resolutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipating and addressing potential technical challenges during the onboarding process. Proactively propose improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Offering guidance on best practices, product features, and account setup to ensure user success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously updating knowledge of Bridge’s products, features, and updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalating complex technical issues to appropriate teams for resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing exceptional customer service to ensure a positive onboarding experience for users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to the improvement of onboarding processes and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for dynamic and curious people that have a passion for solving global user issues, building operations, driving process improvements and want to play a front-line role in building this new operational capability for Bridge and accelerating Bridge’s growth. If you like challenging, scaled problems and are an amazing teammate, we want to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Onboarding Specialist is responsible for providing technical guidance to users during their onboarding journey with Bridge. They proactively address technical queries, troubleshoot issues, and provide solutions to ensure a seamless onboarding process. They work closely with users to understand their needs, offer guidance on best practices, and anticipate and address any potential technical challenges. The Onboarding Specialist collaborates with cross-functional teams, escalates issues as needed, and maintains accurate records of user interactions. Their goal is to provide exceptional customer service and ensure that users have a positive and successful onboarding experience with Bridge.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of implementation consulting in API technologies or other complex technical environments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving and troubleshooting skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical understanding of APIs and experience with SaaS solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable talking about technical concepts, and explaining how Bridge works, both from a product features and API architecture perspective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with an ability to effectively engage and influence various stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating with cross-functional teams in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized and detail-oriented with the ability to manage multiple onboarding flows concurrently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with financial systems, online payments, or e-commerce platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering live technical training to users.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with various code-level debugging &amp;amp; writing of code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

