&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with subscription and usage-based revenue models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of regional market regulations and business practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience in AI, or related technology sectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;History of building commercial or deal processes from the ground up in high-growth environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of scaling deals or commercial operations in rapidly growing organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;APAC Demand Generation is a team of marketers and channel specialists that builds strategies to engage prospects and customers, generate demand for Stripe’s prioritized solutions, and contribute measurable business impact. The team partners closely with global and regional Campaigns, Product Marketing, Field Marketing, Performance Marketing, Lifecycle Marketing, Sales Development, Sales, and Marketing Operations. Its work spans APAC markets, customer segments, and stages of the customer lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe works with startups from their earliest days through global scale. The APAC startup ecosystem is diverse and fast-moving, with founders building for multiple markets, adopting new business models, and making foundational financial-infrastructure decisions earlier than ever.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Demand Generation Manager, Startups, APAC will be the day-to-day demand generation lead for the Startup segment in the region. This person will translate global Startup priorities into an integrated APAC plan, build regionally relevant programs, and independently lead cross-functional execution across channels and markets. The role will connect regional market insight with global strategy and use data to improve how Stripe reaches, engages, and converts startups across their growth journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role reports to the APAC Platforms and Startups Demand Generation lead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop and execute an integrated, multi-channel demand generation plan for startups across APAC, aligned with regional business priorities and global Startup strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Translate global campaigns into relevant regional programs, identifying where messaging, audience strategy, content, channel mix, or execution should be adapted for APAC markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead cross-channel programs spanning paid media, lifecycle and email, content distribution, online and in-person events, field marketing, partner and ecosystem channels, and Sales Development follow-up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the day-to-day performance of the APAC Startup campaign portfolio, using funnel and campaign data to identify opportunities, diagnose gaps, recommend changes, and improve results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with regional Sales and Sales Development teams to align priorities, strengthen lead follow-up, and connect marketing activity to pipeline and activation outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build strong working relationships with global Campaigns, Startup Marketing, Product Marketing, Performance Marketing, Lifecycle Marketing, Field Marketing, Startup Partnerships, and Marketing Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Represent APAC market needs and customer insights in global planning, and share regional results, learnings, and repeatable practices with global and regional partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop programs that engage founders and startup decision-makers at different stages, from company formation and early product adoption through expansion and global growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work with campaign operations and instrumentation partners to establish clear measurement plans, maintain campaign hygiene, and ensure programs can be evaluated accurately.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Independently manage multiple complex, cross-functional workstreams, setting clear goals, timelines, responsibilities, and dependencies while proactively resolving risks and blockers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Design and run experiments that improve audience engagement, conversion, channel effectiveness, and program scalability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate is an experienced demand generation marketer who combines strategic thinking with strong execution. This person is comfortable operating independently, leading through influence, and bringing structure to ambiguous problems. They understand how to build integrated programs across markets and channels and can turn performance data and customer insight into clear action.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;8+ year experience developing and executing B2B demand generation, growth marketing, or integrated marketing programs in the technology industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience owning multi-channel campaigns across multiple APAC markets, with a record of delivering measurable funnel, pipeline, activation, or revenue-related outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong understanding of digital demand channels, including paid media, lifecycle and email marketing, content, online events, and lead management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated ability to independently lead complex cross-functional programs, manage multiple workstreams, and anticipate and resolve execution risks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong analytical skills and experience defining KPIs, interpreting campaign and funnel performance, and translating findings into recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience partnering closely with Sales and Sales Development teams on planning, execution, lead follow-up, and performance improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to align stakeholders across functions, markets, and levels of seniority.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong judgment, curiosity, and a bias toward action in a fast-moving and evolving environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience marketing to startups, founders, developers, or fast-growing technology companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with the APAC startup ecosystem, including accelerators, venture capital firms, technology communities, or other founder channels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience in payments, financial technology, SaaS, financial infrastructure, or an adjacent industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience regionalizing global campaigns and balancing global consistency with meaningful local-market adaptation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Knowledge of account-based marketing, partner marketing, marketing automation, experimentation, and performance optimization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience working in a highly matrixed global organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demo Engineering shows customers how Stripe works instead of just telling them. AI has made demos faster to build, which raises the bar on everything around the build: picking the right story, scoping it to what a customer needs to see, and keeping it current as Stripe ships. We&#39;re looking for technically fluent storytellers who know Stripe&#39;s products deeply and can turn positioning into demos that land in our most visible customer moments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be the bridge between Product Marketing and the demos our field and marketing teams put in front of customers. You&#39;ll take product positioning and messaging and turn it into demo-ready narratives, then use AI-assisted tooling to get them built. You&#39;ll track product launches so our demos stay current, scope Executive Briefing Center (EBC) demos with Solutions Architects and the EBC team, curate and update our demo library, and act as the primary liaison for event content with Product Marketing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate Product Marketing positioning and messaging into demo narratives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design multi-product demo stories that sequence cleanly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct demo builds using AI-assisted tools to prototype quickly and build production-quality work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track Stripe product launches and keep the demo portfolio current and on-message&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curate the Demo Hub so the field can find the right demo for the right customer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary Product Marketing liaison for event demo content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope EBC and strategic customer demos with Solutions Architects and the EBC team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years in a technical, customer-facing, or product role such as solutions engineering, sales engineering, technical product marketing, developer relations, or software engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep technical product fluency: you can explain how APIs and products fit together and judge what can be demoed reliably&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong storytelling and written communication; you can turn a positioning doc into a narrative a customer will remember&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience using AI tools (e.g. Claude Code, Codex) to prototype and build software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment and taste about what matters to a customer audience, from developers to executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable owning projects end to end across Product Marketing, Solutions Architects, Product, Design, and Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a software engineer, or experience building and integrating with Stripe or other RESTful APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with online and in-person payments, subscriptions, card issuing, or other relevant concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scoping or delivering executive briefings, keynotes, or large event demos&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with Product Marketing on launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subject-matter expertise in a relevant industry, vertical, or product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;About the team&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Designers on the Presence team work at the intersection of craft and impact—balancing clarity, polish, and systems thinking with strategic storytelling and experimentation. We collaborate closely with engineering, marketing, content, and product to deliver work that is not only beautiful, but measurably moves the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Designer on the Presence team, you’ll lead complex design projects across stripe.com, helping people understand Stripe’s products, see what’s possible for their businesses, and take the next step. Your work will span new product pages, stories tailored to specific industries and audiences, experiments, and reusable patterns that make exceptional web experiences possible at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll drive projects from early problem framing through launch and iteration, operating independently within your focus area. You’ll turn loosely defined briefs into clear design directions, bring cross-functional partners along, and balance distinctive storytelling with intuitive, effective experiences. This is a hands-on role for a designer who brings a strong point of view, cares deeply about the details, and takes responsibility for how the work performs once it ships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the end-to-end design of complex projects across stripe.com—from defining the problem and exploring concepts to detailed design, implementation, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create clarity from ambiguous briefs by synthesizing user needs, business goals, content, and technical constraints into a coherent design direction and feasible plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex products and capabilities into compelling web experiences that balance storytelling, usability, and clear paths to action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build productive partnerships with engineering, product marketing, content design, brand, and product—aligning on goals, integrating feedback, and communicating decisions and tradeoffs clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineers throughout the process to explore technical possibilities, develop interactions, co-create solutions, and ensure design intent carries through to the shipped experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply and evolve shared components, patterns, and systems, exercising judgment about when to use existing approaches and when a new solution is needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use research, user testing, and performance data to inform decisions, evaluate shipped work, and identify opportunities for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the quality of the team’s work through thoughtful critique, sharing expertise, and leading by example in visual and interaction craft.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in hiring and help new teammates get up to speed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant design experience, ideally in web, product marketing, or brand contexts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong portfolio demonstrating exceptional visual craft, systems thinking, and the ability to make complex information clear and engaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience independently leading complex design projects from problem framing through launch in a cross-functional environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep fluency in layout, typography, color, hierarchy, and interaction, with meticulous attention to how these elements work together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to turn a loose brief into a clear approach, make thoughtful tradeoffs, and maintain momentum as requirements evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and collaboration skills—you can explain your thinking, facilitate alignment, and manage partner expectations proactively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Figma and experience applying and evolving component-based design systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing for CMS-driven websites using modular, scalable patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with AI design tools and workflows for ideation, prototyping, and creative exploration, paired with strong design judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience translating complex technical or financial products into accessible, compelling web experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating closely with front-end engineers, including using prototypes to explore interactions and technical possibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of accessibility, web performance, and SEO best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing for international audiences or multilingual websites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using experimentation and performance insights to improve user journeys and conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of improving shared design patterns, systems, or ways of working—not just delivering individual pages.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Web Presence &amp;amp; Platform (WPP) is organized into two pillars: Platform and Presence. The Platform pillar builds internal systems, tooling, and infrastructure to support the web. The Presence pillar owns Stripe’s public-facing storytelling across stripe.com—including our homepage, product landing pages, industry and solutions pages, and other high-impact go-to-market surfaces. Together, we shape how millions of people understand what Stripe is and what it can do for them.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The recruiting team seeks to build the culture of Stripe by aligning the strongest global talent to our highest impact business needs. They focus on bringing Stripe’s operating principles to life in their recruiting processes, providing the highest-quality candidate experience, and leveraging data driven storytelling to influence the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To further this important mission, we are looking for a driven and collaborative Design Recruiter to grow and scale our global design organization. You can expect high impact and wide-ranging responsibility: owning full-cycle recruiting on niche design searches, contributing to our geo strategy with talent market insights, and delivering best-in-class candidate experience. This person must be a builder who thrives in a learning environment—unafraid to try new things, embrace new ideas, navigate ambiguity, and welcome suggestions for how we can iterate on our processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with senior leaders across the design organization to understand hiring objectives and develop recruiting strategies to identify top talent across various skillsets including product design, brand design, content design, design engineering, web presence design, UX research, and more.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help initiate creative and scalable changes to our existing recruiting processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and analyze metrics and report on hiring progress to design leadership on a regular cadence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focus on creating strategic plans to attract and engage design talent across different geos&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with cross-functional teams like Finance, People Ops, Benefits, Onboarding and Legal to deliver a high-quality and holistic candidate experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience with 4+ years of Design Recruiting experience in a fast-paced, high-growth environment, including in house experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building high performing, high craft design teams and delivering an exceptional candidate experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A growth mindset and truly flexible. You can shift tasks and priorities when circumstances change (at a fast-growing startup, they often do)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An active and data driven approach to problem solving; you enjoy making sense of the trends and using the insights to better your process to make it more efficient&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven abilities to attract passive senior candidates and build a diverse pipelines across different hiring locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong operational rigor with the ability to stay organized amidst change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with an appropriate blend of professionalism and friendliness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Narrative &amp;amp; Editorial team brings together Content Marketing, Brand Marketing, Portfolio Product Marketing, Copywriting, Copy Editing, and Customer Marketing. We create coherent, distinctive stories about the businesses, technologies, and economic forces shaping the internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a senior editorial leader to help bring original stories and insights from Stripe–based on our data, expertise, and customer conversations–to a broader audience via media partnerships and other brand marketing channels. This person will be an exceptional editor, writer, and creative partner with strong instincts about what earns attention: an argument worth making, an unexpected angle, an elegant execution, or a piece of work that people genuinely want to share.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior individual contributor role reporting to the leader of Stripe’s Narrative &amp;amp; Editorial team. The role will spend most of its time shaping major external media partnerships, with the remainder split between helping with original editorial work and advising partner teams on new ideas and their execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the editorial and creative direction for Stripe’s most important external media partnerships, including advertising content, research-led collaborations, and original editorial programs developed with respected publishers and creators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop work that feels native to the audience and editorial environment in which it appears—not generic brand messaging placed beside someone else’s work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn Stripe’s original data analyses, economic insights, customer stories, and more into content pieces that are clear, surprising, useful, and memorable–and that readers and listeners won’t want to skip over.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the full editorial process for partnership work: refining briefs, identifying the strongest ideas, directing creative development, and providing decisive feedback on drafts and final deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct and manage agencies, external creators, and editorial partners as needed, working within existing partnership structures and commercial agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write, edit, and materially improve high-stakes content across formats, including blog posts, newsletter segments, podcast scripts, ad copy, social posts, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate original concepts for creative programs, editorial franchises, and nontraditional formats that broaden how Stripe contributes to conversations about the internet economy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted thought partner to teams across Stripe, helping them clarify ideas, find the strongest expression of their work, and make better creative decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with colleagues in Brand Marketing, Brand Design, Content Marketing, Portfolio PMM, Copywriting, and Customer Marketing to make Stripe’s storytelling more coherent and distinctive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and uphold a clear quality bar for editorial and partnership work, making well-reasoned calls about what is ready to represent Stripe and what still needs improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone with exceptional editorial judgment and a demonstrated ability to make complicated ideas compelling. You may have developed that experience in a newsroom, independent publication, creative studio, agency, research institution, technology company, or another rigorous creative environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 8+ years of relevant experience in editorial, writing, creative development, journalism, publishing, media, brand strategy, or a closely related field. This may include experience writing consistently for a large online followership, even if not professionally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have an exceptional portfolio of published or public-facing work that demonstrates strong writing and editing, original thinking, and an ability to make ideas resonate with an audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are, in the best sense, very online: an active reader of and contributor to the newsletters, social platforms, and niche communities where people debate new ideas about technology, economics, science, business, and culture. You can spot emerging arguments, voices, and formats early—and engage with them authentically, with intellectual honesty and your own point of view.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are an excellent editor. You can diagnose what is missing from a draft or idea, identify the most interesting argument, and give feedback that makes the work materially better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience developing original editorial work, sponsored media, advertising, creative partnerships, or other high-quality audience-facing programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand the difference between work that is merely on-message and work that is genuinely interesting, useful, or worth discussing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can translate complex subjects—including technology, business, economics, science, or policy—into work that is accessible without becoming simplistic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong creative instincts and a sophisticated design sensibility. You understand how language, ideas, visuals, format, and distribution work together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are deeply curious about the technology industry and the broader cultural and economic context in which it operates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable influencing senior stakeholders, external partners, writers, designers, marketers, and agencies without relying on formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can move fluidly between strategy and execution: developing the core idea, shaping the brief, improving the draft, and making the final call on quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have high standards, sound judgment, and enough pragmatism to help teams make excellent work within real constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Education Partnerships team creates meaningful learning and engagement opportunities for students. We collaborate with educational institutions and community partners to design experiences that welcome students and help them explore future possibilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team plans and delivers education initiatives and events of varying sizes, including the Stripe Young Scientist and Technology Exhibition (YSTE), University of Limerick’s Immersive Software Engineering (UL ISE), Patch and Irish Mathematical Trust (IMT).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Education Partnerships Coordinator, you’ll help bring Stripe’s education events and initiatives to life. You’ll work closely with the program lead and internal and external partners to design student experiences, coordinate events, and ensure that participants feel welcomed and supported.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role offers the opportunity to build expertise in education programming and event delivery while gradually taking on more complex projects and responsibilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and project manage meaningful experiences for the student community through events and other engagement activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the programs lead to design the student experience and deliver large-scale events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Welcome students, provide clear guidance, and help ensure that their experiences run smoothly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate event logistics, schedules, materials, communications, and other operational details&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Stripe’s existing education events and partnerships, including YSTE, UL ISE, Patch and IMT events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a thorough understanding of Stripe’s education initiatives and take ownership of increasingly complex responsibilities over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating events, programs, community activities, or comparable projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple workstreams, deadlines, and logistical details in a changing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and thoughtful written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A welcoming and service-oriented approach to working with students, partners, and colleagues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate effectively with internal teams and external organisations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting education, student, early-career, or community programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating large-scale or multi-partner events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in learning about education partnerships and developing broader program-management responsibilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deal Pricing is a dedicated global function that provides deal pricing expertise, financial insights, and deal support for negotiated users to Stripe&#39;s global Go-to-Market teams. We work to ensure deals create economic value for Stripe by establishing the deal commercial framework for a scaling sales organization, actively supporting large or complex deals, and providing pricing insights and feedback to sales, finance, and product leaders. Deal Pricing frequently works with cross-functional business partners across Operations, Finance and Strategy, and Product and there&#39;s constant collaboration with Deal Pricing colleagues across all regions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be instrumental in providing thought leadership to regional sales teams and senior executives and continuing to develop our framework, approach, and associated processes in order to achieve mutually beneficial deals with our sold users while mitigating risk to Stripe. In addition to providing key financial insights and recommendations to business partners and Stripe leadership, you&#39;ll have a chance to stretch beyond the boundaries of finance through business case development and commercial negotiations with all types of customers across the full suite of Stripe&#39;s financial and payment products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a key financial and strategic thought partner to specific EMEA Go-to-Market sales teams and their leadership in both pricing deals at scale and pricing strategic deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage pricing approvals and escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement our pricing and margin guidance and identify levers for commercial uplift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help refine frameworks and processes to evaluate deals and manage pricing activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain up-to-date pricing benchmarks and contribute to team analytical design and production efforts, using this data to enhance our pricing philosophy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in finance or deal pricing at a company, or experience within investment banking or management consulting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to build collaborative working relationships with business partners through a combination of influencing and awareness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to deal effectively with ambiguity and thrive in an unstructured, fast-moving environment by driving business results without significant supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent financial modeling, verbal, and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using LLMs and AI agents to conduct research, analyses, and automate work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the payments or technology sector&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CPQ solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting findings and recommendations to senior leadership, preferably to sales or go-to-market business partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;EMEA Demand Generation is a team of marketers and channel specialists that drive strategies to engage prospects and customers and generate demand for our prioritised solutions. We partner closely with global and regional Campaigns, Product Marketing, Field Marketing, Sales Development, and Sales teams to bring full-funnel product and audience campaigns to life, optimise performance, and drive business impact. Our team works across all customer segments and product lifecycle journeys, and at each stage of the customer lifecycle journey.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Platforms is one of the largest and fastest growing segments in Stripe. This role sits at the intersection of global and regional field teams and has a significant impact across our GTM organisation. From striving to better understand our customers to assessing the health of our business, you will help define and lead Stripe&#39;s Platform and Marketplaces strategy. Additionally, you will realise this strategy by driving marketing activations, building creative new programs, and working with sales and product to ensure full-funnel alignment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires a highly collaborative individual who thinks both strategically and tactically to get things done, is comfortable navigating complexity and can work with both sales and marketing stakeholders. It is a business critical role and a great opportunity to build and have an impact across our GTM organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a multi-channel, regional demand generation strategy and plan to acquire SaaS Platforms and Marketplaces across EMEA in collaboration with global marketers and regional experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with global and regional performance media experts to acquire and re-engage customers through a broad mix of paid media tactics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Land global campaigns in region in conjunction with audience PMMs and global campaign leads to acquire and nurture leads at scale through digital content, paid placement, digital events, targeted nurture programs, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop account-based marketing strategies for named account lists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a cross-GTM coalition including Global Marketing, Regional Sales, Sales Development, and Sales Operations to jointly grow pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own key business and revenue metrics for Platforms and Marketplaces across the full funnel while investigating business health issues such as conversion and lead quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally to define regional requirements as Stripe refines our marketing capabilities, MarTech stack, and lead management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify innovative ways to reach and engage our users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a thought leader representing EMEA as we grow across our campaigns and broader go-to-market at Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continually optimise for efficiency, scale for growth, and prioritize for focus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Who you are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years years of relevant experience running marketing campaigns for enterprise sized companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of paid media tactics, digital marketing strategies, marketing automation, email marketing tactics, account based marketing, and lead management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with Sales teams, including joint planning and execution, driving disciplined lead follow-up, and earning trust as a strategic business partner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of defining and executing end-to-end, multi-channel programmes with a wide range of cross-functional stakeholders that deliver against funnel metrics and KPIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills; able to convey complex topics with simplicity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superb organization and project management skills and the capacity to manage multiple complex projects at once.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical skills and the ability to craft actionable insights from complex data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to work cross functionally in a highly matrixed organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A startup mentality with a bias to action and the ability to flex in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B2B marketing experience owning a regional demand generation strategy across multiple countries, customer segments, and products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the payments, financial technology, or adjacent industries, or marketing FinTech solutions or to FinTech companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a highly dynamic, high-growth tech company or consulting firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Alliances and Channels team focuses on building, supporting, and going to market with professional services firms including systems integrators, consultancies, and managed services providers such as Accenture, PwC, Deloitte, Infosys, and others. In addition, the team leads the go-to-market initiatives with our strategic technology alliance partners including AWS, Salesforce, Adobe, and others. Our objective is to ensure users have access to the broadest set of solutions leveraging the Stripe platform and the deepest set of technology and industry experts, while at the same time ensuring our partners and Stripe build large, mutually beneficial businesses together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Strategic Global Alliances team focuses on a subset of our highest priority partnerships. These partnerships operate at global scale with Stripe and present opportunities to create significant sales pipeline, deals sold, joint solutions, and scaled delivery expertise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll support the overall success of Stripe&#39;s Global Alliance with Accenture and other key GSIs in EMEA, driving joint GTM and co-sell. You&#39;ll work alongside the Accenture Global Partner Development Manager and other GSI PDMs to drive net new demand for the partnership in the field across key markets in EMEA. This position is focused on deepening our joint sales motion, joint solutions, and delivery capabilities. This position is fast-paced, highly visible, and aligned to quarterly metrics. As a Partner Development Manager, you&#39;ll hold a holistic view of the business, generated by and engaged with Accenture and other partners in EMEA, and work across the Stripe Sales segments to enhance and grow partner-related Stripe revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work cross-functionally with Partner Sales Managers, Partner Development Leadership, and Stripe AEs. You&#39;ll demonstrate an understanding of the Stripe Partner Ecosystem and the Stripe sales organization, and recognize high-impact opportunities, solutions, support deals for successful engagement with partners, and maintain high business hygiene.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll drive towards end-customer value that results in business growth to both Accenture (and other GSIs) and Stripe by being partner-centric in all activities, serving as a leader and advocate for them within Stripe, and accurately representing Stripe within the partner&#39;s organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Global Accenture PDM and other GSI PDMs on building strategy, joint solution development, partner enablement, pipeline development, and deal closure in the EMEA region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Accenture and other GSI counterparts to enable Stripe and partner sales teams on the unique joint value prop, lead account mapping workshops, blitz days, and co-create opportunities together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestrate and partner with cross-functional resources to support Stripe partner co-sell and GTM activities and create and maintain a long-term, scalable joint GTM model that drives partner and user success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support key deal execution with partners, both pre-sales and post-sales (working with Stripe PSMs, PSEs, SAs, and AEs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support weekly pipeline reviews to ensure pipeline information is thorough and accurate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broker internal resources, tools, references, and investments needed to achieve quarterly goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of technology GTM experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategy, sales, and development experience, working alongside consulting partners or ISVs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process-oriented mindset with desire to solve individual challenges while building for scale in mind&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and presentation skills, with the ability to speak to different functional leadership both internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to both lead and be a team player on cross-functional teams that include technical, sales, product, and support resources from Stripe and the partner. Creative in terms of leveraging resources to drive outsized impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel and be present with partners and sellers in front of our users and prospects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build and execute territory and opportunity-specific plans, in partnership with the Global PDM and other cross-functional resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent ongoing operational hygiene, accurately representing sales and partner activities in Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accenture direct or indirect GTM experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving GTM with GSIs such as PwC, Cognizant, Infosys, and Deloitte&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to payments, commerce, and Q2C landscape, and understanding of how the Stripe stack can differentiate and complement ISV solutions in different integration models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building successful joint GTM solutions with partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s legal team works on complex technical and legal issues to help protect our growing business. In this role, you’ll join the legal team supporting Stripe’s People team and other business partners across Europe, the Middle East, and Africa (EMEA).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Employment Counsel, you’ll advise our People team and other business partners on employment law across EMEA and proactively manage employment-related risks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our People team to provide subject-matter expertise on employment issues, including recruiting, hiring, performance management, compensation and benefits, leaves of absence, people data privacy, internal investigations, working time, and HR best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively review employment policies to support legal compliance and consistency with best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams to support and maintain employment compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft and negotiate employment-related agreements, including offer letters, contractor agreements, and vendor agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle pre-litigation and litigation matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor developments in employment, AI, and data protection law and advise on developments that may affect Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of specialist, post-qualification employment law experience at a law firm or in-house legal department&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualification to practice law in Ireland or England and Wales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to analyse employment law matters of varying complexity, exercise sound judgment, and make well-reasoned decisions amid ambiguity and incomplete information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to work effectively with multiple stakeholders while maintaining discretion, confidentiality, and professionalism&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organisational and project-management skills, with the ability to manage multiple long- and short-term workstreams, collaborate across teams, and support international employment law matters outside EMEA when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house experience or experience advising technology clients as external counsel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising on employee representative bodies, works councils, and European works councils&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising on jurisdictions outside Ireland and the United Kingdom&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Revenue &amp;amp; Financial Management group is building new products that expand the scope of problems we tackle beyond payments into Revenue Management, Financial Operations and analytics. Right now this includes products like Billing, Invoicing, Revenue Recognition, Reconciliation and the underlying platform for batch and real time processing of large scale financial data to power these solutions. These solutions are going to be key pillars for Stripe’s growing SaaS business and a major revenue stream.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced engineering manager to lead the team building the foundation for accounting system and user-facing product features that will streamline and automate accrual accounting for Stripe customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead your team of talented engineers to solve data engineering challenges at scale and deliver a high level of technical and operational excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product managers and talk to directly to customers to drive a high-impact, prioritized roadmap for your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, coach, mentor, develop, and grow engineers on your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be deeply involved in launching new product features and capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineers and product managers across Stripe to ensure your features are integrated into the Stripe suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to engineering initiatives across the Revenue and Finance Automation (RFA) organization and across Stripe as a member of Stripe’s engineering management team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of engineering management experience and 10+ years of overall experience in the industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully led high-complexity teams, working in parallel on multiple high-impact areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works very well cross-functionally, and is able to think rigorously and make hard decisions and tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives on a high level of autonomy and responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encourages a healthy work environment that’s both supportive and challenging and enables engineers to do their best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical background and hands-on experience in solving large scale and difficult technical problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Values and enjoys working with a diverse group of people with different expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with large scale distributed systems or big data processing systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in high-growth teams similar to Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building financial systems or tools for financial experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with accounting procedures or systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Adaptive Pricing, one of Stripe&#39;s fastest-growing products, makes global selling easier for merchants by enabling them to localize prices in over 150 countries without currency complexities or foreign exchange risk. Our team combines deep technical expertise with a relentless focus on user experience to simplify cross-border commerce for merchants and their customers. We work in a fast-paced, high-impact environment, building scalable pricing infrastructure and innovative features in close collaboration with teams across Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager on the Adaptive Pricing team, you will lead a group of talented engineers building the next generation of global payment experiences. You’ll work alongside technical leaders to set clear priorities, ensure engineering excellence, and cultivate a strong team culture. Your role involves coaching and developing engineers, fostering a culture of collaboration and accountability, and partnering closely with product, design, and leadership. This is a unique opportunity to lead a critical product area with significant business impact while mentoring engineers and shaping Stripe’s global payments future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide your team in building robust, high-performance pricing and currency conversion products that drive Stripe’s global expansion strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive the roadmap and priorities for your team as the editor-in-chief of your team’s plans, collaborating with stakeholders across product, design, infrastructure, and marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish close feedback loops with customers and collaborate closely with partner teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a high level of technical excellence on the team, upholding high engineering standards and implementing best practices throughout your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting your team members&#39; career growth by providing insights and development opportunities tailored to their goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to engineering-wide initiatives as a member of Stripe’s engineering management team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of engineering management experience, directly managing and growing teams of 5+ engineers focused on building and shipping products at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of full time software development experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building extensible, leveraged software solutions, with the ability to empathize with users and advocate for exceptional user experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical acumen to engage thoughtfully with engineers around architecture and implementation decisions, serving as a force multiplier for the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A mindset of autonomy and entrepreneurship, where you&#39;re excited to take responsibility and drive initiatives forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience thriving in cross-functional environments, demonstrating rigorous thinking, effective decision-making, and ability to build strong cross-team relationships&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in financial product companies and interest in financial products and markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills for different audiences (leadership, users, company-wide)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong product and design sense, and enjoy finding elegant solutions to complex problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Agentic payments is a team that’s building new APIs and integration experiences for agentic commerce online. We think that the proliferation of consumer-facing AI experiences will unlock new ways that consumers buy things online, and our existing payments experiences need to evolve to new commercial models that cutting-edge builders are starting. Our first launch, Instant Checkout in collaboration with OpenAI, took the industry by storm and we’re bringing experiences like that to the entire universe of AI agents and sellers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager on Agentic Commerce, you’ll own the shaping and delivery of transformative products that redefine how commerce works, making it more fluid, automated, and aligned with user intent. You’ll collaborate closely with product management, design, data science, and marketing to unlock new opportunities for our customers and partners globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our north star provides a new integration model for AI agents who are looking to build agent-powered online commerce experiences, via their Stripe integration. They will have access to our entire suite of connected sellers, and can focus on the end-user experience. Enabling an AI agent to do this requires new API primitives, new dashboard surfaces, and deep thought about what financial and e-commerce complexity Stripe can simplify on their behalf.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build full stack solutions across Stripe&#39;s ecosystem, including back end services, dashboard interfaces, money movement systems, and integrations with other Stripe primitives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner deeply with product management and design to ship high impact features that increase user autonomy and reduce friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply strong analytical skills to dive into data, test hypotheses, and make informed trade-offs. Set success metrics for the team to ensure solutions are enterprise-grade and quickly meet Stripe’s reliability SLOs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally across Stripe’s broader platform and product teams to integrate agentic commerce capabilities seamlessly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly with users (particularly large enterprises) to understand their business needs and translate requirements into novel product shapes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of engineering experience with a computer science background with hands on development expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native and very comfortable autonomously solving problems with agentic AI tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience coaching and developing senior and staff level individual contributors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience of leading initiatives that touch large engineering organizations, spanning multiple teams to influence tech roadmap planning and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, structuring ambiguous concepts clearly and from first principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in a collaborative environment involving different functions, stakeholders, and subject matter experts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep empathy for users balancing autonomy and guidance in digital commerce experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of engineering management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building APIs or new integration experiences for users, several of them being enterprise grade&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve been on the founding team of a business / startup, taking a product from 0-1&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in eCommerce and/or payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Manager, AI Conversation Platform&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The newly formed Conversation Platform team aims to build a conversation platform for all merchants who use Stripe. We are doing so by (a) automating the easy tasks, and (b) assisting our users in the difficult tasks. Some examples include customizing the Stripe landing page to suggest bespoke integrations, allowing users to command the Stripe API in natural language, and resolving user issues automatically. We are developing RAG based systems on the latest LLMs as well as fine-tuning our own models. We’re an end-to-end team going from ideas to models to shipping in production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving an ambitious vision for AI/ML that benefits our users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Setting the technical &amp;amp; process direction for the team based on business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brainstorm and coordinate product integrations with partner teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proposing new ideas and building prototypes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be an integral part of a larger ML community internally &amp;amp; externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire &amp;amp; develop a world-class team to deliver high-quality ML systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach engineers to help them grow in their careers and maintain a high bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for ML Engineering Managers who are passionate about using ML to improve products and delight customers. You have experience leading teams that develop streaming feature pipelines, build ML models, and deploy them to production, even if it involves making substantial changes to backend code. You are comfortable with ambiguity, love to take initiative, and have a bias towards action.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have at least 4 years of experience managing ML teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working as a Machine Learning Engineer, Applied Scientist or equivalent Individual Contributor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead by example in high-growth, high-impact, ambiguous environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience building &amp;amp; shipping ML systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold yourself and others to a high bar when working with production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in a collaborative cross-functional environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in shipping LLM &amp;amp; RAG systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Checkout Optimization team is the growth team for Stripe’s checkout UIs. They build high-converting, personalized checkout experiences for buyers and agents, as well as the data platform that powers it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team identifies opportunities to improve checkout through rapid product experimentation and delivers optimization at scale through our ML-powered engine. The team also builds the reliable data foundations that enable this work, including experimentation, optimization, and data-informed product decisions across Stripe’s checkout suite.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over the next 6 to 12 months, the team will focus on:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building personalized checkout experiences powered by the ML-based Optimization Engine&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agentic commerce through optimizing OCS experiences for agent buyers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Checkout optimization for rapidly growing AI companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving our data platform, which is critical to leveraging data internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineering Managers at Stripe are responsible for the success of their team. You’ll be deeply involved in the engineering and design processes as well as coaching, mentoring, and leading the team. You’ll have a deep understanding of how to drive efficient engineering teams and you’ll have a strong user focus. You&#39;ll work with engineers on creating technical solutions and communicating effectively across teams and senior leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage a team of talented full-stack product and data engineers, providing mentorship, guidance, and support to ensure their success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand buyer and agent needs and pain points to prioritize workstreams and deliver high-quality checkout experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Design, Data Science, Data Engineering, and engineering teams across Stripe to deliver these solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead experimentation and optimization work that improves checkout conversion and buyer experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and evolve the data platform that enables reliable, self-serve analysis, experimentation, and product decisions across OCS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive high standards for the quality, reliability, and usability of the data products and pipelines that support OCS decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit top engineering talent in partnership with Stripe’s recruiting team to build a diverse and high-performing team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the execution of projects, overseeing the entire development lifecycle from planning to delivery, while maintaining high standards of quality and timely completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on technical leadership, including architecture and design, vision, direction, requirements setting, and incident response processes for your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the team’s direction, from north star vision to goals, OKRs, and roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of engineering management experience, directly managing and growing teams of 5+ engineers focused on building and shipping products at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of full-time software development experience, with a strong background in backend development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across geographies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading growth or product teams that have used experimentation to drive product usage and other metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building extensible, leveraged software solutions that scale to different kinds of user needs, with the ability to empathize with users and advocate for excellent user experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience working in payments and on payments technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience leading a growth team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience leading a data engineering team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The StripeOS engineering team builds the tools Stripe uses to plan and run its work: setting goals, making and recording decisions, and tracking projects from kickoff to launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These tools sit at the center of how Stripe operates. Every team relies on them to stay aligned, make sound decisions, and move quickly, so every improvement we make compounds across the company. Recent advances in AI give us an opportunity to rethink what these tools can do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re an AI-native team reimagining how Stripe plans, decides, and executes. We build polished web and mobile experiences alongside AI agents and assistants that do real work on behalf of Stripe employees. We experiment quickly, put ideas in front of real users, and scale the ones that work. As we do, our scope keeps growing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our users are Stripe employees in every function and at every level, from engineers and product managers to company leadership. We partner closely with the teams that build Stripe’s internal AI platform and developer tooling, and with groups across the company, from engineering to marketing to senior leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a product-minded engineering leader who’s excited to transform how a company plans and executes its work. You’ll lead the StripeOS engineering team as it builds the next generation of Stripe’s planning and execution tools. You’ll set the team’s direction, grow and support its engineers, and stay close to the technical work: shaping architecture, prototyping new ideas alongside your team, putting them in the hands of real users, and turning the strongest experiments into products used across Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This leadership role combines technical depth with broad product scope. You’ll work hand in hand with product managers and designers to define what we build, turning ambitious ideas into the right technical solutions. You’ll combine full-stack engineering with emerging AI capabilities and guide your team through open-ended problems where the right product, interface, and architecture emerge together. The potential impact of this role is enormous, and it will keep growing across the entire company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the team’s vision for AI-native workflows: rethink how Stripe employees plan, decide, and execute with AI at the core, and build agents and assistants that synthesize context, automate repetitive work, and help people make better decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product managers and designers to set the team’s direction and roadmap, turn ambitious ideas into well-scoped technical plans, and guide the delivery of full-stack products, including web and mobile experiences, AI-powered features, and integrations with internal tools and platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay deeply engaged in the technical work: review designs, weigh in on architecture, and prototype new approaches with your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, grow, and support your engineers through coaching, mentoring, and clear feedback, and partner with Stripe’s recruiting team to recruit top engineering talent and build a diverse, high-performing team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape how the team operates, from engineering practices and standards for experimentation to AI-native development that helps the team prototype faster and ship with confidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly with users across Stripe to understand how they work, turn what you learn into products they love, and measure the impact of what the team ships to double down on what makes Stripe employees more productive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set a high bar for quality, reliability, security, and privacy, especially when building on sensitive internal context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of engineering management experience, leading and growing teams that build and ship products at scale, with a track record of taking critical user-facing products from prototype to production and keeping them reliable as they scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of software development experience, with a strong background in full-stack development, technical depth in modern web technologies, performance, and user experience, and the ability to guide engineers on architecture and the design of extensible systems that serve many kinds of users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with modern AI tools and a clear point of view on how AI agents and AI-native workflows can transform the way people work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort leading through ambiguity: framing the right problems, experimenting and iterating, making pragmatic technical decisions, and charting a clear path forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent cross-functional collaboration skills, with experience partnering closely with product managers and designers to define and build products, and a product-minded approach to building delightful experiences that solve real problems and deliver meaningful outcomes for users and the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for enabling people to do their best work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping AI agents or products powered by large language models to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building productivity, collaboration, or internal tools used across a large organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking new products from initial concept through launch and iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in and with geographically distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with modern web and backend technologies, such as Go, Ruby, TypeScript, and React&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to drive work forward autonomously while bringing your team and partners along toward shared goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rigorous thinking and comfort making hard decisions and tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a platform company powering businesses all over the world, Stripe processes payments, runs marketplaces, and detects fraud, helping entrepreneurs start an internet business from anywhere in the world. Commerce Systems provides a central entry point for Stripe teams to monetize products in global markets. We build platforms and services to define and manage pricing, calculate and collect Stripe’s revenue, and empower Stripe and our users to understand and manage revenue and costs. We work on customer-facing experiences, internal platforms, and data pipelines to empower Accounting, Finance, Strategy, Sales, and Stripe’s Products to drive business value across the entire user and product lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a seasoned technical leader to lead a team within the Commerce Systems organization. As the leader in Commerce Systems, your goals will include increasing the self-serve capabilities of the billing platform to accelerate product development across Stripe’s product suite; launching new pricing and monetization capabilities for our product and sales teams; ensuring the rigor, accuracy, and predictability of billing outcomes; and enabling our partners in finance, strategy, and accounting to deeply understand Stripe’s business performance. You’ll work with leaders across product, engineering, sales, and many of our back office functions - finance and strategy, accounting, tax, and compliance - to influence strategy across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Commerce Systems is a core engine powering many of Stripe’s biggest bets, from shipping new products faster to redefining our commercial strategy. The right engineering leadership will enable Stripe to scale more quickly and more reliably as our business accelerates. If that sounds exciting, we’d love to speak with you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the core mission and responsibilities of your team. Set strategies and priorities to balance improvements across multiple dimensions including monetizing new products, enabling greater self-service and improved developer experience, and improving technical foundations and operational excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead engineering and design processes, coaching, mentoring, and supporting your team as they build innovative solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop strong relationships with other leaders and orgs to ensure efficient collaboration and close alignment on objectives and outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a healthy team with a strong bench of leaders by supporting team members’ growth and hiring both internally and externally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ total years of engineering experience with a minimal 4 years of management experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully led high-complexity teams of 8+ engineers, working in parallel on multiple high-impact areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience thriving in cross-functional environments, demonstrating rigorous thinking and effective decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully recruited, mentored, and built high-performing teams, creating an inclusive environment that attracts diverse talent and empowers individuals to thrive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate with a high level of autonomy and responsibility, taking ownership of projects and driving initiatives that contribute to the overall success of the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work effectively with partners in a geographically distributed org, promoting clear communication and collaboration across time zones to ensure alignment and shared goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, enabling clear and persuasive interactions with colleagues and stakeholders, ensuring understanding of technical concepts and fostering collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or improving platforms that empower other developers, optimizing for self-service and extensibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain knowledge in payments, billing, or other financial technology is beneficial but not essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Infrastructure is responsible for the reliability, scale, performance, and cost of Stripe’s systems and the productivity and sentiment of Stripe’s people. You may work on a wide variety of critical business areas within Core Infrastructure. We’re the home for Stripe&#39;s critical tier0 infrastructure systems (Compute, Networking, DocumentDB, Distributed Caching and High assurance engineering). We build the foundational platform for Stripe products and services to allow them to operate at scale. We drive reliability, availability, efficiency and scalability of these systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager in Core Infrastructure at Stripe, you will lead a team solving challenging distributed systems problems and drive critical improvements in our foundational platform.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with senior leadership to define and execute strategic initiatives for Stripe&#39;s core infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading and mentoring a team of experienced engineers, fostering their growth and career development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving technical decisions and architectural improvements for large-scale, distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering with product and engineering teams across Stripe to identify and implement infrastructure solutions that enhance scalability, reliability, and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cultivating a culture of engineering excellence, innovation, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting the engineering team in achieving a high level of technical quality, reliability, and ease-of-use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruiting great engineers, in collaboration with Stripe&#39;s recruiting team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of industry experience in software engineering, with at least 3-4 years in engineering management roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in designing, building, and operating large-scale distributed systems and infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience with cloud technologies, preferably AWS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in multiple areas of infrastructure, such as compute, networking, databases, caching systems, or storage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of leading and growing high-performing engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in managing geographically distributed teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to influence and collaborate across all levels of the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with a data-driven approach to decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to drive technical strategy and roadmap planning for complex infrastructure systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with globally distributed systems and multi-region architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with containerization and orchestration technologies (e.g., Kubernetes).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of performance optimization and capacity planning for large-scale systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in scaling infrastructure platforms to handle millions of requests per second (RPS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of successful cross-functional project leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with programming languages commonly used in infrastructure, such as Go, Ruby, or Java.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Developer Productivity group is responsible for making Stripe’s developers happy and productive. We work on tools, processes, and code refactoring to accelerate Stripe engineering as Stripe scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for people with an interest in building the tools to improve the day to day experience of Engineers in Stripe. The ideal candidate will have a mix of technical expertise in either language processing tools, version control systems, contract testing, build systems, but most importantly a passion for solving developer experience problems, and a pragmatic ability to ship results iteratively. You’ll be working on a mix of fault tolerant distributed systems and also software which runs on individual developer machines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work with a code base of several million lines of code (and counting), used by hundreds of engineers across the globe, who initiate dozens of build jobs per minute. What we do is key to allowing Stripe engineers working in our main business logic layer to have the most productive time of their careers while building and running the features that Stripe and its customers need in order to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Efficiently scaling a fleet of 10,000s of CI workers, balancing the competing priorities of minimising user-facing queuing while also minimising cost and increasing reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to engineering-wide initiatives as a member of Stripe’s engineering management team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the end-to-end experience of how our users engage with CI. This includes working with our users to understand pain points, and deliver incremental, or step-change improvements to their day-to-day workflows across multiple languages, with a higher focus on Java and Ruby.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing &amp;amp; maintaining state-of-the-art developer tooling and increasing tooling reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with other Stripe leaders to design and lead developer productivity best practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower the engineering team to achieve a high level of technical productivity, reliability, and simplicity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit great engineers, in collaboration with Stripe’s recruiting team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help engineers advance in their careers and develop new skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with your users to ensure the capabilities they need to safely, and reliably, deploy to production are available.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting efficient inter-service testing to support teams developing new services, or migrating existing services, to Stripe’s modern service oriented architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of people management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building tools that are used daily by other developers (e.g. CI, build support, devboxes)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for supporting developer productivity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully recruited and built great teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to thrive on a high level of autonomy and responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and persuasive writing and in-person communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have managed teams that designed and operated critical infrastructure, particularly with a broad remit across core capabilities, builds, and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are empathetic to customer needs but visionary enough to not just deliver a faster horse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable planning in quarters, and can set a vision for several years&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are excited about collaborating with teammates across Stripe’s organization, to provide a wonderful user experience for key developer workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable working with geographically distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Privy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to make privacy and user ownership the default online. To do so, we build simple, flexible APIs and tools for developers that make it easy to build new products on crypto rails.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Privy owns the abstractions and infrastructure layer above wallets, integrating across chains, third-party providers, and Stripe products like Treasury and Link. We get to solve hard technical problems while leveraging Stripe&#39;s distribution to reach customers like Ramp, Klarna, Deel, Kraken, Hyperliquid, and Fomo — powering experiences for both mainstream users and crypto natives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineering at Privy is distinguished by:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High urgency—Shipping very small iterations, very fast, to learn very quickly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product taste—Our customers &lt;em&gt;are&lt;/em&gt; developers, and to build effective products for them requires technical knowledge —you will often be &quot;the PM&quot;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security mindset—A great portion of our product is trust. While we have a dedicated security team, every engineer brings security to their designs from the start.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In practice, we use &lt;a href=&quot;https://mcfunley.com/choose-boring-technology&quot;&gt;boring technology&lt;/a&gt; like Node, React, and AWS so we can focus our engineering energy entirely on pushing the boundaries of Privy&#39;s core product, e.g. through hardware enclaves, multi-region low-latency APIs, and blockchain abstractions that are accessible to mainstream developers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Privy, our Forward Deployed Engineers work on the company’s most important customer problems. They partner closely with customers to architect our most complex integrations and build new product features that close the gap to win deals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an Engineering Manager to lead this team as it continues to grow. You’ll be responsible for helping an outstanding group of Forward Deployed Engineers do the best work of their careers while staying laser-focused on helping Privy and its customers win.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-leverage role at the intersection of customers, product development, and engineering. You’ll help the team stay focused on the highest-value work, raise the bar on execution, and help turn customer signal into new products and features.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the manager of this team, you own its overall impact. Great management is a core part of how Privy wins: our managers are force multipliers, performance coaches, and culture carriers who help exceptional people do exceptional work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own team outcomes and business impact for Forward Deployed Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and develop engineers across technical depth, customer empathy, and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold the team accountable to excellence in quality, throughput, and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the team is focused on the right problems and highest-leverage opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product, Solutions Engineering, and GTM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay close to the work—review PRs, help scope technical work, review design docs, and jump in on complex problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a strong team culture grounded in trust, rigor, and urgency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen the feedback loop between customer signal and product roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership and a track record of driving outstanding business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent people management skills and experience growing high-performing engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical judgment and the ability to evaluate architecture and tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A customer-first mindset and comfort translating ambiguous needs into clear technical direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High emotional maturity and strong communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing in a fast-moving, high-expectation environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Privy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to make privacy and user ownership the default online. To do so, we build simple, flexible APIs and tools for developers that make it easy to build new products on crypto rails.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Privy owns the abstractions and infrastructure layer above wallets, integrating across chains, third-party providers, and Stripe products like Treasury and Link. We get to solve hard technical problems while leveraging Stripe&#39;s distribution to reach customers like Ramp, Klarna, Deel, Kraken, Hyperliquid, and Fomo — powering experiences for both mainstream users and crypto natives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineering at Privy is distinguished by:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High urgency—Shipping very small iterations, very fast, to learn very quickly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product taste—Our customers &lt;em&gt;are&lt;/em&gt; developers, and to build effective products for them requires technical knowledge —you will often be &quot;the PM&quot;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security mindset—A great portion of our product is trust. While we have a dedicated security team, every engineer brings security to their designs from the start.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In practice, we use &lt;a href=&quot;https://mcfunley.com/choose-boring-technology&quot;&gt;boring technology&lt;/a&gt; like Node, React, and AWS so we can focus our engineering energy entirely on pushing the boundaries of Privy&#39;s core product, e.g. through hardware enclaves, multi-region low-latency APIs, and blockchain abstractions that are accessible to mainstream developers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager at Privy, you will lead, grow, and shape high-performing engineering teams that make a massive impact on our product and industry. Your North Star is to enable and drive towards the success of Privy’s business overall.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Engineering Manager of your team, the buck stops with you: you are the owner of your team’s ultimate impact on Privy’s product and business. We believe that excellence in management is why our team loves working at Privy. Incredible managers are the core driver behind Privy’s long-term success: they are force multipliers, performance coaches, culture-carriers. They build the scaffolding that supports the team and each individual’s greatest impact. They shape Privy to be the place where each person gets to do the very best work of their careers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We wake up every day driven to show up for our team. We shape roles around the unique strengths of every person and we are deeply grateful for the time we spend together building something greater than ourselves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Infrastructure at Privy is fundamentally a product. With both internal engineers (and increasingly non-engineers) as direct consumers of infra platforms, as well as external product offerings, it is essential that the infra team creates powerful abstractions, educates and grows the Privy team on shipping ever-better software, and operates deeply efficient tooling to be the lever arm for which Privy moves the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own long-term team outcomes and success of Privy’s product and business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the future vision of infrastructure of Privy alongside talented infrastructure engineers, across complex, cutting edge technology like secure enclaves (TEEs) and one-click Bring Your Own Cloud deployments, with performance and high scale as a default.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold the team accountable to excellence in quality, throughput, and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading active infrastructure work across the breadth of the company, from service definition, to reliability engineering, to developer tooling, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the team is working on the right scope of work and projects, align decisions with business impact, and build interfaces with other parts of the org&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fill gaps as a player-coach; review PRs, write and review design docs, investigate incidents – stay close to the metal and reinforce our builder culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach engineers towards growth and their career goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a supportive, fun, motivating, celebratory team culture so that the team wins every week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep ownership and a high-level perspective on driving overall business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance-oriented mindset, with a high bar for quality and excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical excellence to be able to independently evaluate quality and technical feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High emotional maturity, insightfulness, and care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong past experience as a manager and leader – excellent management takes reps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with any of the following a plus:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and operating systems supporting hundreds of millions of users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secure enclave platforms, like AWS Nitro Enclaves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Observability, incident response, capacity planning, performance tuning, and infrastructure automation (IaC, CI/CD for infra)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in building low-latency, high-throughput systems for trading or payment processing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Any blend of public cloud/BYOC architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Internal Systems Automations Platform team’s mission is to unlock productivity across all of Stripe’s internal systems. We build solutions to transform core processes for Finance, Accounting, People, Legal, Sales, Marketing, and more. We orchestrate the full automation lifecycle, using artificial intelligence (AI) for planning, analysis, and reasoning, and deterministic scripts, code, and pipelines for reliable and trustworthy execution. We enable technical and nontechnical users to build hybrid code and no-code automations while working with central Operations, Developer Productivity, Infrastructure, and machine learning (ML) teams on behalf of all Internal Systems customers to build powerful platforms together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced engineering manager with a passion for simplifying complex systems and driving operational efficiency. In this role, you’ll analyze existing processes across Stripe’s internal systems, use automation platforms where possible, and design new solutions when needed. You will implement cutting-edge automation solutions, including AI agents, robotic process automation (RPA), and data pipelines, and build best-in-class platforms. You’ll be responsible for continuously improving workflows to maximize efficiency and deliver meaningful business impact across a broad set of internal stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead your team of talented engineers to design and deploy data pipelines and intelligent workflows that simplify operations for internal customers, including Finance, Accounting, Legal, People, Sales, Marketing, and Operations teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product managers and talk directly with users to drive a high-impact, prioritized roadmap for your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, coach, mentor, develop, and grow engineers on your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be deeply involved in launching new product features and capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineers and product managers across Stripe to ensure your features are integrated into the Stripe suite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of engineering management experience and 10+ years of overall experience in the industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience working on high-scale systems with a strong technical foundation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works very well cross-functionally and is able to think rigorously and make hard decisions and tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives on a high level of autonomy and responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encourages a healthy work environment that’s both supportive and challenging and enables engineers to do their best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical background and hands-on experience in solving large-scale and difficult technical problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with diverse internal teams and stakeholders across Finance, Legal, Operations, and other business functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI, large language model (LLM), or ML technologies is highly valuable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of context-driven AI agents that can autonomously figure out solutions when given business problems and context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About The Team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The payments landscape is changing rapidly and our team is at the forefront of this change. Depending on where you live, you may be used to paying with a credit card (United States), iDeal (Netherlands) or UPI (India), amongst hundreds of other global payment methods. It turns out how you pay is increasingly dependent on where you are and what business you&#39;re buying from. The Local Payment Methods team is responsible for Stripe&#39;s fastest growing payments business. We build payment methods that help businesses drastically increase their revenues and grow their business. Undergirding all of this we also build the platform that allows us to build and distribute payment methods at scale&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineering Managers at Stripe are responsible for the success of their team. You’ll be deeply involved in the engineering and design processes as well as coaching, mentoring, and leading the team. You’ll have a deep understanding of how to drive efficient engineering teams and you’ll have a strong user-focus. You’ll be working with engineers on creating technical solutions and communicating effectively across teams and senior leadership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage a team of talented engineers on the team, providing mentorship, guidance, and support to ensure their success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand user needs and pain points to prioritize engineering work and deliver high quality solutions that meet user needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the execution of projects, overseeing the entire development lifecycle from planning to delivery, while maintaining high standards of quality and timely completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on technical leadership (architecture/design, vision/direction/requirements setting, and incident response processes) for your reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the team’s direction, from north star vision, to goals/OKRs, and roadmap. Align with the broader MaaS organization, and our customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive execution on the roadmap, making sure we deliver big bets, but stay noble to an ever-changing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a collaborative and inclusive work environment, promoting innovation, knowledge sharing, and continuous improvement within the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our recruiting team to attract and hire top talent, and define the overall hiring strategies for your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Who you are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of management experience with a total of 12+ years of software engineering experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has built products before, and wants to be involved in product development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a team with multiple workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical enough to drive clarity with staff engineers about architecture and technical strategic decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works effectively cross-functionally and is able to think rigorously, communicate effectively, and make or coordinate hard decisions and tradeoffs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills for different audiences (leadership, users, company-wide).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing rigorous incident response processes and on call rotations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encourages a healthy work environment that’s both challenging and supportive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experiences working on banking products, if not payments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1 id=&quot;engineering-manager-machine-learning-credit-risk&quot;&gt;Engineering Manager, Machine Learning Credit Risk&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Credit Risk team develops intelligent systems that help Stripe identify high-risk accounts, minimize credit losses, and improve profitability. Credit risk is a complex machine learning problem that requires us to distinguish emerging risk from healthy business activity while giving legitimate users a clear and reliable experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team consists of machine learning engineers who build models and systems used across Stripe’s credit-risk products. We work closely with partners in Product, Data Science, Credit Strategy, Operations, and other engineering teams. Together, we help stakeholders make informed decisions and support sustainable growth wherever credit risk affects Stripe’s products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an engineering manager to lead the Credit Risk team and shape how Stripe uses machine learning to manage credit risk at scale. You’ll set the team’s technical and product direction, connect advances in machine learning to measurable business outcomes, and help engineers deliver reliable systems that balance loss prevention with the user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work across engineering, product, data science, and risk to identify the highest-impact opportunities and turn them into a focused roadmap. You’ll also hire and develop engineers, strengthen the team’s technical practices, and contribute to machine learning and engineering leadership across Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and execute the strategy for detecting and mitigating credit risk through machine learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own outcomes related to credit losses, profitability, detection quality, and the user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design and delivery of reliable machine learning models, services, and decision systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate advances in machine learning into practical capabilities that support the team’s business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Data Science, Credit Strategy, Operations, and engineering teams to define priorities and deliver cross-functional programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, hire, and develop machine learning engineers while building an inclusive and effective team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to broader engineering and machine learning initiatives as a member of Stripe’s engineering management team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience managing engineers who build and operate production machine learning systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying machine learning to complex, real-world problems and leading the technical delivery of models and supporting systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting strategy and working across engineering, product, data science, operations, and business teams to deliver measurable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience recruiting, managing, and developing engineers in a fast-moving environment with significant autonomy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with credit risk, fraud detection, financial risk, trust and safety, or another domain involving decisions under uncertainty&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience balancing risk reduction with customer or user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building machine learning systems that support high-stakes, time-sensitive decisions at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting a multi-year technical direction while delivering progress through quarterly plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing geographically distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Risk Detection is focused on providing a delightful experience for our merchants and minimizing friction, while ensuring the safety of our users in the financial ecosystem. Whenever the Risk team takes action on an account, we work to notify Merchants and provide clear status on what’s happening, enable guided workflows for resolving their issues, and redefine our overall Risk processes to make them as smooth as possible for good merchants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an engineering leader to lead and grow a strong team of engineers, build relationships with customers internally and externally, and champion our vision of making Stripe’s risk management a feature that attracts and retains merchants, and becomes a product differentiator. This is an exciting opportunity to partner with teams across Stripe to build the best merchant experience, and contribute directly to Stripe’s growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Support the team in delivering a high level of technical quality and impact via APIs, user-facing experiences, services, and systems&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Recruit, hire, scale, and develop an amazing team of engineers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Executing cross-functionally with leadership, product teams, infra teams &amp;amp; risk strategists&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Be actively involved in strategic direction and platform decisions that impact all of Stripe and Stripe customers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;At least 3 years of engineering management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience as a Machine Learning Engineer or equivalent&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have managed teams that can collaborate with product teams, respond rapidly to customer needs along with building technology and capabilities that are strategic and foundational in nature&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy designing, measuring &amp;amp; improving user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are empathetic to customer needs but visionary enough to not just deliver a faster horse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable planning in quarters, and can set a vision for several years&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable working with geographically distributed teams and remote workers&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Money Management products (Financial Accounts, Treasury, Global Payouts, Issuing, and Capital) let businesses and platforms hold, move, spend, and earn on their money using the same infrastructure they already use for payments. Asia-Pacific (APAC) Money as a Service (MaaS) is a newly formed team based in Singapore. The team is responsible for bringing this product suite to Asia-Pacific markets, enabling global businesses and platforms to use these capabilities directly or offer them to their APAC users, and building the local rails, compliance, and partner integrations that make it all work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll make some of the most significant strategic, product, and technical decisions for money management in Asia-Pacific at Stripe. The systems this team builds let businesses and platforms integrate with Stripe once, then open accounts, move money, and issue cards across an expanding set of APAC markets and currencies. Businesses and platforms can grow across the region without rebuilding their stack for each country.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead multiple pods and grow the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for the team’s output: what ships, when, and how well it works for users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the engineering side of a zero-to-one charter, turn an ambiguous regional strategy into a sequenced roadmap that reduces risk, make decisions about whether to build, integrate, or partner, and coordinate launches across licensing, bank and network partners, and compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the business outcome alongside peers in product, go-to-market, legal, compliance, and partnerships, bring a product point of view, and push back when the plan is wrong&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay hands-on and in the details: read the code, review designs, use the product the way our users do, and understand how Stripe’s money movement stack works end to end so you can make sound technical calls under uncertainty&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the operating system for a newly formed team: hiring, rituals, quality standards, on-call practices, and the processes that let the team move fast while keeping money movement safe and reliable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire great engineers, develop them, and give direct, timely feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone with a founder’s mindset: high agency, comfortable with ambiguity, and biased toward shipping. You’ve built something from nothing, you know what it takes to launch a product in a new market, and you don’t wait for a perfect specification or for permission. You care about users and the product as much as about the code, and you’d rather own an outcome than a process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of engineering management experience and 8+ years of software engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking a product or team from zero to one: a new market, a new product line, or a team you built and scaled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of hiring, developing, and retaining strong engineers and building a high-performing, inclusive team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical depth to engage credibly on architecture, reliability, and tradeoffs in complex distributed systems, along with strong product judgment and the ability to translate user and market needs into engineering priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication with technical and non-technical audiences, including senior stakeholders across time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, banking, or money movement, especially launching regulated financial products (accounts, payouts, cards, or lending) in new markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in APAC markets, including working with local banks, networks, or regulators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Founder, founding engineer, or early-stage startup experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with distributed partner teams across United States, European, and APAC time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using artificial intelligence (AI) tools to improve execution, quality, and team effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Service Infrastructure enables Stripe’s engineers to build and ship products using efficient, reliable, service oriented architectures. This organization sits at the boundary between Infrastructure and Product where they engineer Stripe’s service frameworks, standard user-facing API semantics, async orchestration platforms, developer tooling, and mission critical product infrastructure (e.g. webhook fulfillment). Key priorities for this group include delivering an amazing internal developer experience, enabling Stripes to effectively leverage Infrastructure platforms, and driving systemic improvements to Stripe’s API availability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager of Managers within the Service Infrastructure organization, you will lead multiple teams, collaborate with infrastructure and product engineering leaders, and advance Stripe’s architecture. You will operate some of the company’s most critical services and you will collaborate with Stripe’s product engineering teams to develop frameworks and abstractions that accelerate the company’s most important product launches.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with high-visibility teams and their stakeholders to support key engineering initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on technical leadership (architecture/design, vision/direction/requirements setting, and incident response processes) for your reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand user needs and pain points to prioritize the right engineering work at the right time to enable product engineers to ship new features quickly and reliably.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with leaders across the company to drive improvements to Stripe’s architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage processes to help infra teams do their best work and interface effectively with the rest of Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and grow a team of engineers and engineering leaders, including line managers, to deliver high business impact projects on schedule with high-quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partners with our recruiting team to attract and hire top talent, and define the overall hiring strategies for your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience being a manager of managers (leading managers and senior ICs) of teams of at least 25 people.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience managing teams that ship and operate critical distributed system infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Led staff or principal engineers with a track record of driving alignment between highly technical collaborators on architectural or strategic decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managed effective incident response processes and on-call rotations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managed engineering teams working on API design, abstractions, frameworks, or client libraries (e.g. building internal or external developer products).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively managed demanding/conflicting stakeholder and partner relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving business and product success in a highly cross-functional organization with a high level of autonomy and responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully built a team, defined its mission, and executed on its goals. Experience recruiting, mentoring, and retaining great people that fulfill this mission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Worked effectively cross-functionally and are able to think rigorously, communicate effectively, and make or coordinate hard decisions and tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading partially remote teams and colocated teams in distant geos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encourages a healthy work environment that’s both challenging and supportive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of management experience, including 5+ years of being a manager of managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills for different audiences (leadership, users, company-wide).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience changing culture across large organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a variety of common infrastructure platforms (databases, logging, event streams, metrics, caching, etc).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building products using static (Java) and dynamically (Ruby) typed programming languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing with and contributing to open source framework ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing sustainable, in-house framework and abstraction ecosystems in large engineering organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building with cloud primitives from AWS or other cloud providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

