&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Platform Sales team works with B2B Software Platforms to help them facilitate payments for their customers using our Stripe Connect product. Software Platforms, also known as B2B Indirect, are software platform businesses who serve other businesses. Platforms already using Stripe include Shopware, Jimdo, Eversports and Shopify.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a key member to the Stripe Platforms team, you will manage and elevate relationships with a named account list while identifying new growth opportunities and ways Stripe can exceed expectations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re motivated, smart, persistent, and a great teammate, we want to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Executive (Grower), you will create partnerships between Stripe and the most innovative and fastest-growing software platforms in the world by helping them to understand how Stripe’s online commerce infrastructure can make payments a competitive advantage for their businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly manage and nurture a named account list and develop account plans for winning and expanding business with upper middle market and enterprise SaaS Platform companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain key relationships with C-level executives, while orchestrating the right executive touch points as well&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle from lead to close for upper middle market and enterprise companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with company leaders from multiple functions (e.g., Engineering, Product, and Finance) to lead complex product workshops and financial analyse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft and lead complex, bespoke commercial &amp;amp; contractual negotiations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to shaping our platform partnership strategy and building repeatable processes and scaled engagement models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and contribute to team projects to develop and refine our sales process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with Product and Engineering teams to help drive product strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an adept salesperson and relationship manager capable of engaging in business-level and technical conversations at multiple levels of the organization, including the CTO, COO, and CFO. You have experience working with upper middle market and enterprise companies. You have an in-depth understanding of the buyer journey and can lead a complex, multi-party sale in a highly consultative manner. You are used to building value in competitive situations and enjoy working on products that require deep product understanding, combined with technical knowledge. You are naturally analytical and enjoy digging into business models and helping customers quantify their investment decisions. You get excited about prospecting, and are capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish. Finally, you enjoy building – you like to actively participate in the development of our sales process, the articulation of our value proposition, and the creation of key tools and assets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of sales experience, preferably selling a technical product, with a track record of top performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience directly selling a technology product or service, preferably at an API-first company, with a record of top performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of moving sales processes forward from inception to close by leading complex, multi-party sales in a highly consultative manner, understanding strategies and applying value proposition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great listening skills and ability to quickly become a trusted resource for decision-makers across technology and finance orgs within software companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to understand complex technical problems and understand how Stripe’s solutions can address them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A positive attitude and tireless work ethic when encountering blockers to success, whether external or internal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex negotiations involving bespoke commercial agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in technology and a deep understanding of the space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in or excitement in learning about financial technology infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fastidious approach to CRM hygiene and experience utilizing thorough sales forecasting metrics on a weekly/quarterly basis and communicating them in a succinct manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-office expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Office-assigned Stripes in most of our locations are currently expected to spend at least 50% of the time in a given month in their local office or with users. This expectation may vary depending on role, team and location. For example, Stripes in our Bucharest, Romania site have an 80% in-office expectation, and those in Stripe Delivery Center roles in Mexico City, Mexico and Bengaluru, India work 100% from the office. Also, some teams have greater in-office attendance requirements, to appropriately support our users and workflows, which the hiring manager will discuss. This approach helps strike a balance between bringing people together for in-person collaboration and learning from each other, while supporting flexibility when possible.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups use Stripe to accept payments, grow revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet. We have significant work ahead, which creates an opportunity to do meaningful, high-impact work with colleagues and users around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s New Zealand business is growing, and we are building our enterprise new-business capability in the market. The Enterprise team focuses on winning and developing relationships with New Zealand’s largest and most strategic companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Enterprise Account Executive, New Business, you will establish and grow a new enterprise territory. You will identify must-win accounts, build a high-conviction pipeline, develop executive relationships, and lead complex sales cycles that help prospective users use Stripe to modernise and grow their businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute a territory strategy for New Zealand’s largest prospective enterprise users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create new pipeline through thoughtful outbound prospecting, account research, partner engagement, executive networking, and targeted account plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full new-business sales cycle, from initial outreach and discovery through solution design, commercial negotiation, close, and transition to implementation and post-sales teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop trusted relationships with senior business and technical stakeholders, including leaders across Finance, Product, Engineering, Operations, Digital, and Technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex, multi-threaded sales processes involving multiple business units, decision-makers, and internal and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Articulate Stripe’s business and technical value across the platform, connecting customer priorities to measurable commercial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Solutions Architects, Product, Partnerships, Marketing, Legal, Deal Pricing, and post-sales teams to develop and close strategic opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead commercial negotiations for complex and bespoke agreements while protecting long-term customer value and Stripe economics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build account plans, mutual action plans, financial analyses, and executive-level presentations that advance opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help establish and refine Stripe’s enterprise sales motion in New Zealand by sharing market insight, improving messaging, and contributing to repeatable sales practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a high-performing enterprise seller who thrives in new-business environments. You know how to open doors at large organisations, earn credibility with senior stakeholders, and lead complex sales cycles from ambiguity to a clear commercial outcome.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are commercially rigorous, technically curious, and persistent. You can balance strategic account planning with the day-to-day discipline needed to build pipeline and maintain momentum across long sales cycles. You are comfortable operating with autonomy and enjoy building a territory where there is substantial opportunity to define the playbook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of Sales experience with at least 3+ in&amp;nbsp; enterprise new-business sales, ideally in complex B2B software, cloud, fintech, payments, or technology environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success opening and closing net-new enterprise customers, with a clear record of meeting or exceeding sales targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing a territory or greenfield account strategy, including defining target accounts, creating pipeline, and building executive relationships from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage complex, multi-stakeholder sales cycles involving technical, financial, operational, and executive buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience selling to senior leaders, including CFO, CIO, CTO, COO, Chief Product Officer, and other executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead sophisticated commercial negotiations, including bespoke agreements and cross-functional approval processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and executing account plans across complex organisations with multiple business units and decision-makers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written, verbal, and presentation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial judgement, analytical capability, and ability to connect product capabilities to customer business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in a fast-paced, ambiguous environment with high ownership and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be based in Auckland, with travel across New Zealand as required and occasional international travel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling at a leading enterprise software, cloud, or platform company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling payments, financial infrastructure, fintech, or other technically complex platform products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling into large New Zealand or ANZ enterprise organisations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a high-growth technology company where territory strategy, messaging, and sales processes were still being developed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with technical pre-sales, product, partnerships, and implementation teams on enterprise opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a significant amount of work ahead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Executive on Stripe’s Hunter Enterprise team, you’ll drive new business by building relationships with prospective enterprise customers across Australia. You’ll work with a named account list, identify where Stripe can solve complex business challenges, and turn those opportunities into long-term customer relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Enterprise Account Executive, you’ll focus on acquiring new enterprise customers across Australia. This is a hunting role: you’ll build pipeline through targeted outbound prospecting, develop relationships across complex organisations, and lead opportunities from initial engagement through commercial negotiation, signing, and launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll create and execute account strategies that connect prospective customers’ business priorities with Stripe’s platform. Working with executive and technical stakeholders, you’ll develop business cases, shape multi-product solutions, and demonstrate Stripe’s value in competitive sales processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a commercially ambitious and highly autonomous seller who can balance near-term revenue delivery with the relationship building required to win strategic enterprise accounts. You should be comfortable creating opportunities rather than relying solely on inbound demand, and working through both technical and commercial complexity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a named portfolio of prospective enterprise accounts across ANZ and develop strategic account plans to win new business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute targeted outbound strategies to create qualified opportunities and maintain a strong pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map complex organisations, identify decision-makers, and build relationships with executive sponsors and stakeholders across Finance, Product, Engineering, and Payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the full new-business sales cycle, from prospecting and discovery through solution development, commercial negotiation, and signing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand prospective customers’ business and technical challenges, and position Stripe’s platform and products against their priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead product workshops, business case development, and financial analyses that help prospective customers quantify the value of adopting Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop competitive deal strategies and lead complex negotiations involving multiple stakeholders and bespoke commercial agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal technical, product, partnerships, and post-sales teams to shape solutions and support a coordinated transition from signing to implementation and launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you’re encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of sales experience, including at least 2 years working with enterprise customers, preferably at a technology company, with a demonstrated record of exceeding commercial targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience winning new enterprise customers through self-generated pipeline, targeted prospecting, and strategic account development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to develop and execute account plans across complex organisations with multiple business units, stakeholders, or subsidiaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading complex, multi-stakeholder sales cycles from discovery through solution development, commercial negotiation, and close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate complex technical capabilities into clear business value and engage confidently with senior business and technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation and negotiation skills, including experience building business cases and securing executive support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritise independently and make progress in a fast-moving environment with ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling to enterprise organisations in Australia and New Zealand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling payments, financial infrastructure, or technically complex software platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a growth-stage internet or software company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with technical pre-sales, product, partnerships, and implementation teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employer:&lt;/strong&gt; Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment type:&lt;/strong&gt; Full-time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; 383 Kent Street, Sydney, NSW 2000, Australia&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applications open:&lt;/strong&gt; 30th October 2026&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applications close:&lt;/strong&gt; 30th November 2026&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Platform Sales team works with B2B software platforms to help them facilitate payments for their customers using our Stripe Connect product. Software platforms, also known as B2B Indirect, are software platform businesses that serve other businesses. Platforms already using Stripe include Shopify, Lightspeed, and Mindbody.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Enterprise Account Executive for new business (Hunter), you&#39;ll create partnerships between Stripe and the most innovative and fastest-growing software platforms in the world by helping them understand how the Stripe online commerce infrastructure can make payments a competitive advantage for their businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly manage and nurture a named account list and develop account plans for winning and expanding business with enterprise platform companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain key relationships with C-level executives, while orchestrating the right executive touchpoints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to shaping our platform partnership strategy and building repeatable processes and scaled engagement models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop outbound strategies to create and nurture opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle from lead to close for enterprise platform companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop relationships with executive stakeholders at new and existing clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with company leaders from multiple functions (e.g., Engineering, Product, and Finance) to lead complex product workshops and financial analyses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and contribute to team projects to develop and refine our sales process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with Product and Engineering teams to help drive product strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re an adept salesperson and relationship manager capable of engaging in business-level and technical conversations at multiple levels of the organization, including the CTO, COO, and CFO. You have an in-depth understanding of the buyer journey and can lead a complex, multi-party sale in a highly consultative manner. You&#39;re used to building value in competitive situations and enjoy working on products that require deep product understanding, combined with technical knowledge. You have a problem-solving focus and enjoy digging into business models and helping customers quantify their investment decisions. You get excited about prospecting, and are capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish. Finally, you enjoy building—you like to actively participate in the development of our sales process, the articulation of our value proposition, and the creation of key tools and assets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re motivated, smart, persistent, and a great teammate, we want to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in spoken and written German and English&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of sales experience, preferably selling a technical product, with a track record of top performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience directly selling a technology product or service, preferably at an API-first company, with a record of top performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of moving sales processes forward from inception to close by leading complex, multi-party sales in a highly consultative manner, understanding strategies and applying a value proposition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Listening skills and ability to become a trusted resource for decision-makers across technology and finance organizations within software companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to understand complex technical problems and how Stripe solutions address them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A positive attitude and tireless work ethic when encountering blockers to success, whether external or internal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex negotiations involving bespoke commercial agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in technology and a deep understanding of the industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in or excitement in learning about financial technology infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fastidious approach to CRM hygiene and experience using thorough sales forecasting metrics on a weekly and quarterly basis and communicating them in a succinct manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Privy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to make privacy and user ownership the default online. We build simple, flexible application programming interfaces (APIs) and tools that help developers create products on crypto infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Privy provides the abstraction and infrastructure layer above wallets, integrating across blockchain networks, third-party providers, and Stripe products such as Treasury and Link. We solve complex technical problems while using Stripe’s global reach to support customers including Ramp, Klarna, Deel, Kraken, Hyperliquid, and Fomo. Our technology powers experiences for both mainstream users and crypto-native audiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://privy.io/blog/announcing-our-acquisition-by-stripe&quot;&gt;[Privy and Stripe: Bringing crypto to everyone&lt;/a&gt;]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Account Executive, Product team connects Privy’s technology with companies building new products across fintech and crypto. The team works closely with Product, Engineering, and Go-to-Market partners to understand prospective customers’ needs, shape technical and commercial solutions, and turn market insights into product and sales strategy. Its focus includes priority segments such as neobanking, payments, and brokerages.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Enterprise Account Executive you’ll own complex enterprise sales cycles and help expand Privy’s work with companies across fintech and crypto. You’ll build relationships with senior commercial and technical stakeholders, develop new opportunities, and help refine Privy’s enterprise sales approach. You’ll also contribute to Privy’s global growth strategy and represent the company at industry events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Head of Go-to-Market (GTM) to build and close a strong pipeline of enterprise prospects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and test outbound campaigns based on market and customer feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a pipeline across multiple ideal customer profiles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build deep expertise in Privy’s products and lead discovery calls with fintech prospects to understand their needs and explain Privy’s value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle, from sourcing opportunities through contract close, and serve as the primary commercial contact for prospective customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the Go-to-Market team’s strategy across North America and other global markets, including Latin America, Asia, and Africa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze market trends and emerging opportunities to inform Privy’s positioning and sales strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Privy at industry events and conferences as a spokesperson for its fintech business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 to 10 years of experience in sales, business development, or a related field, including experience selling a technical product and a record of strong performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience selling technical products within fintech, crypto, or a related industry. You can build a pipeline, lead complex sales cycles, and develop trusted relationships with commercial and technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading complex, multi-stakeholder enterprise deals involving legal, compliance, engineering, and other buyer-side teams through contract close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in an early-stage environment and build repeatable processes where none exist.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building strong networks within a specific industry, ideally fintech, payments, or crypto.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, negotiation, relationship management, and sales skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling API-first or developer-focused products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead discovery conversations with technical buyers, including chief technology officers and product leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with crypto infrastructure, such as stablecoins, on-ramps and off-ramps, wallets, and custody, or a demonstrated ability to learn the space quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Revenue Suite Product Sales is a team of functional and technical specialists who both lead and advise on deals for the most strategically important products in Stripe’s portfolio.&amp;nbsp; The Sales team has been tasked with attacking a $100B market opportunity for back office finance automation across billing, tax, revenue reporting, and data.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Revenue Suite Account Executive (Existing Business) at Stripe, you&#39;ll use your sales and product expertise to help drive growth through existing Stripe customers. You&#39;ll collaborate with the core sales, marketing, product marketing, and product teams to develop deep product and industry knowledge and drive strategic deals. You&#39;ll lead in-depth product discussions with existing and prospective customers and build and execute against our go-to-market strategy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive revenue to achieve targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead sales and upsell conversations of Stripe for existing and prospective customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive strategic thought leadership within assigned territory to ensure user success and revenue growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the sales process and competitors for Stripe, including software, hardware, and payments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as both an internal and customer-facing expert on Stripe, especially for your specialised products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize and relay customer feedback and our findings to inform Stripe&#39;s product roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with Product, Marketing, and User Operations teams to help amplify our growth trajectory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;You&#39;re an adept salesperson, capable of engaging in business-level and technical conversations at multiple levels of the organization, including CEO, CFO, and CTO. You&#39;re used to building value in competitive situations and enjoy working on products that require deep product understanding, combined with technical knowledge. You&#39;re as comfortable working with clients as with internal stakeholders (including executives). You&#39;re excited to become an expert and to share your knowledge. You&#39;re an organized self-starter, an excellent communicator who is detail-oriented and has a track record for improving the processes and organizations around you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of sales or prospecting experience at a technology company and a track record of top performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning a direct sales quota, with direct sales experience closing new business and expanding existing users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to build strong collaborative working relationships with business partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to deal with ambiguity and thrive in an unstructured, fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to be a self-starter capable of driving business results without significant supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hands-on mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation skills, particularly for in-person meetings with multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex negotiations involving bespoke commercial agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex technical requirements and craft solutions across multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience selling financial services or similar software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in selling billing solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to sell in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe MALPB operates in a complex, fast-moving regulatory environment. The Risk and Compliance team is responsible for ensuring that our expansion is grounded in a bulletproof governance framework that matches the speed of our technology.&lt;br&gt;Having successfully established our foundational ERM policies, taxonomy, and risk registers, we are entering the integration phase. This team is building the future of &quot;AI-Native&quot; risk management—where governance frameworks are embedded into daily business operations through automated data pipelines and LLM orchestration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a risk professional who combines strong enterprise risk management (ERM) experience with an analytical mindset and an interest in technology. Grounded in risk, audit, or compliance, you’ll help strengthen risk management across Stripe MALPB by bringing &amp;nbsp;independent judgment, cross-functional collaboration, and clear communication to complex business challenges. ERM expertise is the primary focus, complemented by SQL skills and curiosity about how AI and automation can improve risk and control processes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We are looking for a rare breed of professional: someone with the executive presence to stand up a banking governance program, combined with the hands-on engineering capabilities to automate it themselves. &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;As Enterprise Risk Management Lead, you will lead MALPB’s ERM program end-to-end, translating its established framework into consistent practices across the bank. You will provide independent second-line oversight and challenge, deliver clear reporting to management and the Board, and improve how the bank identifies, assesses, monitors, and responds to risk.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead risk assessments. &lt;/strong&gt;Run the annual Risk and Control Self-Assessment (RCSA) cycle, providing independent second-line challenge of first-line risk assessments, risk ratings, and control effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintain core risk infrastructure. &lt;/strong&gt;Maintain the Master Control Library, Central Risk Register, and enterprise risk taxonomy, with effective version control and change management to reflect evolving operations and emerging risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Monitor risk appetite and remediation. &lt;/strong&gt;Aggregate, analyze, and validate Key Risk Indicators (KRIs) against Board-approved risk appetite thresholds. Escalate breaches, require appropriate Management Action Plans (MAPs), and track remediation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver decision-ready reporting. &lt;/strong&gt;Combine quantitative risk metrics with qualitative assessments of emerging risks to produce the quarterly Enterprise Risk Scorecard and present clear, actionable insights to the Management Risk Committee and Board of Directors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply data-driven analysis. &lt;/strong&gt;Use basic SQL queries and existing reporting tools to extract and sample data for control verification, partnering with technical teams on more complex analysis, automation, and system integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use AI to improve execution. &lt;/strong&gt;Explore and apply AI tools to support control monitoring and testing, partnering with technical teams to develop agents that flag potential anomalies or control deficiencies for expert review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advance continuous monitoring. &lt;/strong&gt;Progressively supplement point-in-time testing with automated dashboards and ongoing monitoring of key operational and regulatory controls.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in enterprise risk management, operational risk, or risk advisory within a regulated financial institution, fintech company, or Big Four technology-risk practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience implementing and embedding ERM programs—including RCSAs, KRIs, risk registers, and control libraries—within active, fast-paced business operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, including the ability to interpret large datasets, assess data quality, and translate findings into meaningful risk insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of SQL, including the ability to write basic queries for data extraction and analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
