&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in software engineering, integration engineering, solutions engineering, technical consulting, or a comparable customer-facing engineering role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to write code in languages such as Go, Java, Python, C#, C++, or similar, and quickly understand and debug unfamiliar code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong generalist technical experience, including SQL and an understanding of APIs, data structures, distributed systems, and software architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or delivering integrations between complex systems and third-party APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of API security, reliability, testing, and production-readiness practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to move between architecture and implementation, using code, logs, and data to solve open-ended problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to explain technical concepts clearly to engineers, business stakeholders, and senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A user-first approach and confidence leading technical work across multiple teams in an ambiguous, fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI-native companies, developer infrastructure, cloud platforms, or other rapidly scaling technology companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payments or financial infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI coding assistants or LLM-based agents in engineering work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering migrations, multi-product implementations, or international launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical writing skills and a willingness to teach and mentor others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a technology company focused on improving the conditions for economic growth and prosperity. We build programmable financial infrastructure, rethinking from first principles how financial services should work, to make it easier and cheaper for any business to start and scale. More than 10 million &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/customers&quot;&gt;businesses&lt;/a&gt; build on Stripe, spanning the economic frontier—from solo founders to established enterprises—united by a practical focus on growth. The most ambitious companies in the world use Stripe as core infrastructure to grow faster. They process trillions of dollars a year on Stripe, equivalent to around 1.6% of global GDP. While economic growth makes everyone better off, open markets also enable greater variety. When any business can easily serve a global customer base, the quality and diversity of products in the world increase, and craft and creativity are unleashed into the smallest niches. Our own growth is wholly contingent on the success of the businesses building on Stripe. We therefore invest back into our technology at an unusual rate. We make &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/roadmap&quot;&gt;upgrades to our products&lt;/a&gt; every single day to deliver compounding gains to our customers. We maintain some of the most &lt;a href=&quot;https://status.stripe.com/&quot;&gt;reliable APIs&lt;/a&gt; on the internet. We build entirely new &lt;a href=&quot;https://tempo.xyz/&quot;&gt;pieces&lt;/a&gt; of &lt;a href=&quot;https://mpp.dev/&quot;&gt;financial&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://joinopenstandard.com/&quot;&gt;infrastructure&lt;/a&gt; to enable new ideas. And our significant advances in &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/radar&quot;&gt;risk and fraud&lt;/a&gt; infrastructure over many years are making the internet economy safer and more accessible.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Though people at Stripe don’t tend to take themselves seriously, Stripe is a fairly serious place: our customers are depending on us for their livelihoods. We admire ambition, intensity, curiosity, humility, and rigor. The most effective people become knowledgeable about many domains besides their own. Any company is an applied exercise in understanding some aspect of society or the market. In working with so many (especially the new and innovative ones), we think that Stripe is one of the very best places to learn about how the world works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;APAC Payments TechOps is a team based in Singapore. Our charter is to improve the health and resilience of our payment acquiring volume, making it easier for Stripe to build and operate the integrations that support hundreds of billions of dollars in payments annually. Our team partners closely with payments and platform engineering teams to assess systems or processes that create high operational workloads, then develops durable solutions via code, tooling, data, and process improvements. We are responsible for the financial data quality of key systems at Stripe, ensuring that data is quarantined without impacting downstream systems while implementing the right changes upstream to prevent recurring issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every internship at Stripe centers around a real, legitimate project that our team urgently needs, touching many parts of our operations and stack. We will support you in shipping it. Yes, you will actually ship it. Example projects include building automation to detect anomalies in financial data, improving reconciliation tooling, or streamlining certificate management workflows. As a Stripe intern, you&#39;ll be tackling important projects while working alongside exceptional people who insist on doing their best work. You&#39;ll learn from people with high standards who are great at inspiring others to do more and go further. We value technical and personal growth, and see our internship program as a vehicle to foster both.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate problems in systems by examining code, writing SQL queries, reading logs, and inspecting data pipelines to understand system behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write code that will be used in production and has meaningful impact to Stripe&#39;s payment operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give and receive technical feedback through code reviews or design discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with other engineers and cross-functional stakeholders to proactively seek and incorporate feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn quickly by asking great questions, by working with your intern manager and teammates effectively, and by communicating the status of your work clearly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In exchange, you&#39;ll have the support and opportunity to pursue big ideas and change how things work, with a high degree of autonomy. You’ll be mentored by some of the most creative and technically rigorous people in the industry, working on teams reshaping how money moves and how businesses grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ambitious builder:&lt;/strong&gt; You’re energized by building solutions without clear precedent and solving problems with far-reaching consequences. Successful Stripes are deeply curious, and prefer the joy of discovery to the comfort of certainty.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rigorous thinker:&lt;/strong&gt; You appreciate that things worth doing are rarely simple. You enjoy working on problems that have never been tackled before.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptable problem solver:&lt;/strong&gt; You adapt quickly and treat obstacles as opportunities. At Stripe we embrace kindness while encouraging Stripes to take measured risks and act boldly, even in the absence of consensus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong fundamental understanding of computer science through pursuit of a Bachelor&#39;s, Master&#39;s, or PhD degree in computer science, information systems, data science, or a related discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some experience and familiarity with programming, either through side projects or classwork. We work mostly in Ruby, Go, and Python. We believe new programming languages can be learned if the fundamentals and general knowledge are present&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience from previous internships or other multi-person projects, including open source contributions, that demonstrate evaluating and receiving feedback from mentors, peers, and stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to learn unfamiliar systems and form an understanding of those systems, through independent research and working with a mentor and subject matter experts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 2 years of university education, or equivalent work experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with SQL and working with data, either through coursework or personal projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with developer tools (e.g. git)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong interest in understanding the root cause of issues and building durable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;One or more areas of specialized knowledge balanced with general skills, such as data engineering, systems debugging, or financial data analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to write clearly to explain your work to stakeholders, team members, and other Stripes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Payments organization owns some of Stripe’s most critical payment flows and a platform that processes hundreds of billions of dollars in payments a year. Our team builds and scales the infrastructure and financial partner integrations that enables Stripe to accept, manage, and payout money across many countries, currencies, and payment methods.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work is core to Stripe’s business, and thousands of developers use our platform and infrastructure to create valuable products and services that billions of people use. Our goal is to increase the GDP of the internet by making it easy to build global products, services, and platforms that handle money.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical Operations roles in Payments are a dynamic and key component of Stripe&#39;s success. Focused on financial partner integrations and funds flow expansion, we sit at the intersection of product/platform engineers and financial partners, connecting them to ensure that everyone thrives and nothing is lost in translation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team partners closely with various finance and infrastructure engineering teams to ensure timely delivery of accurate data between financial partners, internal stakeholders, and Stripe leaders. We report and trace all of Stripe’s money movement transactions, including payments in more than 30 currencies and dozens of countries. You’ll own building and scaling Stripe’s manual and programmatic financial reporting and reconciliation processes for intra-company and outgoing money movement transactions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become a domain expert in an area of Stripe’s payments stack&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find automated solutions and implement tool updates to drive operational efficiencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with Stripe&#39;s financial partners to drive alignment on product usage, troubleshoot and solve technical problems or breakages&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organize and direct complex technical changes and projects between Stripe and our partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and automate inefficient or unnecessary manual processes through code changes, partner agreements, or making and coordinating more complex code changes across Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design future anomaly detection systems and tools to ensure that data flowing through our partner and internal systems is reliable and correct&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across the company, including engineering, accounting, financial partnerships and product, to trace and account for billions of dollars moving through the Stripe platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle inquiries from internal Stripes and external partners&#39; technical teams, often requiring detailed investigation and sometimes code changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical Operations roles are one part coding and one part managing projects. The ideal candidate will have experience in both, but successful candidates may index more highly in one or the other. We work mostly in Ruby and Java. However, languages can be learned: we care much more about your general coding skill than knowledge of a particular language or framework.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-6 years of experience in a technical role (ex: Technical Operations, Software Engineer, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience managing communications and workflows with technical and non-technical teams across internal and external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to write high quality code. We work mostly in Ruby and Java. However, languages can be learned: we care much more about your general coding skill than knowledge of a particular language or framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort using SQL to navigate Stripe&#39;s data and diagnose the scope and urgency of issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be able to build operational processing and tooling from scratch to prevent repeatable issues&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with developer tools (e.g. git), and an ability to make well-scoped code changes in Stripe&#39;s codebase&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great technical problem-solving skills, with an ability to develop a working understanding of a technical system using a variety of methods. These include (but aren&#39;t limited to): reading/writing code, reading documentation or partner specifications, running debugging programs, reading logs, asking well-formed questions to domain experts, or digging into the raw data through various interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of and experience with payment technologies and ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing communications and workflows with external financial partners and vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Money Management products (Financial Accounts, Treasury, Global Payouts, Issuing, and Capital) let businesses and platforms hold, move, spend, and earn on their money using the same infrastructure they already use for payments. APAC Money as a Service (MaaS) is a newly formed team, based in Singapore, responsible for bringing this product suite to Asia-Pacific markets, enabling global businesses and platforms to use these capabilities directly or offer them to their APAC users, and building the local rails, compliance, and partner integrations that make it all work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;None of this works without financial partners: the banks, card networks, and licensed institutions whose systems our products run on in each market. Technical Operations in APAC MaaS owns the day-to-day health of those partner integrations, existing and new, and the working technical relationship with the partners behind them. We sit between product and platform engineering, Stripe&#39;s partnerships and compliance teams, and our partners&#39; technical teams, which gives us an unusually complete view of how money moves in the region: the code and the real-world mechanics behind it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits where Stripe&#39;s engineering meets the financial institutions we build on, and it is broader than most technical operations seats. You&#39;ll own the health of the partner integrations that power APAC MaaS, and you&#39;ll be the technical face of Stripe to the banks, networks, and institutions behind them. One week that means working through a partner specification and reconciling settlement files; the next, shipping tooling or running an operational review with a partner&#39;s engineering team. Because every APAC launch depends on partner readiness, you&#39;ll have direct line of sight into what the team ships and a real say in how. It&#39;s a role that builds technical depth and partner judgment at the same time, in a region where we&#39;re still writing the playbook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the operational health of APAC MaaS&#39;s financial partner integrations across accounts, payouts, and card issuing: monitor them, catch problems early, and drive issues to root cause and durable fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary technical point of contact for our partners in the region. Run recurring operational reviews, manage escalations end to end, align on product usage and specifications, and keep both Stripe and the partner on track against their commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead partner-facing technical change: onboarding and certifying new integrations, specification changes, migrations and cutovers, and incident reviews, coordinating Stripe engineering, partnerships, compliance, and the partner&#39;s teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and resolve issues across the stack. Read and write code, query data, work through logs and partner reports and files, and make scoped changes in Stripe&#39;s codebase when that is the right fix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reconciliation and anomaly detection so that money moving through our partner integrations is correct, traceable, and accounted for, in collaboration with engineering, accounting, and partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remove manual work through code, tooling, or changes to how we operate with partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become the team&#39;s domain expert on how money actually moves in each APAC market: rails, cutoffs, settlement cycles, file formats, return codes, and partner-specific behavior. Document it and make it usable by the rest of the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring partner realities into product and engineering decisions, and define what &quot;partner-ready&quot; means for each market launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re equally at home in a partner&#39;s steering call and in a debugger, and you enjoy moving between the two. You are precise: you read the specification to the end, you notice when a reconciliation is off by one record, and you follow up until the loose end is closed. You build trust with external counterparts by being prepared, direct, and reliable, and you can hold a partner (or Stripe) to a commitment while keeping the relationship strong.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years in a technical role (for example Technical Operations, Software Engineering, Integration Engineering, or Solutions Architecture), including meaningful time working directly with external technical counterparts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning working relationships with external partners such as banks, card networks, processors, or similar institutions: running operational reviews, managing escalations, and driving technical changes to completion across organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to write high-quality, maintainable code and SQL, read and navigate an unfamiliar codebase, and make scoped changes safely; familiarity with developer tools such as Git&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of payments or money movement technologies and ecosystems, such as bank transfers, payouts, card issuing, settlement, or reconciliation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail, with a track record of working from specifications, file formats, and financial data where small errors have real consequences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great communication skills, both oral and written, with the ability to frame messages for technical and non-technical audiences inside and outside Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great problem-solving skills, with an ability to develop a working understanding of a technical system using a variety of methods: reading and writing code, writing SQL queries, reading documentation or partner specifications, running debugging programs, reading logs, asking well-formed questions of domain experts, or digging into the raw data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with banking and payment rails, settlement, and reporting conventions in Asia-Pacific markets such as Australia, Singapore, Hong Kong, or New Zealand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking a new partner integration live: certification, go-live, and hypercare&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with card issuing, processor, or network integrations, or with ledgering and financial data quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with distributed teams and partners across US, European, and APAC time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI tools to improve execution, quality, and effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of cmpanies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our organization is on a mission to unlock local payment methods (LPMs) at scale. As a growing share of e-commerce moves to non-card payments, LPMs represent a massive opportunity for Stripe that’s measured in billions of dollars. We support high-volume payment methods and the platform that will enable Stripe to onboard new LPM partners at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team is the connective tissue between product engineering, payment partners, and support. We own reliability and customer outcomes for the payment methods we operate. We integrate new LPMs, ship security and reliability enhancements, and eliminate toil at its source so Stripe can grow its LPM portfolio to match its ambitions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll ship code to eliminate recurring operational work and integrate LPMs on our standardized platform. You&#39;ll own those integrations beyond launch, using automation and root-cause fixes to make them easier to operate as Stripe adds more payment methods. Alongside integration work, you&#39;ll own security and reliability enhancements for the systems our pillar owns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll balance project work with a business-hours support rotation, answering technical questions from merchants and internal teams. This role does not include a 24/7 pager or incident on-call.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unblock merchants and internal teams by independently investigating technical issues through code, logs, and data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remove operational barriers to LPM growth by automating recurring work and fixing its root causes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own security and reliability enhancements across our pillar&#39;s systems, shipping code changes and infrastructure migrations with product engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate LPMs on our standardized platform and own their reliability and customer outcomes beyond launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve technical problems efficiently with AI tools, checking outputs against source evidence and validating code changes before deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable scaled support teams to resolve repeatable issues independently through runbooks, tooling, and training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize operational improvements with product engineering teams, agree on ownership, and measure the outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TechOps IRE roles combine software engineering, data analysis, AI systems development, and cross-functional partner management. The ideal candidate brings experience across technical systems, data investigation, and complex project ownership. They find genuine satisfaction in making things run reliably at scale through both human judgment and intelligent automation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical background, including 2+ years of experience designing, building, and operating software systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly fluent with developer tooling (e.g. version control, CI/CD, real-time observability metrics and logs) and an ability to make well-scoped code changes in a large codebase&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop a deep understanding of complex systems through reading &lt;em&gt;and&lt;/em&gt; writing code,&amp;nbsp; studying documentation and partner API specifications, running debugging tools, reading logs, querying raw data, and asking precise questions of domain experts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building with AI and LLM tooling with established clear outcomes. You don&#39;t need experience with any specific framework, but you should be able to pick up new tools quickly and think clearly about where automation adds value versus where human judgment is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL skills and proficiency navigating a variety of data systems to diagnose and scope issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to frame messages appropriately for both technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An instinct to build solutions that increase the leverage of the people around you—not just to solve the problem in front of you, but to eliminate the class of problem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of and experience with payment technologies, open banking, and financial data ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or operating agentic or LLM-powered workflows in a production environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Presto, Splunk, Logscale or similar data querying and log analysis tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing technical relationships with external partners or vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a technology company focused on improving the conditions for economic growth and prosperity. We build programmable financial infrastructure, rethinking from first principles how financial services should work, to make it easier and cheaper for any business to start and scale. More than 10 million &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/customers&quot;&gt;businesses&lt;/a&gt; build on Stripe, spanning the economic frontier—from solo founders to established enterprises—united by a practical focus on growth. The most ambitious companies in the world use Stripe as core infrastructure to grow faster. They process trillions of dollars a year on Stripe, equivalent to around 1.6% of global GDP. While economic growth makes everyone better off, open markets also enable greater variety. When any business can easily serve a global customer base, the quality and diversity of products in the world increase, and craft and creativity are unleashed into the smallest niches. Our own growth is wholly contingent on the success of the businesses building on Stripe. We therefore invest back into our technology at an unusual rate. We make &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/roadmap&quot;&gt;upgrades to our products&lt;/a&gt; every single day to deliver compounding gains to our customers. We maintain some of the most &lt;a href=&quot;https://status.stripe.com/&quot;&gt;reliable APIs&lt;/a&gt; on the internet. We build entirely new &lt;a href=&quot;https://tempo.xyz/&quot;&gt;pieces&lt;/a&gt; of &lt;a href=&quot;https://mpp.dev/&quot;&gt;financial&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://joinopenstandard.com/&quot;&gt;infrastructure&lt;/a&gt; to enable new ideas. And our significant advances in &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/radar&quot;&gt;risk and fraud&lt;/a&gt; infrastructure over many years are making the internet economy safer and more accessible.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Though people at Stripe don’t tend to take themselves seriously, Stripe is a fairly serious place: our customers are depending on us for their livelihoods. We admire ambition, intensity, curiosity, humility, and rigor. The most effective people become knowledgeable about many domains besides their own. Any company is an applied exercise in understanding some aspect of society or the market. In working with so many (especially the new and innovative ones), we think that Stripe is one of the very best places to learn about how the world works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;APAC Payments TechOps is a team based in Singapore. Our charter is to improve the health and resilience of our payment acquiring volume, making it easier for Stripe to build and operate the integrations that support hundreds of billions of dollars in payments annually. Our team partners closely with payments and platform engineering teams to assess systems or processes that create high operational workloads, then develops durable solutions via code, tooling, data, and process improvements. We are responsible for the financial data quality of key systems at Stripe, ensuring that data is quarantined without impacting downstream systems while implementing the right changes upstream to prevent recurring issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a company, we believe in end-to-end ownership of projects. For any given project, we have one person on point. While they don&#39;t necessarily have to do all the work themselves, it&#39;s their job to make sure all the work gets done. We launch betas and prototypes as early as we can. This helps ensure that we&#39;re building what users actually want.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate directly with peer engineers and cross-functional stakeholders to execute complex technical projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give meaningful feedback on code reviews and technical designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that the systems your team operates continue running well and can scale to meet the needs of our users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the skills to own a project, and eventually an entire domain, from beginning to end, learning project management and technical leadership skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn quickly by asking great questions, working with your intern manager and teammates effectively, communicating the status of your work clearly, and building with the latest AI tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In exchange, you&#39;ll have the support and opportunity to pursue big ideas and change how things work, with a high degree of autonomy. You’ll be mentored by some of the most creative and technically rigorous people in the industry, working on teams reshaping how money moves and how businesses grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ambitious builder: &lt;/strong&gt;You’re energized by building solutions without clear precedent and solving problems with far-reaching consequences. Successful Stripes are deeply curious, and prefer the joy of discovery to the comfort of certainty.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rigorous thinker:&lt;/strong&gt; You appreciate that things worth doing are rarely simple. You enjoy working on problems that have never been tackled before.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptable problem solver:&lt;/strong&gt; You adapt quickly and treat obstacles as opportunities.&amp;nbsp; At Stripe we embrace kindness while encouraging Stripes to take measured risks and act boldly, even in the absence of consensus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in computer science or a directly related field, obtained by summer 2027, or equivalent work experience with no more than 18 months of professional experience (excluding internship).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience and familiarity with programming, either through side projects or classwork. We work mostly in Java, Ruby, JavaScript, Scala, and Go. We believe new programming languages can be learned if the fundamentals and general knowledge are present.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience from either previous internships or working collaboratively on multi-person coding projects (in a university or professional setting).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to learn unfamiliar systems and form an understanding of those systems, through independent research and working with a mentor or subject matter experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written communication skills, with the ability to explain your work to stakeholders, team members, and other Stripes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to leverage AI tools to accelerate development while applying rigorous critical thinking and professional judgement to review, refine, and validate all outputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;One or more areas of specialized knowledge (frontend, backend, infrastructure or other technologies) balanced with general skills and knowledge.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in code review practices, and an understanding of how to safely update production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with navigating and managing work in large code bases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading small projects independently, and contributing to larger projects alongside peers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate with high agency in navigating complex technical obstacles independently, knowing precisely when to unblock oneself and when to ask for help.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To advance Stripe’s important mission, we are building a world class Internal Audit (IA) team. Our purpose is to strengthen the organization’s ability to create, protect, and sustain value by providing the board and management with independent, risk-based, and objective assurance, advice, insight, and foresight. We are consumed with the goal of moving as fast as the business, being powered by technology, and increasing the maturity of Stripe’s controls where it matters the most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our IA team is responsible for providing objective assurance on the design and operational effectiveness of Stripe’s internal controls and business processes, its compliance with laws and regulations, its risk management framework, and other governance processes. Organized as a single global function, the team operates under a unified methodology, set of policies, and governance model — with specialized leads who bring deep domain expertise while working in alignment with that shared framework. We’re looking for a leader with extensive finance, operations, fiduciary, and regulatory compliance audit experience who will help us build and scale a global audit program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior member of the EMEA IA team you will be central to shaping our audit landscape in one of the most dynamic sectors of FinTech. In this pivotal role, you will help drive the execution of a comprehensive, risk-based internal audit strategy that not only anticipates emerging risks but also aligns seamlessly with our management&#39;s vision and regulatory landscape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the Internal Audit team, you will harness your expertise in governance, risk management, and internal controls to produce invaluable assessments that empower our Board, Audit Committee, and senior leadership to make informed, strategic decisions. This is more than just an auditing position; it&#39;s an opportunity to influence the very framework of our operations, protect our organization from unforeseen challenges, and bolster our commitment to excellence and compliance in the rapidly evolving world of Fintech. If you&#39;re looking to make a significant impact and elevate your career in an innovative and supportive environment, this is your chance to step into a role where your insights will drive meaningful change and ensure our continued success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is office-based in Dublin, Ireland.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and execute risk-based internal audits and provide input into a risk-based internal audit strategy that ensures comprehensive, end-to-end audit coverage. This strategy should reflect emerging risks, management priorities, and regulatory obligations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee evaluation and testing of governance, risk management, internal controls, compliance, financial reporting, and operational processes to ensure their effectiveness, accuracy, and regulatory compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present independent, objective reports directly to senior leadership on the effectiveness of internal controls, risk management, and governance processes, communicating complex technical and regulatory risks to senior stakeholders in clear, actionable terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to engage with partners and regulators; help prepare and present audit evidence and findings to enhance confidence in our internal oversight processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clearly communicate complex risks and impacts to senior stakeholders, including the Board, Audit Committee, and regulators (e.g., FCA, CBI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with senior management and cross-functional teams - including engineering, product, treasury, legal, compliance, and operations - to translate audit findings into durable, structured remediation plans with control enhancements, tracking all corrective actions to verified closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Invest in understanding the business to better identify areas of need and opportunities to advise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and stay current on applicable regulatory requirements and (e.g., GAAP, IFRS, PSD2, EMD2, EBA, etc.), emerging trends and best practices.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in internal auditing, risk management, or compliance, preferably within the banking or financial services sector.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in auditing financial controls, operations and regulatory compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience in risk-based audit planning, execution, and reporting across governance, compliance, financial reporting, and operational controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional certification such as CIA, CPA, CAMS, CRCM or similar is required (or active pursuit).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills with experience using data analytics and continuous monitoring tools to support audit activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills; ability to present complex issues clearly to non-technical senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead cross-functional remediation efforts and track closure of corrective actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High degree of integrity, independence, and professional skepticism.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s degree in Accounting, Finance, MBA, or related advanced degree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a regulated financial institution or network with complex relationships among network partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with audit management software, automation platforms, and advanced data analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of building continuous audit/monitoring programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Employee Relations and People Risk &amp;amp; Compliance team is a relatively new center of excellence here at Stripe. We are striving to build a respectful, balanced, well-skilled team focused on enabling the People team, managers, and ICs to navigate challenging career moments while balancing compliance, empathy, and risk, resulting in success and engagement for all.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an exceptional leader for the Employee Relations, People Risk &amp;amp; Compliance function to join our team at Stripe with coverage for our locations in EMEA and APAC. This individual will have deep subject knowledge and expertise in employee relations, a strong understanding of people related risk in the regulatory space and will be an instrumental player/coach, who will lead the team focusing on improving and implementing frameworks, guidelines, approaches, and best practices. The International Employee Relations, People Risk &amp;amp; Compliance Leader&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;will be highly cross functional and collaborative, partnering to inform and support Stripes and cross functional colleagues, both within and outside of the People team. This role reports into the Global Employee Relations, People Risk &amp;amp; Compliance leader at Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Case Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide support to or personally lead medium to high complexity employee relations investigations, making recommendations on appropriate courses of action, matching investigation strategy to the complexity, risk, sensitivity, and confidentiality of the investigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide guidance on complex performance management cases, depending on what support needs are determined with People Partners and People Consultants.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure cases are handled fairly, consistently, transparently, in a timely fashion, and in line with company culture, policies, and appropriate local laws.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advising&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Counsel People Partners, People Consultants, and business leaders on ER issues, trends and risks to foster sound business decisions, rooted in commerciality and aligned with Stripe’s Operating Principles.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that optimal decisions are made by leaders, People Partners and other stakeholders through influencing, coaching, and by providing technical expertise and sound strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and refresh training offerings depending on company needs and external regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish best practices and frameworks for critical business and regulatory activities and/or policies, in partnership with our employment legal team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage proactive and positive relationships with works councils and unions where applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the International team, building an exceptional performance bench&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect, analyze, interpret and make recommendations on ER related data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure alignment to the larger strategy of the People team and Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scaling&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve, socialize and rollout processes, approaches, guidelines, practices and operating procedures to use in EMEA, APAC and globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement appropriate risk frameworks relevant to the People team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and conduct training for leaders, managers, employees, People Partners, People Consultants, Talent Partners, and other stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain an organized case management system; ability to run analytics and metrics, produce dashboards, and drive monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree required; JD, MBA, or other Advanced Degree preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of Employee Relations/Human Resources experience managing complex global investigations and people related risk required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of direct management/supervisory experience leading cross-border teams required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting up and managing productive relationships with works councils and/or unions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive understanding of the regulatory environment in which Stripe operates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior written oral communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to remain positive, collaborative and objective while under pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of positively influencing leaders, teams, and stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to be a coach, mentor, advise, and partner with stakeholders at varying levels of seniority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of ER, people risk labour relations, training, and conflict resolution, along with direct experience leading complex global investigations at all levels, including executive level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with and extensive experience in employment laws in the EMEA region (and APAC preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work under pressure and deal with complex issues, while maintaining composure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced decision maker who uses good reasoning and sound judgment required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to be discreet and maintain confidentiality is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be self-motivated and have an enhanced ability to prioritize/plan in a fast-paced, high growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open to travel (some travel may be required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;Who we are&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before Stripe, every growing internet platform needed a payments team. Today, every growing internet platform needs a way to establish trust in its users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identity verification is a core piece of economic infrastructure for online businesses. Stripe Identity enables businesses to digitally verify their users through identity documents and other signals for fraud prevention, regulatory, and trust and safety use cases. We are building the future of identity verification and trust in the digital economy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Identity Product Experience team owns Stripe Identity’s mobile SDKs for iOS, Android, and React Native. These SDKs enable businesses to embed secure, high-quality identity-verification experiences directly in their mobile applications. Our work spans mobile user experience, reusable SDK architecture, camera and document-capture experiences, developer experience, security, accessibility, reliability, and integration with Stripe’s backend systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Stripe Identity?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build mobile experiences that help establish trust between businesses and their users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solve challenging product and technical problems involving mobile platforms, sensitive data, fraud prevention, and global scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create SDKs used by developers across industries, including fintech, marketplaces, and online platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape the future of digital identity and make verification easier, safer, and more accessible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our vision is to build the world’s most trusted store of verified identities, enabling frictionless identity verification across Stripe and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for engineers who care deeply about mobile craft and the entire user journey. You should enjoy translating complex technical and regulatory requirements into simple, polished experiences; working through ambiguity; and learning new technologies and systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us to build mobile identity-verification experiences that businesses can integrate easily and that their users can trust.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an iOS engineer on the Identity team, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain Stripe Identity’s mobile SDKs and verification experiences across iOS, Android, and React Native.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create intuitive, polished experiences for complex flows such as identity-document and selfie capture, while accounting for accessibility, device capabilities, and varied real-world conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reliable and extensible SDK APIs and reusable components that make it easy for developers to integrate Stripe Identity into their applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across mobile clients, supporting APIs, and services to deliver features end to end rather than treating the mobile application as an isolated layer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve SDK performance, reliability, observability, testing, release processes, and backward compatibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make thoughtful architectural decisions that balance user experience, developer experience, security, privacy, and long-term maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with product managers, designers, machine-learning engineers, backend engineers, user researchers, and other mobile teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Stripe users and field teams to understand integration challenges and turn their feedback into product and platform improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help establish and evolve mobile-engineering practices across Identity and Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate and maintain the systems and SDKs the team owns, including diagnosing production issues and improving them based on what we learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Who you are&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of professional software-development experience, including meaningful experience building and shipping mobile applications or SDKs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing for at least one major mobile platform using technologies such as Swift or Objective-C for iOS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software-design fundamentals and experience creating maintainable APIs, components, or frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering mobile functionality beyond an isolated UI layer for example, integrating with APIs and services, handling local state, or working with device capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience testing, debugging, monitoring, and improving mobile software in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate effectively with engineering, product, design, and other technical and non-technical partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A demonstrated commitment to building high-quality user and developer experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building mobile SDKs, shared libraries, or developer-facing APIs used outside your immediate team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with both iOS and Android, or with cross-platform technologies such as React Native or Kotlin Multiplatform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with camera, image-processing, document-capture, biometrics, or other device-integrated mobile experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing mobile software that handles sensitive data and applies security and privacy principles by default.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with accessibility, internationalization, mobile performance, and unreliable network conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mobile CI, automated testing, release automation, observability, or developer-productivity tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to backend APIs or services that support mobile products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to simplify complex requirements and favor durable, scalable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort reasoning clearly and moving with urgency in a fast-paced, ambiguous environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Stripe’s products, ideally through integrating Stripe APIs or SDKs into another application.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Corporate Technology (CorpTech) Services team is a strategic support partner to all Stripes, in office and remote.&amp;nbsp; We ensure the successful operation of new hires, account off-boards and critical business systems with a global team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Tier 1 Support Engineer to join the AMER CorpTech Services team to provide in-person, thoughtful and individualized support for all Stripes. Stripe is looking for individuals who can work in a fast paced environment and work autonomously to deliver team oriented results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be responsible for providing technical assistance and support related to computer systems, hardware, and software. Respond to queries, run diagnostic programs, isolate problems, and determine and implement solutions.&amp;nbsp; In-person support is required as well as setting up desks and managing/auditing peripherals.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical support to Stripes, contingent workers, and vendors in person, by email, through Slack, and through the ticketing system, guiding users through troubleshooting and following up to confirm resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose and resolve computer hardware, software, and system issues, including troubleshooting scripts, automation, and Stripe-provided macOS, ChromeOS, and iOS devices and peripherals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and maintain workplace applications, including Google Workspace, Slack, Zoom, Jira, and Confluence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provision laptops for New Stripe onboarding and fleet upgrades, support vendor and contractor onboarding, and contribute to global account offboarding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain office technology, including printers, Zoom Rooms, and room schedulers, and own IT asset management with accurate, actionable equipment records&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain internal and user-facing technology documentation, and contribute to New Stripe onboarding and training materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote established IT best practices and escalate issues to the IT Systems and Infrastructure team as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have the ability to take initiative on tickets and contribute to project design and implementation. You are skilled at writing, updating and maintaining technical documentation and sending directed communications. You are comfortable working as an individual contributor on a global team that is driving towards a common goal. You will best succeed in this role by leading on things you are passionate about while supporting others in their passion.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You love problem solving and collaborating with others to provide world class support. Being the best fit for this position means you are both humble and confident. You strive towards excellence but understand your limitations and don’t hesitate to ask for help when needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have at least 2 years of experience delivering IT technical support or help desk services, with extensive expertise in Apple environments and software systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate comprehensive hands-on experience managing SaaS applications including Google Workspace, Slack, Zoom, Jira, and Confluence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess solid familiarity with automation scripts (Bash, Python, or Ruby) alongside endpoint management technologies like FleetDM and Apple DEP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exhibit the capability to work autonomously, effectively handling support inquiries while coordinating seamlessly with global cross-functional partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring exceptional written communication abilities to author clear IT guides, combined with a customer-centric mindset and strong collaborative spirit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Corporate Technology (CorpTech) Services team supports Stripes working in offices and remotely around the world. We keep critical business systems running and support onboarding, offboarding, and everyday technology needs.&amp;nbsp;We’re looking for a Tier 1 Support Engineer to join our Americas team, providing thoughtful, individualized, in-person support while collaborating with a global team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll resolve hardware, software, and business-system issues, maintain office technology, and support executives and high-stakes meetings. This role requires in-person support, including desk setups and equipment management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on support for executive devices, including macOS and iOS provisioning, configuration, secure migrations, and travel technology readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support high-stakes meetings and events through advance checks, active conferencing troubleshooting, and dedicated meeting-day technical support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage rapid incident response, containment playbooks, and dedicated ticket queues with tiered service-level agreements for sensitive executive requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve technical issues for Stripes, contingent workers, and vendors in person and through email, Slack, and the ticketing system; troubleshoot hardware, scripts, automation, and applications including Google Workspace, Slack, Zoom, Jira, and Confluence, and follow up to confirm resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provision laptops for onboarding and fleet upgrades, support onboarding training and third-party vendor setup, and contribute to global offboarding tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain office technology, including printers, Zoom Rooms, and room schedulers; manage desk setups, peripherals, and equipment inventory with accurate asset records&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain user-facing and internal technical documentation, promote established technology practices, and escalate issues to the IT Systems and Infrastructure team as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have the ability to take initiative on tickets and contribute to project design and implementation. You are skilled at writing, updating and maintaining technical documentation and sending directed communications. You are comfortable working as an individual contributor on a global team that is driving towards a common goal. You will best succeed in this role by leading on things you are passionate about while supporting others in their passion.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You love problem solving and collaborating with others to provide world class support. Being the best fit for this position means you are both humble and confident. You strive towards excellence but understand your limitations and don’t hesitate to ask for help when needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 2 years of experience in an IT help desk or technical support role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Apple hardware and software, Google Workspace, Slack, Zoom, and Atlassian tools, including Jira and Confluence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of script execution and troubleshooting using languages such as Ruby, Bash, or Python, and working knowledge of device provisioning and endpoint management tools such as DEP and FleetDM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently prioritize support requests and project work while collaborating with a global team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication, including technical documentation, and an empathetic, customer-focused approach to problem-solving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of executive IT support experience, including hands-on device support, high-stakes meeting support, and handling sensitive requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Manager on the Enterprise team at Stripe, you&#39;ll drive future growth at Stripe by building new relationships with prospective companies, turning them into happy Stripe users. You&#39;ll manage and elevate relationships with a named account list within a key vertical while identifying new growth opportunities and ways Stripe can exceed expectations. This role will be dedicated to accounts focused in Japan.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Enterprise Account Manager,, you will own a portfolio of established enterprise customers and drive their continued growth with Stripe. This is a hunting role within existing accounts: you will identify new opportunities to increase payment volume, activate additional products, expand Stripe’s footprint across business units and subsidiaries, and build long-term customer stickiness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will create and execute account strategies for complex technology customers, engaging both executive and technical stakeholders to understand their priorities and translate Stripe’s platform into clear commercial and operational value. The role spans the full expansion cycle, from account planning and opportunity creation through commercial negotiation, activation, and post-launch growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a commercially ambitious and highly autonomous seller who can balance near-term revenue delivery with the long-term relationship building required to grow a strategic book of business. You should be comfortable navigating technical and business conversations with leaders across the business.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a named portfolio of existing enterprise customers and develop strategic account plans to grow Stripe’s revenue, product adoption, and market share.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, create, and progress expansion opportunities across customer business units, subsidiaries, geographies, and product lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute outbound strategies within existing accounts to develop new executive relationships and create qualified opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the full expansion sales cycle, from opportunity identification and discovery through commercial negotiation, activation, go-live, and continued growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand customers’ complex business and technical challenges, and position Stripe’s core platform and products as solutions to those needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead product workshops, business case development, and financial analyses that help customers quantify the value of investing further in Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with internal teams including Product, Engineering, Partnerships, and Post-Sales to coordinate migrations, activations, and strategic customer initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of sales experience, with at least 2 years working with enterprise customers, preferably in a technology company, with a demonstrated record of exceeding commercial targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience growing and expanding existing upper-middle-market or enterprise customer relationships, including identifying new opportunities within a portfolio rather than relying solely on renewals or inbound demand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to develop and execute strategic account plans across complex organisations with multiple business units, stakeholders, or subsidiaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience leading complex, multi-stakeholder sales cycles from discovery through commercial negotiation, activation, go-live, and continued growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate complex technical capabilities into clear business value and engage confidently with senior business and technical stakeholders, including Product, Engineering, Finance, and executive leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a growth-stage internet or software company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech or payments is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business-level English proficiency is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a manager in this role, you will lead a team of high-performing Account Executives, primarily focused on acquiring and onboarding Stripe users in&lt;strong&gt; Japan&lt;/strong&gt;. You will help them develop their skills and deliver on ambitious targets, while also working directly with our prospects and early stage users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Sales Manager at Stripe, you will play an instrumental role in fueling Stripe’s growth through initiating, acquiring and ramping Stripe’s key SMB and Commercial prospects.&amp;nbsp; We are looking for a proactive leader who has demonstrated success dealing with ambiguity, operating in a high-growth environment, managing high-performing teams and solving problems with limited oversight. Ideal candidates will have experience managing a technology sales team, and possess first-class analytical, communication and relationship-building skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, develop and lead a team of Account Executives who focus on SMBs and Mid-market businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with senior leadership to develop the long-term vision and strategy for the team, and manage day-to-day operations with a focus on performance against key sales metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for acquiring and ramping prospective Stripe users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and guide the team in developing consultative and value-based sales skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire, motivate and enable development of team members to promote career growth and impact for Stripe&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively and cross-functionally across the organization to help shape Stripe’s products and solutions to meet customer needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play a personal and direct role in building customer relationships, up to C-level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re looking for someone who has:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant, revenue management experience, with at least 2+ years of people management experience or mentoring capacity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading sales in an early stage, high-growth technology environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to hire, train and coach a high-performance sales team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build relationships with strategic client and industry thought leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated passion for SMBs and Midmarket businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand and articulate technical concepts, and translate them into industry- or business-relevant terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience forecasting and managing a high growth commercial business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience running complex sales cycles, ideally with both smb and commercial size companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience leading a team in an office outside of the company headquarters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in the payments industry and/or fintech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

