&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Legal Entity Controller (Bangalore)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To further this important mission, we&#39;re building our Accounting team in Bangalore Finance and are looking for someone to help us scale for the future in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;End-to-end controllership for assigned legal entity(ies), including financial close, statutory reporting, audit readiness, regulatory filings, and adoption with the board or local management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preparation and sign-off of statutory financial statements and coordination of statutory adoption processes with local boards and directors and external advisors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage external auditors and local service providers, setting scope, driving timelines, resolving findings, and maintaining high-quality documentation for audits, reviews, and regulatory inspections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee monthly, quarterly, and year-end close, leading complex journal entries, reconciliations, technical accounting assessments, variance analysis, and executive reporting packages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design, implementation, and maintenance of entity-level accounting policies and internal control frameworks, and own SOX and internal control compliance and remediation where applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary business partner to Tax, Treasury, Legal, FP&amp;amp;A, and regional finance teams on transactions and policy changes that affect the entity&#39;s accounting, tax, and regulatory outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, prioritize, and deliver process improvements and automation initiatives that materially increase accuracy, speed, or scalability of entity accounting (RPA, ERP configuration, reporting pipelines, templates, or tooling)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve technical accounting questions and apply US GAAP, IFRS, and local GAAP judgment — escalate to central technical accounting teams when needed with well-formed recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide coaching and mentorship to more junior accounting teammates, and lead cross-functional projects and working groups to improve operating models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a subject-matter expert for entity-level reporting requests, internal and external audits, regulatory inquiries, and management escalations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional accountancy qualification (CA, ACA, ACCA, CIMA, or equivalent) with 9+ years of progressive accounting experience, including significant controllership exposure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on experience with monthly and year-end close, statutory financial statement preparation, external audits, regulatory filings, and variance analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of US GAAP and IFRS, and experience applying local GAAP and converging treatments across frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience owning internal control programs (SOX or similar) and executing control design and remediation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of delivering automation or process simplification at the entity level (ERP, reconciliation tooling, reporting pipeline improvements)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical and problem-solving skills, advanced Excel ability, and experience with financial systems (e.g., Oracle, Workiva, Blackline, or similar). Familiarity with SQL and BI tools or scripting is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management — ability to partner with Tax, Treasury, Legal, FP&amp;amp;A, and regional teams to drive timely, risk-mitigated outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High integrity, sound professional judgment, attention to detail, and the ability to operate under tight deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading or mentoring junior finance professionals and managing external advisors or service providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of (or experience in) the technology or payments industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oracle suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hubble and SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Growth Marketing is a team of performance-driven marketers and channel specialists. We partner closely with growth product, regional and demand marketing, and sales to drive revenue through self-serve and sales motions. We work globally, on the full customer lifecycle, and with all company segments - from startups to the largest enterprises. This role is focused on driving growth for Stripe Capital.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Capital provides access to fast, flexible financing to businesses, with the mission of helping them accelerate their growth. Businesses use the funds for marketing, hiring, geographic expansion, working capital, new equipment purchases, and much more. Capital has scaled meaningfully over the last few years, both in terms of user impact (over 81,000 businesses received financing through Stripe Capital in 2025 alone) as well as financial impact as a business line within Stripe. Over 95% of our users say they love using Capital, making us one of the most popular products at Stripe—and we&#39;re just getting started.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;As a Lifecycle Marketing Manager, you will be a key driver of global marketing efforts supporting our self-serve user acquisition motions to drive demand and revenue growth for Capital&lt;/em&gt;—&lt;em&gt;designing, implementing, and optimizing scaled, global lifecycle campaigns across user segments and life stages. You will help create uncommonly great email marketing campaigns and multi-channel experiences for Capital through a relentless focus on user experience and channel optimization.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive ideation, strategy, and execution of scaled lifecycle campaigns across email and in-product notifications to drive core business outcomes (e.g. new user acquisition, product activation, revenue), and test into and scale new channels (direct mail, push notifications, etc)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify customer needs, ideate solutions to improve user experience, and generate ongoing user-driven insights to inform campaign strategy and optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage marketing automation, behavioral data, and ML-based techniques to create personalized experiences at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze trends, develop actionable insights to optimize against targets, and socialize relevant learnings across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with key stakeholders across Growth, Product, Engineering, Data Science, Analytics, Sales, and Marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of work experience in a marketing role designing and launching multi-channel campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience analyzing and taking action on the performance of marketing campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience writing marketing briefs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience leveraging data, AI, and ML-driven techniques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of B2B marketing experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of email marketing, direct mail, and push notification experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Marketo, Salesforce, and/or Salesloft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in fintech on lending products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team brings Link’s brand and product stories to life through compelling, platform-native organic social content. Working closely with Brand, Creative, and agency partners, we turn strong ideas into high-quality storytelling that informs and engages audiences. The team also tests new creative approaches, uses performance and community insights to refine what works, and shares learnings across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brand extension into organic social&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Steward Link’s brand promise, brand voice and tone and creative standards for the organic social channels (in particular, Instagram, TikTok, and X); you&#39;re the internal authority on what on-brand looks like within the organic channel working in close partnership with our head of brand internally&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate Link’s broader brand positioning into social-specific strategies and briefing frameworks the agency can work from with clear guardrails&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and pressure-test agency-originated ideas for brand integrity before they get produced; catch what&#39;s off and redirect with specificity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our Head of Brand to ensure social is a genuine expression of brand health, a testing ground, and a helpful input to shape the evolution of our brand over time based on learnings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform Strategy &amp;amp; Channel Direction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve platform-specific strategies with clear rationale: which channels we&#39;re on, what role each plays, what &quot;winning&quot; looks and feels like on each&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring platform fluency to evaluate whether agency ideas are actually native to each channel, knowing the difference between a post that was adapted for TikTok and one that was built for it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the agency on format choices, creative approaches, and content types per platform; your direction should make their output sharper&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay ahead of platform shifts; be the internal authority on what&#39;s changing and what it means for our creative approach and channel mix&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agency Direction &amp;amp; Partnership Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the agency relationship day-to-day: brief quality, feedback quality, creative reviews, and the overall standard of the work coming out of the partnership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and refine briefs that give the agency enough strategic and creative direction to produce strong first drafts&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a review and feedback cadence that&#39;s efficient and that makes the agency&#39;s work measurably better over time; you&#39;re their best creative partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage agency output against brand standards, platform performance expectations, and business priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the stakeholder approval process.&amp;nbsp; Map who needs to weigh in at each stage, build the workflows that move content through Legal, Compliance, Brand, and leadership review without killing creative momentum, and get smarter about how to frame work to earn fast alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Editorial Oversight &amp;amp; Content Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the editorial calendar strategy — priorities, themes, moments, and content types — even when the agency is driving the calendar mechanics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and approve content before it publishes with a dual lens: is it on-brand and is it built to perform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Over time as the channel content matures, ensure the content mix reflects a coherent strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Community &amp;amp; Engagement Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the escalation layer: anything sensitive, high-stakes, or genuinely ambiguous comes to you before it goes out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surface community signals: what&#39;s resonating, what&#39;s creating friction, what people are actually asking and relay that back into Product, Comms, and CS as useful input&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance &amp;amp; Measurement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the measurement framework: define what matters, ensure dashboards exist, and deliver performance reviews to marketing leadership that connect social activity to brand and business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate agency performance reporting and help refine as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use performance data to sharpen briefs and strategic direction; close the loop between what we’ve learned and what the agency is asked to do differently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Integration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate organic social into launch plans from Day 1 alongside Product Marketing and Brand Marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with PR/Comms on earned media, crisis response, and executive social presence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Legal and Compliance on content approval frameworks; keep the agency informed Stakeholder Alignment &amp;amp; Approval&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a stakeholder map: who has approval authority, who has input rights, and what the right sequencing looks like for different content types and risk levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design approval workflows that move fast without cutting corners.&amp;nbsp; The goal is fewer revision cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the judgment and relationships to pre-align key stakeholders before formal review so approvals confirm, not derail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frame content for internal audiences as skillfully as for external ones.&amp;nbsp; Know how to present creative work in a way that earns confidence and moves decisions forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the agency’s guide through Link’s internal process; protect them from last-minute redirects by front-loading alignment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong candidates will have depth on both sides of brand and channel expertise&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brand Experience (non-negotiable)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7 years of experience that includes meaningful time working in or alongside brand strategy. You&#39;ve been in the room where brand positioning decisions get made and have developed real opinions about what brands stand for and why&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve stewarded a brand voice across contexts, partners, and platforms, including directing external partners to express it faithfully&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can evaluate creative work against a brand standard with precision, not just instinct and give feedback that actually improves the work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand how organic social contributes to brand health over time and can make that case internally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Channel Expertise (non-negotiable)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep platform literacy across Instagram, TikTok, X; you know each platform&#39;s mechanics, audience behavior, and content dynamics well enough to evaluate work made for them&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve owned or directed organic social at a channel level and understand what genuinely native content looks like versus content that was adapted and shows it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong short-form video instincts: you can evaluate, redirect, and improve video concepts and executions with confidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical fluency: you can read performance data, ask good questions about it, and use it to drive better creative decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agency &amp;amp; Creative Direction Experience (critical for this role)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve managed an agency or external creative partner in a senior capacity — you know how to write a brief that unlocks good work, run a review that improves it, and hold a partner accountable without micromanaging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve navigated the dynamic of an agency bringing ideas to an internal team: you know when to push back, when to build on, when to redirect entirely, and how to do all of that in a way that keeps the partnership productive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your feedback makes work better — you can articulate what&#39;s wrong and point toward what&#39;s right with enough specificity to be useful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Also Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Legal/Compliance on regulated or high-scrutiny content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaborator, particularly with Brand, Comms, and Product Marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent writer: briefs, feedback,Demonstrated ability to navigate complex internal approval processes.&amp;nbsp; You’ve worked in environments with multiple stakeholders (Legal, Brand, Comms, leadership) and know how to build the relationships and workflows that get good work approved without grinding to a halt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong Plus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building creator or ambassador programs (and directing an agency to support them)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social listening platform fluency (Brandwatch, Sprinklr, Sprout Social, or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI content tools for evaluating, prompting, and directing AI-assisted production from an agency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a fintech, payments, or consumer brand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing to early-adopter audiences and/or in the agentic technology space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Growth Platform builds the machine learning systems that help businesses discover and use the Stripe products that meet their needs. Our recommendations reach users across the Dashboard, email, onboarding, documentation, and AI agent interfaces. We combine an understanding of each business with models that decide which recommendation is useful, when to show it, and how to learn from the outcome.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work spans recommendation and ranking models, contextual bandits, agent-based recommendations, and the data and evaluation systems behind them. We build shared capabilities that product, marketing, and sales teams can use across Stripe. Success means helping businesses take useful actions and adopt products that help them grow, while keeping recommendations relevant and avoiding unnecessary messages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build and operate production ML systems that improve how Stripe recommends products, content, and next steps to businesses. You will own work from problem definition and feature development through training, evaluation, deployment, monitoring, and iteration. Working with data scientists, engineers, and product partners, you will turn model improvements into measurable user and business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, train, evaluate, deploy, and maintain models for recommendation, ranking, and personalized action selection across Growth Platform surfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve contextual bandit and policy-learning approaches, including exploration, reward design, and how recommendations adapt to user context and feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build agent-based recommendation capabilities that use business context to identify relevant products and integration options, with evaluations that test recommendation quality and usefulness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop reliable data and feature pipelines for training and inference. Improve data freshness, feature quality, and consistency between training and production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reusable tooling for model evaluation, retraining, and safe rollout so the team can test and ship improvements faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the quality and operation of the team&#39;s ML components: write tested production code, monitor models and pipelines, investigate failures, and improve reliability, latency, and cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and analyze online experiments with data science partners. Connect offline evaluation to product adoption and incremental impact, with guardrails for dismissals, unsubscribes, and user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product engineering to integrate models into recommendation delivery systems, and with ML infrastructure teams to use and improve Stripe&#39;s shared training, feature, and serving capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with product, marketing, and sales partners to identify problems that shared ML capabilities can solve, and make practical choices about where modeling adds value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a machine learning engineer with a builder mindset. You care about the business problem, the quality of the model, and what happens after it ships. You can move between modeling and software engineering, make practical tradeoffs, and take ownership of an ambiguous problem through production and measurement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of industry experience in machine learning engineering, software engineering, or applied data science, with hands-on experience building and shipping ML models in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills in Python and experience writing maintainable, tested production code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience designing, training, and evaluating ML models using frameworks such as PyTorch, TensorFlow, XGBoost, or scikit-learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building data or feature pipelines, proficiency in SQL, and familiarity with distributed data processing tools such as Spark or PySpark.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong understanding of statistics, model evaluation, and experimentation, including the ability to recognize data leakage and distinguish offline model improvements from business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience deploying, monitoring, and debugging production ML systems, and evaluating tradeoffs among model quality, reliability, latency, and cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to turn an open-ended business problem into a technical approach and collaborate effectively with engineering, data science, product, and business partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with recommendation systems, ranking, personalization, or marketplace and advertising optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with contextual bandits, policy learning, causal inference, or off-policy evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and evaluating LLM applications, including structured extraction, embeddings, or recommendations grounded in user and business context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building reusable ML capabilities used by multiple products or teams, including training automation, feature systems, or model monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with product growth, lifecycle messaging, or systems that balance short-term engagement with longer-term user outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Link is a digital wallet designed for fast and secure online payments. It allows consumers to save and use their preferred payment methods across the Link network, helping them check out quickly and securely wherever Link is accepted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Link Fraud and Auth team works to make Link the most trusted and highest-performing way to pay. We protect consumers and merchants from fraud, abuse, and financial loss while maximizing authorization rates for good users. Our work spans consumer-facing experiences, payment infrastructure, and ML powered risk systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We manage fraud and financial risk across a growing range of novel Link features, including Link’s agentic wallet, stored balance, and LPMs. The team also owns Instant Bank Payments, a proprietary payment method built on ACH rails, offering merchants immediate confirmation while protecting them from bank-initiated returns. IBP is the heart of Link’s revenue engine, giving LFA engineers the opportunity to shape and scale one of Link’s most important products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a machine learning engineer on Link Fraud and Auth, you’ll build and operate models and risk decisioning systems that protect Link while helping more legitimate payments succeed. You’ll work across the full machine learning lifecycle, from analyzing fraud patterns and identifying opportunities to building, deploying, monitoring, and improving models in production. You’ll use data to form hypotheses, make practical modeling choices, and define technical direction in partnership with Engineering, Product, and Data Science. Your work will directly influence Link’s fraud performance, authorization rates, and ability to expand into new products and payment experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, train, evaluate, deploy, and own machine learning models that detect fraud and abuse across Link.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use large-scale datasets to investigate emerging threats, develop hypotheses, and identify opportunities to improve payment performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop pragmatic machine learning solutions, including tree-based models and other approaches suited to real-time risk decisioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design data pipelines, features, evaluation methods, experiments, and monitoring systems that support reliable production models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and improve risk decisioning systems that integrate with other parts of Stripe’s payments stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own ambiguous problems from initial analysis and problem definition through technical design, implementation, launch, measurement, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Engineering, Product, Data Science, and Risk partners across Stripe to turn model improvements into durable product outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of industry experience building and shipping machine learning models in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills in Python and experience with common data and machine learning tools, such as SQL, Spark, and XGBoost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of production machine learning systems, including data pipelines, feature development, model evaluation, deployment, monitoring, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with large and complex datasets and applying data analysis, statistics, and experimentation fundamentals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to take an open-ended business problem, determine where machine learning can help, and own the solution through production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment in selecting practical modeling approaches and evaluating tradeoffs among model performance, system complexity, latency, and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills and the ability to work across teams and contribute to peers&#39; success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying machine learning to fraud detection, risk modeling, payment authorization, identity, account security, or another adversarial domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building real-time, low-latency machine learning or risk decisioning systems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating models into production services and designing reliable systems around model outputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payments, fintech, digital wallets, or money movement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software engineering skills and experience designing solutions across the machine learning and product stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Radar ML team builds the machine learning systems that power Stripe’s Radar fraud and abuse product suite. Our models make real-time decisions across a significant share of internet commerce - helping businesses stop fraud, increase authorization, and grow safely. By turning economy-scale datasets into compelling ML products, the team directly improves customer outcomes and drives meaningful revenue for Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is growing, and expanding into multiple new areas. We are building abuse protections across the full customer life-cycle, adaptive and customizable fraud systems for enterprises, and risk intelligence for 50+ global payment methods.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own ML problems from conception to production: analyzing new fraud and abuse patterns, exploring large-scale datasets, experimenting with model architectures, designing evaluations, deploying models, and monitoring performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your work may include developing transformer architectures for payment data, building graph-powered intelligence across consumers, leveraging LLMs to detect emerging attacks, or rapidly prototyping new protections with frontier AI labs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have opportunities to ship 0→1 products, and to improve mission-critical ML models operating at Stripe scale.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, train, evaluate, and deploy models that detect fraud and abuse across Stripe’s global network.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate emerging fraud and abuse patterns, identify where ML can help, and rapidly develop effective solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design features, datasets, evaluation methods, and experiments for noisy, delayed, and adversarial environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve model architectures, training methods, and production systems to increase model quality, coverage, and adaptability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor production behavior and improve models as data, customer needs, and attack patterns change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance model quality with legitimate-user impact, latency, reliability, and operational complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering, product, data science, risk experts, and leading Stripe users to turn modeling improvements into differentiated Radar products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to reusable tools and AI-assisted workflows that help the team develop and operate ML systems more effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a fast, pragmatic problem solver with deep ML expertise and a bias toward action. You are excited to work at the frontier of payments and AI - turning advances in machine learning into production systems that address new forms of fraud and abuse. You’ve built ML models and shepherded them to production, landing impact for users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience developing, evaluating, and deploying machine learning models in a production environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong foundations in machine learning, data analysis, statistics, model evaluation, and experiment design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming and software-engineering skills, with experience writing tested, maintainable code for production ML applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or operating production ML systems, including one or more of large-scale data and feature pipelines, distributed model training, low-latency inference, model deployment, or production monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to investigate ambiguous problems, reason from data, and choose pragmatic technical approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate technical ideas and results clearly and collaborate effectively across disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning an ML problem across the full lifecycle, from problem framing and data exploration through deployment, monitoring, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing or productionizing modern deep learning, graph-learning, or LLM-based approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and optimizing real-time, low-latency ML systems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying ML to fraud detection, integrity, trust and safety, identity, cybersecurity, or another adversarial domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience rapidly building 0→1 products, working directly with customers, or operating effectively in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active interest in the latest ML developments, and how they can be leveraged to solve business problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Transaction Risk team builds the machine learning systems behind Stripe Radar, helping businesses prevent fraud and abuse while letting legitimate customers through. We combine intelligence from across Stripe’s global network with real-time models and AI agents to protect businesses across the customer lifecycle, from signup and free trials to payments and ongoing usage, with a growing focus on the emerging threats facing AI companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is growing, and expanding into multiple new areas. We are building abuse protections across the full customer life-cycle and solving emerging token fraud problems to make Stripe the default fraud and abuse solution for AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own major ML systems and initiatives from problem definition to production. You&#39;ll find where ML can make the biggest difference, design the approach, build and ship models and the systems around them, and keep improving them as data, users, and attackers change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your work may include protecting businesses from abuse across the customer lifecycle, building adaptive and customizable fraud systems for Stripe&#39;s largest users, or extending risk intelligence to 50+ global payment methods. Across all of these, you&#39;ll use modern approaches, such as transformer models over payment data, graph intelligence across consumers, and LLMs that detect emerging attacks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have opportunities to ship 0→1 products, and to improve mission-critical ML models operating at Stripe scale, often driving several efforts in parallel and setting the technical bar for the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design and delivery of ML projects end to end, from framing the problem and sizing the opportunity through deployment, monitoring, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, train, evaluate, and deploy models that detect fraud and abuse across Stripe’s global network, and own the production systems they run on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate emerging fraud and abuse patterns, decide where ML can have the most impact, and quickly turn those insights into shipped protections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design features, datasets, and evaluation strategies for noisy, delayed, and adversarial environments, and set the bar for experimental rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sound architecture and modeling tradeoffs between model quality, legitimate-user impact, latency, reliability, and operational cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the go-to expert for the systems you own: lead incident response for model regressions, reduce operational toil, and make your systems easy for others to build on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering, product, data science, risk experts, and leading Stripe users to turn modeling improvements into differentiated Radar products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn recurring problems into reusable components, tools, and AI-assisted workflows that speed up the whole team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers, give thoughtful design and code reviews, and help new teammates ramp up quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an experienced ML engineer who combines deep modeling expertise with strong engineering judgment. You&#39;ve owned ML systems in production, shipped multiple meaningful improvements, and made the people around you more effective. You move fast without breaking things, you&#39;re comfortable leading through ambiguity, and you&#39;re excited to work at the frontier of payments and AI, turning advances in machine learning into production systems that address new forms of fraud and abuse.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience developing, evaluating, and deploying machine learning models in a production environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of leading ML projects from problem definition to production, with measurable impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep foundations in machine learning, statistics, model evaluation, and experiment design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming and software-engineering skills, with experience writing tested, maintainable code for production ML applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and operating production ML systems, including several of: large-scale data and feature pipelines, distributed model training, low-latency inference, model deployment, or production monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring engineers or technically leading projects with multiple contributors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to investigate ambiguous problems, reason from data, and choose pragmatic technical approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate technical ideas and results clearly and collaborate effectively across disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying ML to fraud detection, integrity, trust and safety, identity, cybersecurity, or another adversarial domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing or productionizing modern deep learning, graph-learning, or LLM-based approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and optimizing real-time, low-latency ML systems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning the operational health of critical ML systems, including on-call, incident response, and migrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience rapidly building 0→1 products or working directly with customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building AI-assisted tooling or agents that measurably increased a team&#39;s velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;The Stripe Accounting Team is responsible for supporting all products at Stripe, consulting on accounting implications, and supporting teams&#39; ability to make informed strategic decisions. We are responsible for the accurate and timely recording of all business-generated transactions on our balance sheet and income statement. We operate in a fast-paced environment and collaborate significantly with cross-functional and international teams.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an M&amp;amp;A/Integration Accounting leader to own cross-functional accounting integration strategy and execution. In this role, you will lead complex integration initiatives, establish policy alignment, oversee business combination accounting (including technical valuations), and serve as the accounting authority for Stripe’s strategic investment portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a controllership/oversight function over subsidiaries until they are integrated into the broader Stripe teams/systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Corporate Development, Tax, Corporate Legal, Finance &amp;amp; Strategy, and external service providers for diligence and integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate and influence unintegrated teams to align with Stripe policies, procedures, and norms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the directly responsible individual ensuring timely and accurate reporting of unintegrated subsidiaries/businesses, and strategic investments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the evolution of our financial close and reporting programs by implementing leading practices, efficiency opportunities, and internal controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own program management of finance integration workstreams end-to-end. Build the plan, sequence dependencies, track functional commitments, surface risks early, and drive decisions to closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope and lead complex, cross functional projects and process improvements spanning multiple teams to find long term and scalable solutions which effectively integrate into Stripe’s systems and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and perform monthly and quarterly close activities, including balance sheet reconciliations, variance analyses and analytical reviews, producing internal management reporting and external audit support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research, prepare, and review technical accounting analyses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Stripe-approved AI tools (and create your own) to accelerate and improve your work. This is an immediate expectation, not an aspiration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of relevant public accounting and/or industry experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant M&amp;amp;A integration experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.A. or B.S degree in Accounting or Finance (CPA strongly preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in U.S. GAAP and ability to research complex accounting issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and organizational skills, both written and verbal, with the ability to convey financial concepts to both financial and non-financial audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and experience working with large data sets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience partnering with cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with internal controls (design, implementation and execution)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated history of taking on various types of challenging projects and producing results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solution-oriented mindset with enthusiasm for establishing best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage multiple complex projects simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPA or similar qualification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a public company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payments or Tech industry experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Competitive Programs team, which is part of the Go-to-Market (GTM) Strategic Programs team, is a new team dedicated to establishing and scaling Stripe’s Competitive Programs capability. Stripe operates in a dynamic and evolving competitive landscape. This role will help Stripe understand market developments and translate competitive insights into actionable guidance for teams and users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In partnership with Market Intelligence, you will identify meaningful threats and opportunities early, mobilize cross-functional action, and turn market and deal signals into better Product, Marketing, and GTM decisions. You will own the competitive operating system: program design, cross-functional coordination, deal triage and routing, visibility, and accountability. Product, Sales, PMM, Pricing, and other functions retain ownership for decisions and delivery in their domains.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a player-coach role: you will build the team, lead the most complex programs, and apply the same skills to other high-priority GTM programs as business needs evolve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead and develop a team of program managers that helps Stripe compete more effectively in its highest-priority situations. You will turn an emerging capability into a durable operating model: set team goals and work plans, prioritize scarce capacity with Stripe leadership and Market Intelligence, and ensure centrally staffed competitor programs are measurable and connected to the functional teams that own decisions and delivery.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-ambiguity management role. You will partner with senior leaders across Sales, Product, Product Operations, Marketing, Market Intelligence, Pricing, Finance &amp;amp; Strategy, and GTM Operations to turn unclear competitive problems into focused programs with clear objectives, owners, decision forums, operating cadences, and measures of success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Initially, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop the Competitive Programs team, setting objectives, allocating work, and maintaining a high bar for judgment, execution, and stakeholder management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish the P0/P1 portfolio and operating model with Market Intelligence and GTM Strategic Programs leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personally lead the highest-complexity programs and build the playbooks, escalation paths, and operating mechanisms that enable faster, more coordinated responses without centralizing functional decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the team’s SOKRs, portfolio priorities in partnership with Stripe leadership, work plans, and success measures; allocate program-management capacity across the highest-priority competitive needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, coach and retain a high-performing team of program managers who can operate independently in ambiguous, high-stakes environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly lead—and coach program managers to lead—the design, launch, and lifecycle of centrally staffed P0 and P1 competitor programs, including recommendations to continue, adjust, graduate, or re-elevate programs as the market changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and continuously improve the program-management layer of Stripe’s competitive operating system, including playbooks, program standards, decision logs, operating reviews, escalation mechanisms, and executive reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Market Intelligence to translate competitive, customer, and deal signals into prioritized actions; ensure Product, PMM, Sales, Pricing, Product S&amp;amp;O, and other functional partners have clear accountable owners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create decision-oriented updates for senior leadership on program health, competitive risks, outcomes, capacity needs, and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead select cultural initiatives, surface systemic friction, and ensure the appropriate functional teams own durable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply the team’s program-design and execution capabilities to other strategic GTM priorities as business needs evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You are a strategic, hands-on people leader who is energized by ambiguous, cross-functional business problems. You set direction without waiting for perfect information, move fluidly between executive strategy and program detail, and maintain the operational rigor needed to deliver durable results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You help senior leaders make trade-offs while ensuring programs have clear owners, milestones, decisions, and success measures. You build trust across functions, name risks directly, resolve ambiguity, and hold partners accountable to commitments. You are excited by the intersection of market dynamics, product and commercial strategy, GTM execution, and organizational change—and understand that Competitive Programs makes Stripe faster and more coordinated without replacing functional ownership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;9+ years of experience in program management, business operations, GTM strategy, management consulting, or a related discipline, including experience in a commercial organization such as Sales, Marketing, Product, or GTM Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2+ years of people-management experience, including setting objectives, allocating work, coaching experienced ICs, and managing performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success leading complex, global, cross-functional programs from problem definition through implementation, adoption, and durable operational handoff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A player-coach mindset: high ownership, sound judgment, adaptability under pressure, and a collaborative, hands-on approach that sets a high bar for quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience establishing goals, work plans, operating cadences, decision forums, and success measures for initiatives spanning regions, segments, product lines, and multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment in prioritizing competing demands and allocating limited team capacity to the highest-value work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to navigate senior stakeholders with differing incentives and decision rights; drive alignment while making trade-offs and escalation paths explicit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to structure qualitative and quantitative inputs into clear recommendations, assess program health and risk, and guide prioritization with data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive communication skills, including facilitation of senior working sessions and decision-oriented reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing competitive programs, strategic-account programs, product-launch programs, commercial transformation, or other high-stakes GTM initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a new operating model, program-management team, or repeatable playbook from the ground up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering closely with Product, Product Operations, PMM, Sales, Pricing, Finance &amp;amp; Strategy, Market Intelligence, and GTM Systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with competitive intelligence, win/loss analysis, sales enablement, pricing, commercial strategy, product-feedback mechanisms, or executive account programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a B2B technology, enterprise software, fintech, payments, or platform company; comfort using SQL, BI tools, or similar methods to analyze pipeline, adoption, revenue, and operational data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our users are the heart of our business. Stripe’s Global Customer Success Team is responsible for managing our largest and most strategic relationships, such as Doordash, Lyft, and Shopify. In this manager role you’ll be responsible for a high-performing team of Customer Success Managers. You’ll lead and coach the team, helping them deliver on ambitious targets, roll up your sleeves to work directly with executives at existing enterprise Stripe customers and partner cross functionally to help users execute their business priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a hands-on, visionary leader who has demonstrated success dealing with ambiguity, operating in a high-growth environment, and solving complicated problems with limited oversight. Ideal candidates will have management and leadership experience scaling a technology Customer Success team, superior communication skills, and a track record for building trusted relationships with senior stakeholders and understanding unique customer needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Manager to lead a team of high-performing Customer Success Managers to build and grow the relationships with our most complex users. You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, develop, and lead a team of Customer Success Managers supporting strategic, relationship-based accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help drive an engagement model focused on building durable user relationships, increasing adoption, delivering value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop both the vision and strategy for the team, driving progress toward customer health, renewal and growth metrics&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for identifying risks and opportunities early, and helping the team build and work through mitigation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach, mentor, and guide the team in developing consultative customer success and sales skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Stripe’s solutions to meet client needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong operating rhythms for the team, including account planning, health reviews, renewal forecasting and business reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire, motivate, and enable the team by setting clear expectations, providing direct feedback and supporting their individual development and career growth.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re looking for someone who has:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of customer-facing experience in customer success, account management, or sales with 5 years of people management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payments or Fintech experience and/or experience in a complex SaaS consumption environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading sales or account management in a high-growth technology environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to hire, train, and coach a high-performing user-facing team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to support the Customer Success Managers’ efforts through strategic advice on account strategies, and serving as executive sponsor with key relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate in a high-growth environment and work through ambiguity to solve complex customer and business problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated passion for Stripe’s mission, and helping users succeed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a high-growth stage Internet/software company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

