&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Financial Crimes Operations team helps protect Stripe’s financial ecosystem while supporting legitimate businesses. We conduct risk-based reviews and investigations, applying sound judgment and operational rigor to identify and mitigate financial crime risks. We collaborate across Operations, Compliance, Risk, Product, and Engineering to build effective, scalable processes and support compliance with applicable requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Financial Crimes Operations Manager, you’ll lead and develop a team conducting complex financial crime reviews. You’ll own day-to-day team performance, help investigators navigate ambiguous cases, and build a culture of sound judgment, accountability, and continuous improvement. Working with cross-functional partners, you’ll strengthen review quality, improve workflows, and help the team scale while balancing risk, efficiency, and user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop a team of investigators through regular feedback, performance conversations, and career development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage daily operations, including workload prioritization, queue health, and capacity planning, to meet quality and service-level expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the team through complex and ambiguous reviews, ensuring risk assessments and recommendations are well-supported, clearly documented, and appropriately escalated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reinforce consistent application of policies and procedures, partnering with relevant stakeholders to resolve questions and address gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use operational data to identify trends, understand performance drivers, and take action on quality, productivity, and turnaround times.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with quality and training teams to address recurring errors, strengthen investigative skills, and improve onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Compliance, Risk, Product, Engineering, and other Operations teams to resolve issues and improve review processes and tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to simplify workflows and introduce automation while maintaining appropriate controls and human judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate changing business priorities and requirements into clear team goals and actionable operating plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster an inclusive team environment where people raise concerns, learn from mistakes, and take ownership of outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in financial crime operations, customer due diligence, anti-money laundering investigations, or a closely related risk function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience directly managing an operations team, including coaching, performance management, and employee development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A working understanding of risk-based reviews, including assessing business models, ownership structures, customer activity, and relevant financial crime risk indicators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage operational delivery against quality, productivity, and service-level expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical judgment, with the ability to evaluate incomplete or conflicting information and recognize when to escalate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain complex findings and provide actionable feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using spreadsheets, reporting tools, or operational dashboards to diagnose problems and guide decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize competing demands, lead through change, and collaborate effectively across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading complex financial crime investigations or risk review teams in a payments, fintech, or financial services environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reviewing higher-risk businesses or complex ownership structures across multiple markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience improving investigative workflows, quality frameworks, training programs, or case-management tools.&lt;/li&gt;
