&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Policy team works to understand and shape the regulatory and political environment in which Stripe operates — advising on product and business strategy, developing Stripe&#39;s policy positions, and engaging with policymakers and regulators around the world. The Policy Development &amp;amp; Strategy team sits at the center of this work, connecting Policy to Stripe&#39;s product and business teams and ensuring the company can pursue a proactive, coordinated policy agenda.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Millions of businesses use Stripe as a core platform to build and grow their own businesses, and increasingly that means building with AI. As AI becomes central to how businesses are built and run, this raises new questions: how infrastructure for AI should operate, what responsibilities sit at the infrastructure layer, and how to keep that infrastructure open, secure, and trusted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a public policy professional to define Stripe’s approach to these questions and carry it into the world. In this role, you will develop Stripe’s positions on the public policy issues raised by AI infrastructure and help set the principles behind how Stripe’s AI platforms are governed, including trust, safety, and supportability. You will engage policymakers, regulators, industry groups, civil society, and other partners on these issues, in partnership with Stripe’s Government Relations team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The right person will be equally comfortable working through a hard policy question with Product and Legal teams, briefing senior leaders, and representing Stripe&#39;s position with regulators or industry coalitions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop Stripe&#39;s policy strategy for AI infrastructure. &lt;/strong&gt;Identify existing and emerging public policy issues and develop substantive positions and priorities that advance Stripe’s interests and reflect our values.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape platform policy principles. &lt;/strong&gt;Work with the cross-functional teams that own day-to-day enforcement to set the principles and frameworks behind platform governance, acceptable use, model listing, and escalation, while preserving the benefits of neutral and open infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive cross-functional alignment. &lt;/strong&gt;Bring Product, Legal, Comms, Risk, Operations, and Government Relations to shared positions and priorities, and advance work from open question to decision to external execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advise the business on difficult policy choices. &lt;/strong&gt;Identify emerging risks and opportunities, translate external policy developments into product and business-model implications, and make recommendations on launches, supportability questions, public commitments, and other high-stakes decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop Stripe&#39;s external policy positions. &lt;/strong&gt;Turn internal policy work into external policy positions on AI infrastructure regulation in the US and globally: US AI policy at the federal and state level, national-security and export-control regimes, the EU AI Act, and emerging rules and standards for AI intermediaries and providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engage externally on the substance. &lt;/strong&gt;Engage policymakers, regulators, national security agencies, industry groups, standards bodies, academics, civil society, and other stakeholders to understand and anticipate policy developments; help build relationships and coalitions; and work with the Government Relations team to proactively shape policy debates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead proactive public-policy initiatives and partnerships. &lt;/strong&gt;Identify opportunities for Stripe to convene stakeholders, support research, develop industry frameworks, or partner with external organizations on difficult AI-governance and trust-and-safety questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop narratives and executive materials. &lt;/strong&gt;Produce data-driven policy briefs, consultation responses, talking points, presentations, and executive communications that use Stripe’s data to turn technically and legally complex questions into clear positions for internal and external audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in public policy, platform policy, trust and safety, technology policy, government, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong policy judgment and a track record of developing positions on complex, contested issues where the legal or regulatory answer is not obvious.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meaningful familiarity with trust and safety, platform governance, or online-service policy, including how policy choices translate into product and operational decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong public-policy instincts and experience engaging policymakers, regulators, industry groups, or other external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI policy and governance, and the range to engage credibly on fast-moving technical and regulatory questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to drive cross-functional work across Product, Legal, Operations, Comms, and business teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication, including the ability to produce concise policy analysis and represent a position credibly with senior internal and external audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ambiguity and a bias toward building: this role will often require creating a position, framework, or external strategy where none exists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience at a technology or AI company, government agency, think tank, or civil-society organization working on AI, platform governance, trust and safety, or technology policy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with national-security, export-control, or cybersecurity policy; familiarity with payments or internet infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;JD, MPP, or equivalent advanced degree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Stripe, you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach. Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;careers-listing-details__body&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;hds-text careers-listing-details__body-content hds-text--md hds-text--soft&quot;&gt;
&lt;article&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Specialist Solutions Architects (SSA) are domain experts aligned to specific Stripe solutions and customer buying centers. We have in-depth knowledge of specific solution offerings and a deep understanding of customer challenges. We align with specialist product sellers on deals, advise the broader pre-sales team on complex opportunities, support pipeline development and revenue attainment, serve as an advisor on go-to-market sales plays, and provide critical insights to our product and engineering teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/article&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Specialist Solution Architect, you will lead in-depth product discussions with our top users and prospects and execute against our go-to-market strategy for our Money Management products, including Stripe Capital, Issuing, Treasury, and our global Payouts suite. You will educate our product and engineering teams on market trends and strongly influence the product roadmap for the Money Management product suite at Stripe, helping us become the primary way merchants run their businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a subject matter expert on Stripe’s Money Management products (including Capital, Issuing, Treasury, and our global Payouts suite) to accelerate opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate a deep understanding of embedded finance applications that leverage Stripe’s products, articulating how they combine to create a compounding platform for our users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consult with users on a broad range of embedded finance use cases, from charge card programs and global payouts to a comprehensive suite of financing options including revenue-based financing, loans, and lines of credit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the compliance requirements of solutions built with Stripe products, especially as we expand our offerings into new markets and use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, share, and learn best practices and reusable assets with the broader GTM organization to enhance the quality and efficiency of the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create reference architectures to uplevel the team and refine reference solutions based on product enhancements and feedback from customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the Money Management product sales team and be an active part of the opportunity team for Stripe’s largest customers to lead strategy and own key relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a “Voice of the Customer” internally, providing actionable insights to product stakeholders to influence the Money Management product roadmap and feature prioritization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide critical insights on emerging technologies, including the application of stablecoins for money movement, lending, and global financial access, to influence the product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply understand the sales process for the product and provide the Sales team with tools and training to qualify potential leads, including simplifying our distribution for faster onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on competitive analysis and market differentiation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support marketing events including executive briefings, conferences, user groups, and trade shows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in a technical sales, pre-sales, or solutions architecture role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of product experience with embedded finance solutions, such as card issuing, lending, or treasury management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with integrating RESTful APIs into web applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills, comfortable explaining complex concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for learning and researching current and emerging products to develop innovative solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to build strong collaborative working relationships with business partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to deal effectively with ambiguity and thrive in an unstructured, fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of software engineering and architecture patterns, with the ability to understand how a wide variety of technologies and systems interact with each other&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience enabling and scaling a GTM team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in systems design, with a background building and deploying complex applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Finance Operations (FinOps) team is Stripe’s global backbone, dedicated to delivering and continuously improving essential business services - billing and collections, procurement, monetization, payroll, and travel and expenses. We drive company value through data-driven insights, operational rigor, and a relentless focus on excellence. As strategic partners, we shape business decisions, champion technology-enabled solutions, own operational strategy, and collaborate across global functions to enable Stripe’s growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Monetization Services Specialist - Pricing Activation to join our growing team. This individual will help us improve user experience through accurate and timely onboarding of contracts, workflows and deliver improvements in our integrated financial systems with business partners, financial colleagues, and engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own accurate and timely activation of sold custom pricing contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the pricing activation of custom pricing contracts in Stripe’s billing systems, from intake and requirements validation through configuration and post-activation checks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate legal terms including approved pricing, product, invoicing, and effective-date terms into accurate billing configurations; identify and escalate ambiguous or conflicting terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform quality-control and reconciliation checks to confirm that configurations produce the expected billing outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal systems, deal desk, legal, sales ops, internal audit, go-to-market, engineer and account managers to develop and improve operational processes and programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with sales to investigate and resolve user inquiries related to onboarding and rate discrepancy issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze our processes and instigate changes to help scale our operations and improve user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with other Stripe teams to assist with system implementations for billings, collections, and assist with internal and external ad-hoc audit support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help scale and optimize our processes by assisting with the execution of key projects and programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain unique insights into how businesses of varying sizes and industries operate and scale on Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can quickly learn the Stripe ways of working and make a real impact through process enhancements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a part of building a brand-new team and operational culture for Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to or act as DRI for with monthly and quarterly flux analysis of key metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to or act as DRI for ad hoc projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4-5&amp;nbsp; years of relevant financial operations/pricing activation experience or 4+ years of strong customer service experience with a degree in Business Administration, Finance, Tech, or relevant field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and organizational skills, both written and verbal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills and demonstrated ability to work independently, analyze problems and data sets to make complex investigation decisions&lt;/li&gt;
