&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our EMEA Marketing team is a dynamic, fast-growing group that loves turning customers into enthusiastic Stripe advocates. We work hand-in-hand with our Sales team to build demand, help users get the most out of our products, and craft marketing plans that truly resonate with local audiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a lot still to build, and we’re tackling it as a diverse, international team that thrives on collaboration, bold innovation, and genuine curiosity. If you love to learn and want to make a meaningful impact, we’d love to have you join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior individual contributor, you’ll align regional and global marketing teams around shared priorities for EMEA Velocity, secure investment to deliver them, and balance global strategy with regional needs. You’ll directly lead high-priority initiatives across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll shape how Stripe grows its Velocity segment across EMEA, with a particular focus on winning and expanding relationships with priority commercial accounts. You’ll combine regional strategy with hands-on field marketing, building programs that generate demand and accelerate pipeline across different markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the primary marketing partner on the EMEA Velocity leadership team, you’ll own the regional marketing strategy and investment plan. You’ll work closely with Sales leadership to identify the biggest opportunities across markets, decide where marketing can make the greatest difference, and turn those priorities into measurable business results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll lead account-based programs, executive engagement, and market-relevant campaigns for priority commercial accounts, bringing together regional and global teams to deliver them. Your programs will engage senior decision makers and operational leaders on reducing developer complexity, improving conversion, and increasing the return on their financial infrastructure. You’ll also partner with Demand Generation on scaled digital demand campaigns and programs, connecting those efforts with regional business priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior individual contributor, you’ll lead through influence across markets and teams, aligning Sales, Demand Generation, Product Marketing, and Global Campaigns around a shared plan. You’ll balance regional priorities with local customer needs, use results to guide investment, and build approaches that can scale across EMEA. You’ll help shape the marketing approach and directly lead the initiatives where regional context and ownership matter most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own the integrated marketing strategy for the Velocity segment across EMEA, turning business goals, market dynamics, customer needs, and competitors into clear priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with regional Sales and Sales Development (SDR) leadership to set shared priorities, take part in pipeline reviews, and steer marketing investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build full-funnel campaigns around the problems businesses are trying to solve, such as taking payments online, growing recurring revenue, and getting paid faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead high-touch field marketing, targeted account-based programs, and executive events, including dinners and roadshows, for priority commercial accounts. Partner with Demand Generation on scaled digital demand campaigns and programs, connecting those programs with regional Sales priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-market with the SaaS Platforms and Partner teams to reach merchants through the software they already use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build Stripe’s brand with these businesses through customer stories, executive engagement, and industry initiatives, and lead the programs yourself where local context and senior ownership matter most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the regional marketing budget and use pipeline generation, pipeline progression, priority-account engagement, and ROI to guide investment. Partner with relevant teams to measure contributions to product adoption and customer advocacy, and use results to prioritise, scale, or change programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring regional and global teams (including Demand Generation, Product Marketing, and Global Campaigns) together to deliver the plan, and adapt global strategy to local buyer expectations, regulation, and the competitive landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re an experienced B2B marketing leader who has owned an integrated marketing strategy across a country, region, or comparably broad portfolio. You can set clear direction, make clear commercial trade-offs, and partner credibly with senior Sales and go-to-market (GTM) leaders—all while staying close enough to execution to turn strategy into measurable business results.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements for the role. If you meet them, we encourage you to apply. Preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of B2B marketing experience, including ownership of integrated marketing strategy and budget for a region or broad portfolio in tech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GTM business partnering: Proven track record partnering with senior Sales and GTM leaders to turn commercial targets into marketing plans and investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scaled and high-touch marketing: Experience running both scaled digital demand and high-touch account-based marketing for larger prospects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial accountability: Success generating pipeline, accelerating deal velocity, and managing multi-program budgets tied to clear ROI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-functional leadership: Demonstrated ability to align regional and global teams (Demand Generation, Product Marketing, and Communications) without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategy and hands-on delivery: Comfort moving between multi-quarter planning and delivering key initiatives yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive communication: Strong written and verbal skills, with the ability to explain technical products in business terms and present recommendations to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain knowledge: Experience in payments, fintech, embedded finance, ecommerce, or high-growth B2B SaaS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ecosystem and platform GTM: Experience marketing to software platforms, SaaS businesses, marketplaces, or building joint co-marketing programs with technology and ecosystem partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Positioning &amp;amp; localization: Proven ability to take category or business-model positioning and translate it into regional and local-market programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive advocacy: A track record of building customer advocacy and influence strategies with senior commercial stakeholders (Founders, CEOs, and CFOs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builder mindset: Comfort building marketing approaches where the playbook, tooling, or route to impact is still taking shape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our EMEA Marketing team is a dynamic, fast-growing group that loves turning customers into enthusiastic Stripe advocates. We work hand-in-hand with our Sales team to build demand, help users get the most out of our products, and craft marketing plans that truly resonate with local audiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Platforms is one of the largest and fastest-growing segments at Stripe. Our team works with ambitious software companies, including Shopify, Treatwell, Sage, and Wix. We help them to embed payments, payouts, and financial services directly into their software, transforming payments from an operational cost center into a core revenue engine. Because these businesses vary widely by vertical, technical maturity, and local market dynamics, our marketing balances a clear EMEA-wide strategy with the flexibility to activate locally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a lot still to build, and we&#39;re tackling it as a diverse, international team that thrives on collaboration, bold innovation, and genuine curiosity. If you love to learn and want to make a meaningful impact, we&#39;d love to have you join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll lead marketing strategy and plan delivery for Stripe&#39;s Platforms segment in EMEA, and serve as the main marketing partner on the EMEA Platforms Leadership Team. You&#39;ll set the regional field marketing strategy and investment plan, and shape how Stripe shows up across the region&#39;s platform ecosystem. You&#39;ll be accountable for demand, pipeline, customer advocacy, and Stripe&#39;s long-term market position in this segment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior individual contributor, you&#39;ll bring regional and global teams together around shared marketing priorities for EMEA Platforms, secure the key investment areas to deliver them, and balance global strategy with regional needs. You will directly lead high-priority initiatives across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own the integrated EMEA Platforms marketing strategy, turning business goals, market dynamics, customer needs, and competitors into clear priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with EMEA Platforms GTM leadership to set shared priorities, actively participate in business and pipeline reviews, and drive investment decisions for the highest-value opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and oversee the full-funnel marketing plan for this segment, encompassing brand, demand generation, account-based marketing, pipeline generation and acceleration, executive engagement, and customer advocacy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop industry and account programs for strategic customers and high-potential prospects, helping Sales engage the right stakeholders with relevant messages and field marketing programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring regional and global teams (including Demand Generation, Product Marketing, and Communications) together to deliver the marketing plan, and adapt global strategies to regional buyer expectations, regulation, and the competitive landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build Stripe’s brand presence for EMEA Platforms through executive engagement, industry initiatives, and customer stories, and lead the programmes yourself where local context and senior ownership matter most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the EMEA Platforms marketing budget and the commercial metrics across demand, pipeline progression, product adoption, priority-account engagement, and ROI. Use the results to prioritise, scale, or change investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent EMEA Platforms across EMEA and global marketing, bring local market insight into planning, and share what works with other regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re an experienced B2B marketer who has owned a country, regional, or similarly broad marketing strategy. You can set direction, make investment trade-offs, and work credibly with senior Sales and GTM leaders. You stay close enough to execution to turn the strategy into commercial results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements for the role. If you meet them, we encourage you to apply. Preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of B2B marketing experience, including ownership of integrated marketing strategy and investment for a region or comparably broad portfolio in enterprise technology or a complex B2B environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of acting as a strategic marketing partner to senior Sales and GTM leaders, turning commercial priorities into marketing plans and investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting strategy while staying close enough to execution to run programmes from business case through delivery and measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Success generating and accelerating enterprise or mid-market pipeline, progressing strategic accounts, and driving product adoption and expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional leadership, with a proven ability to align regional and global teams (including those with different goals and reporting lines) without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership of multi-programme portfolios and budgets, and the ability to use data and market insight to prioritise investments and make trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication, with the ability to explain technical concepts in business terms and present complex recommendations to executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good judgement and comfort making decisive calls when priorities compete or information is incomplete.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programme management skills, including experience using agencies or contractors to scale the team&#39;s capacity, and a working knowledge of Salesforce and common marketing tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing to software platforms, SaaS businesses, marketplaces, or other ecosystem-led business models.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of payments, embedded financial services, fintech, or ecommerce.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing segment or category positioning and turning it into regional and local-market programmes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing joint go-to-market programmes with technology, consulting, or other ecosystem partners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building customer advocacy programmes and influence strategies with senior enterprise stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a marketing approach where the playbook, resources, or route to impact was still taking shape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help define and amplify the Stripe story and connect our products with our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Product Marketing team’s mission is to generate insights that inform Stripe’s product strategy, lead go-to-market for our suite of products, and create and execute campaigns that drive product growth. Product Marketing is a highly cross-functional role at Stripe, partnering closely with Product and Engineering, Sales, Design, Developer Relations, and Communications. Unlike many other Product Marketing teams, our team works across the entire product lifecycle—from helping shape the product, to driving launch and commercialization, to growing product adoption after launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the regional product marketing lead for Latin America, you will champion the needs of users across the region and help define and develop a strong, trusted brand in the market. You will connect product, sales, and marketing to support Stripe’s growth while delivering successful user outcomes. Based in Mexico City, you will bring deep regional insight to Stripe’s product strategy and go-to-market execution across Latin America.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the delivery of regional product marketing priorities that drive growth for businesses across Latin America with a focus on Mexico, in close partnership with Product, go-to-market, and Marketing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop deep expertise in the needs of current and prospective users through user research, competitive landscape analysis, and product knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, deploy, and maintain market-specific value propositions, narratives, and messaging for marketing content, campaigns, and sales collateral&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive high-quality product launches and adoption by partnering with Product, Sales, Engineering, Marketing, Design, Communications, Partnerships, and other cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve seller effectiveness across the region through product and solution training, market-specific content and tools, and field support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor indicators of product adoption, usage, and satisfaction to identify barriers and opportunities across the regional growth funnel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with country and regional marketing teams to develop content programs for priority events, integrated campaigns, and ongoing demand generation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in B2B technology marketing or sales, including product marketing experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing value propositions, messaging, go-to-market strategies, and sales materials for multiple markets or customer segments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading cross-functional initiatives and building alignment with senior stakeholders across Product, Sales, and Marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High professional fluency in Spanish and English, as this role will develop market-specific messaging and work with users and internal teams across Latin America&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel domestically and internationally for business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing technology products or services across Latin America&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial services, or financial technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a global technology company with distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe provides regulated payments and financial services products, and also has a number of regulated subsidiaries, including in the United States (Money Transmitter and lending licenses). These licenses have programs of periodic and ad hoc regulatory reporting stemming from license requirements, and are critical aspects of the supervisory mechanisms for these entities. The Global Regulatory Reporting team leads the process by which we report regulatory data externally to regulators in support of our payments licenses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you&#39;ll support the Global Regulatory Reporting team by partnering with Legal, Compliance, Accounting, Business and Product, and Data Analytics teams across Stripe to maintain the Stripe North American regulatory reporting program. This includes understanding and documenting the applicable regulatory reporting requirements in the region, implementing systems and processes for comprehensively tracking those requirements for each of the Stripe North American entities, maintaining the end-to-end processes for the collation of data, production of reports, and continuously monitoring compliance to meet the expectations of regulators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is both a technology company and a financial services company, and you&#39;ll need to be comfortable straddling both of those worlds every day. You&#39;ll enjoy dealing with that puzzle, seeking creative solutions and moving quickly, often in the face of ambiguity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end U.S. regulatory reporting program for digital assets including stablecoin-related financial activities, including defining reporting scope, governance, timelines, and accountability across required regulatory filings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interpret U.S. regulatory reporting requirements applicable to stablecoins, digital assets, payments, and custody, and translate them into clear reporting specifications, data definitions, and execution plans in partnership with Legal and Compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full regulatory reporting lifecycle, from data sourcing and aggregation through validation, internal review, sign-off, and timely submission to regulators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure regulatory reports accurately reflect stablecoin-specific activities and risks, including issuance, redemption, circulation, reserves, custody arrangements, and transaction flows across on-chain and off-chain systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and maintain a robust regulatory reporting control framework, including data quality checks, reconciliations, documentation, and issue remediation to support audit and exam readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering, Data, Finance, Compliance, and Legal to improve data lineage, transparency, and automation across regulatory reporting processes as the business scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own regulatory reporting change management, including assessing the impact of new or evolving stablecoin regulations, product launches, and system changes on reporting scope, data requirements, and controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain regulator-ready documentation, including reporting methodologies, assumptions, data lineage, and process documentation to support supervisory reviews and examinations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary point of contact for regulatory reporting matters during U.S. regulatory exams, audits, and regulatory inquiries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, Business Administration, or a related field; equivalent practical experience in financial services regulatory reporting will be considered&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience leading the delivery of an ongoing regulatory reporting program within a regulated financial services environment, ideally supporting stablecoin issuance, payments, or custody-related activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of U.S. compliance and regulatory obligations applicable to stablecoins, including evolving federal and state frameworks (including, but not limited to, the GENIUS Act and related Treasury, banking, and payments guidance)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent working knowledge of the U.S. payment stablecoin regulatory landscape, with experience engaging directly with U.S. federal regulators (e.g., OCC, Treasury) and state regulators on regulatory reporting, data submissions, or supervisory requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work across complex data environments, including navigating on-chain and off-chain data sources, internal ledgers, and third-party systems to produce accurate, cohesive, and regulator-ready reporting deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reading, analyzing, and compiling financial statements, reserve-related data, transaction-level reporting, and other financial regulatory reports relevant to stablecoin and payments activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in financial services with direct exposure to stablecoins, digital assets, payments, e-money, or other money services business activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success executing complex, cross-functional programs in fast-growing organizations, with an emphasis on building scalable, repeatable regulatory reporting processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and judgment, with the ability to quickly understand novel or ambiguous regulatory and data challenges and drive balanced, risk-aware solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently and efficiently in a fast-paced, high-volume, and evolving regulatory environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to collaborate effectively across Compliance, Legal, Finance, Engineering, Data, Product, and Accounting teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong “culture of compliance” mindset, with the ability to translate regulatory expectations into practical, business-aligned execution without impeding responsible growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with stablecoins, digital assets, payments, or fintech platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with regulatory reporting for banks, trust companies, payment institutions, or money services businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on Call Reports FFIEC041 and FFIEC031&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting regulatory exams, audits, or supervisory reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to reporting automation, data pipelines, or reporting tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe has a growing focus on our Renewals business and opportunity to drive growth. Our team provides strategic &amp;amp; operational partnership to those specialized sellers, cross-functional product partners, and leadership. Partnership is provided across three pillars:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategy and planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytics and insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within the GTM Strategy &amp;amp; Operations organization, our team, the renewals team of our GTM Post Sales Strategy &amp;amp; Operations is focused on driving business changes across business operations, insights, process, and tooling. We facilitate incremental Stripe productivity improvements to help our specialized sellers deliver key revenue results for their remit and drive Stripe Revenue. &amp;nbsp;We are a global team with resources in the Americas, Europe and Asia Pacific.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team is still very nascent, with the majority of our near term focus on building business foundations, which necessarily entails a focus on operational projects (process design, business cadences, systems work). This analyst is a critical person to the foundations and scale of the Renewals business. Their role includes: measuring and providing insights on performance, forecasting, and process improvement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set annual and quarterly SOKRs and track performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build actionable reports and insights for leadership reporting forums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare for QBRs and other leadership meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Examine operational or financial data to uncover trends and guide decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;System and operational workflow management analysis and investigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve business processes through data driven decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
