&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe, LLC. is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become a domain expert in Connect and Risk and Compliance areas of Connect.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle inquiries from internal Stripes and external partners&#39; technical teams with detailed investigation and sometimes code changes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organize and direct complex technical changes as part of product releases and merchant onboarding and migrations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and automate inefficient or unnecessary manual processes by making direct code changes, or coordinating more complex code changes across Stripe.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design alerting systems using existing tools to respond to incidents quickly, or prevent them altogether.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct data analysis to understand the impact of risk and compliance interventions on the users and surface future product opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must have a Bachelor&#39;s degree or foreign equivalent in Computer Science, Information systems, Engineering, or a related field, plus 2 years of experience in Technical or technical user-facing roles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must also have 2 years of experience in each of the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developer tools including git;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scripting and automation skills including Ruby and Python;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Writing tooling and automation, including testing and idempotency;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Observability tooling including metrics (Prometheus, Datadog), logging (LogScale), and distributed tracing (Honeycomb);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Incident response, on-call rotations, runbooks, and postmortem processes; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using SQL and relational databases including PostgreSQL or MySQL for operational tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary: $137,000.00 - $205,600.00 /yr.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This salary range represents the base salary range for the role and any sales commissions/sales bonuses targets, if applicable, would be in addition to the base salary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;40 hrs/week&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;100% Telecommuting permitted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Multiple Positions Available.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional benefits for this role may include: equity, company bonus or sales commissions/bonuses; 401(k) plan; medical, dental, and vision benefits; and wellness stipends.&lt;strong&gt; CA75&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
