&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;To help support that mission, in August we &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/newsroom/news/stripe-agrees-to-acquire-openrouter&quot;&gt;announced&lt;/a&gt; that Stripe had agreed to acquire OpenRouter, a leading AI model gateway and routing platform. While that acquisition is under regulatory review and has not yet closed, our intent is that this role will support the OpenRouter team following the closing of the acquisition.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;OpenRouter helps developers and businesses access and use a broad range of AI models through a unified platform. This role sits at the intersection of OpenRouter and Stripe, supporting hiring across Tech, GTM, and Core teams. You’ll serve as a bridge between the 2 organizations, bringing Stripe’s recruiting standards, talent networks, and resources to OpenRouter while protecting its speed and minimizing operational overhead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll align to Tech, GTM, or Core, but you won’t be dedicated to a single job profile within that function. For example, a GTM Recruiter may support Sales, Solutions Architecture, Marketing, or other GTM roles as priorities shift. The same model applies across Tech and Core.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own full-cycle recruiting for your aligned function, moving across job profiles based on business priority, from intake and market mapping through offer acceptance and onboarding handoff. You’ll combine direct execution with consultative partnership, working closely with hiring managers to clarify needs, advise on talent markets, build and engage qualified pipelines, and move candidates through structured, timely processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll operate with startup speed while leveraging Stripe’s infrastructure and reach. You’ll use metrics to identify risk and guide action, while keeping recruiting outcomes, not reporting or process for its own sake, at the center of the work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own full-cycle recruiting across the full range of roles within your aligned function, Tech, GTM, or Core, moving between job profiles as business priorities shift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build qualified and inclusive pipelines through hands-on sourcing across communities, referrals, events, market mapping, relationship-based outreach, and other creative channels beyond inbound applications and standard LinkedIn outreach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner consultatively with hiring managers to translate business priorities into clear role requirements, search strategies, structured assessments, and timely decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use funnel metrics, market evidence, and candidate feedback to identify risks, recommend actions, and communicate progress without allowing reporting or process to substitute for recruiting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver a thoughtful candidate experience and maintain relationships with prospective candidates for immediate and future needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as an operational bridge between OpenRouter and Stripe by absorbing coordination where possible, maintaining continuity, and reducing the time OpenRouter leaders spend navigating recruiting processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flex across job profiles within your aligned function when priorities shift or additional coverage is needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, including direct ownership of sourcing, assessment, stakeholder partnership, and closing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience recruiting in a high-growth technology startup, preferably during a stage below 200 employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated recruiting depth in at least 1 of the following areas: Tech, GTM, or Core, with experience recruiting across multiple job profiles or clear evidence you can move between profiles as business priorities shift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated interest in and ability to personally conduct hands-on sourcing and build qualified pipelines through creative channels beyond inbound applications and standard LinkedIn outreach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering consultatively with hiring managers, managing multiple searches, and using recruiting metrics and market evidence to identify risk and guide action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work through ambiguity, adapt quickly as priorities change, and balance direct execution with longer-term pipeline building&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience recruiting across both startup and larger-company environments and helping teams work effectively across different operating models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting structured, competency-based hiring processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience recruiting across multiple geographies or advising on location strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience using recruiting technology, talent intelligence, or AI tools to improve sourcing and candidate experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is beloved by developers for the simplicity of our APIs, the thoroughness of our documentation, and our focus on developer experience. The Technical Solutions Engineering (TSE) team supports our developer-users and champions developer experience as central to the overall user experience. TSE interacts directly with developer-users more than any other team at Stripe, so your role will have a significant impact on what Stripe is known for and values most. When we do our job well, developers all over the world can smoothly launch and grow their businesses on Stripe, whether they’re integrating payments for the first time or building complex financial systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TSEs understand the fundamentals of programming incredibly well and eagerly familiarize themselves with others’ code. You’ll explain technical concepts about Stripe’s products, build and debug integrations with developers, and produce and improve guides that help our users solve problems and succeed with Stripe. You’ll interact with developers of all skill levels through a variety of channels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Early on, current team members will devote time to teaching you and helping you develop expertise in Stripe, its services, and how we interact with users. Later, we’d love for you to take on this role with others on the team and Stripes broadly, as teaching is a great way to learn and reinforce what you know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you enjoy working with all kinds of code, researching quickly, writing clearly, and helping others build products their businesses depend on, we want to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate with external developers based in Asia pacific and China region to help them build applications using Stripe’s infrastructure across programming languages and frameworks, including Java, Python, Ruby, PHP, Go, Node.js, .NET, React, React Native, Swift, Objective-C, and Kotlin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unblock external developers facing complex integration challenges through support channels, including email, ticketing software, internal issue trackers, community platforms such as Stack Overflow, and real-time chat platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain internal and external documentation, examples, integration demos, and code snippets that demonstrate usage patterns for Stripe’s infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify points of friction developers encounter and collaborate with engineering teams to improve Stripe products, including participating in planning sessions, design reviews, and development meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain internal support tooling for TSE and Stripe Support more broadly, such as a retrieval-augmented generation copilot powered by a large language model or the Invoice Explainer Admin tool&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a developer advocate and educational resource within Stripe by preparing training for non-developers and responding to product integration questions in real time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 4 years of full-stack software development experience, with a proven track record of building web or mobile applications that deliver high-quality user experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience explaining technical concepts and the ability to explain how Stripe works to both technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to write clean code in multiple programming languages and read code that may be less well structured&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to support users during working hours in your region, with occasional weekend coverage to monitor or support critical infrastructure. The team is largely remote and supports working arrangements that accommodate family care and other needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High professional fluency in spoken and written Mandarin and English to explain technical concepts, troubleshoot integrations, and answer questions over video calls and through written support channels for English- and Mandarin-speaking users across Asia-Pacific, including China&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to write clearly and quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;General software engineering skills and an understanding of concepts that support learning new languages and frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience teaching or coaching developers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with substantial autonomy and limited supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Computer Engineering, or a related analytical field of study&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
