&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;📍Dublin, Ireland | 💰€68,000 - €85,000, Incentive Awards tied to your performance ➕ benefits&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;⭐Our Regulatory Affairs team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a pragmatic, organised and personable individual to strengthen our Regulatory Affairs team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Regulatory Affairs team is the central team responsible for maintaining open and collaborative relationships with our regulators across the Monzo Group. In the Regulatory Affairs team, you’ll support and strengthen Monzo’s regulatory relationships and work closely with Executives to help shape our vision and regulatory affairs strategy as Monzo continues to grow. You’ll also work closely with our contacts at the Irish and European Regulators and support the wider Regulatory Affairs team with engagement with other relevant Regulators (PRA and FCA), responding to information requests, preparing for meetings and submitting regulatory submissions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are on a mission to &lt;em&gt;Make Money Work for Everyone&lt;/em&gt; and we’ve grown to over 15 million customers globally. For Regulatory Affairs this means ensuring our regulators are kept informed, managing regulatory requests and educating colleagues on the regulatory landscape.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate a “three lines of defence” model of risk management at Monzo. You’ll be sitting in the second line as part of our Risk and Compliance team, working in the Regulatory Affairs Team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🔑You’ll play a key role by...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preparing for and facilitating regulator meetings, reviews and requests. Preparation includes working closely with Executives and stakeholders throughout the business to prepare and advise them on how best to meet regulatory expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keeping our regulators up to date with proactive notifications on products and strategic initiatives, as well as leading on regulatory communications during an incident.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the governance and tracking of regulatory deliverables, deadlines and activities ensuring stakeholders are held accountable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taking responsibility for the preparation, submission and management of technically complex regulatory submissions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with subject matter experts in Risk and Compliance and across the business to coordinate and prepare for regulatory visits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preparing data driven reports for the Executives that are clear, concise and informative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building and enhancing our policies and procedures for engaging with regulators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Being a champion of risk and compliance and building respectful and collaborative relationships with all levels of stakeholders across the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🤩We’d love to hear from you if…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have proven experience in a regulatory affairs role at an Irish/European regulated financial services firm or at an Irish or European financial services regulator&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have knowledge of CBI and/or ECB regulatory and supervisory obligations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a deep understanding of managing relations with important external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have excellent written and verbal communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have an ability to lead and manage multiple projects to short deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a critical thinker and not afraid to challenge&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are self-motivated, highly organised and focused on executing well&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy collaborating as a team and is able to work independently with changing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a genuine interest in the regulated financial services environment and how it is changing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🙌What’s in it for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰A salary range of €68,000 - €85,000 ➕Incentive Awards tied to your performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📍This role will have a hybrid working model, based in our Dublin office 2 - 3 days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⏰We offer flexible working hours and trust you to work enough hours to do your job well, and at times that suit you and your team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏝 Annual Leave - 34 days including public holidays (24 holiday days + 10 public holidays)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚€1,200 learning budget each year to use on books, training courses and conferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏥Private healthcare scheme&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰Pension scheme: the minimum contribution is 4% and Monzo matches any additional contributions that you make up to a maximum of 6%&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💛Wellbeing benefits: financial education, women’s and men’s health support, mental health benefits, including coaching and counselling&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🌈 The application journey has 4 key steps&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Short video call with a member of the hiring team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A take home task (practical written exercise)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow up video call with the Hiring Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Final stage 2-part Role Specific and Behavioural interviews with members from the wider Risk and Compliance collective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This process should take around 3-4 weeks - your schedule is really important to us, so we promise to be as flexible as possible!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have some guidelines on using Artificial Intelligence (AI) to ace an application and interview at Monzo. &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/the-ultimate-guide-on-using-ai-to-ace-an-interview-at-monzo&quot;&gt;You can read them here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ll only close this role once we have enough applications for the next stage. Please submit your application as soon as possible to make sure you don’t miss out.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-ÉS1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunities for everyone&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Diversity and inclusion are a priority for us and we’re making sure we have lots of support for all of our people to grow at Monzo. At Monzo, we’re embracing diversity by fostering an inclusive environment for all people to do the best work of their lives with us. This is integral to our mission of making money work for everyone. You can read more in our &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/diversity-and-inclusion&quot;&gt;blog&lt;/a&gt;, 2026 &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/our-2026-diversity-and-inclusion-report&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Diversity and Inclusion Report&lt;/a&gt; and 2025 &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/gender-pay-gap-report-2025&quot;&gt;Gender Pay Gap Report.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re an equal opportunity employer. All applicants will be considered for employment without attention to age, ethnicity, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, family or parental status, national origin, or veteran, neurodiversity or disability status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have a preferred name, please use it to apply. We don&#39;t need full or birth names at application stage.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;🚀 We’re on a mission to make money work for everyone.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re waving goodbye to the complicated and confusing ways of traditional banking.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After starting as a prepaid card, our product offering has grown a lot in the last 10 years in the UK. As well as&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/current-account/personal&quot;&gt;personal&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/business-banking&quot;&gt;business&lt;/a&gt; bank accounts, we offer &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/current-account/joint-account&quot;&gt;joint accounts&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/current-account/16-17&quot;&gt;accounts for 16-17 year olds&lt;/a&gt;, a &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/current-account/under-16s&quot;&gt;free kids account&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/flex&quot;&gt;credit cards&lt;/a&gt; in the UK, with more exciting things to come beyond. Our UK customers can also &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/savings&quot;&gt;save&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/investments&quot;&gt;invest &lt;/a&gt;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/pensions&quot;&gt;combine their pensions&lt;/a&gt; with us.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With our hot coral cards and get-paid-early feature, combined with financial education on social media and our award winning customer service, we have a long history of creating magical moments for our customers!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re not only about selling products - we want to solve problems and change lives through Monzo.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;📍 London | 💰 £60k – £80k base salary | £100k – £135k OTE&amp;nbsp; + &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/careers#benefits&quot;&gt;Benefits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Monzo Business team ⭐&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monzo Business helps businesses manage their money, and more than a million businesses (1 in 6!) in the UK bank with us. Now, we’re exploring how we can help more established businesses switch to Monzo, across the UK and Europe 🚀&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Many of those businesses have more complex needs. They may need help understanding whether Monzo is right for them, moving their banking or getting the most from our products. A great conversation with the right person can make a real difference.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ve started building a sales team and testing a more personal approach. Now we’re looking for a Sales Manager to lead a team of Account Executives and help us turn what we’re learning into a repeatable, effective sales motion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a chance to build something new. You’ll coach your team, help them deliver great results and use what you see every day to make the way we sell better. You’ll work closely with Revenue Operations (RevOps), Product and other teams to improve our processes and customer journeys.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll also help build an AI-first sales motion from the start. We want someone who’s curious about AI and automation, actively experiments with new tools and can help the team spend more time on conversations that matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🔑 You’ll play a key role by...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leading a team of Account Executives.&lt;/strong&gt; Manage a pod of 6–8 people and be accountable for its performance, from reaching the right businesses and converting opportunities to customer activation and quality. Translate the wider Business strategy and set clear expectations, understand what’s driving results and act when performance needs to improve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coaching and developing your team.&lt;/strong&gt; Spend time listening to calls, reviewing opportunities and giving clear, regular feedback. Help each person build their skills and confidence, recognise great work and address underperformance fairly. Help hire and onboard new team members as we grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Building the sales motion.&lt;/strong&gt; Turn what you and your team learn into better ways of working. Spot friction in lead handling, follow-up, handovers and the sales process; test improvements, measure their impact and share what works so we can build a repeatable playbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Staying close to customers.&lt;/strong&gt; We expect Sales Managers to also take a few sales calls each week and make a few sales a month. Use what you learn from customers and the sales journey to coach the team, identify product needs and improve the motion. Most of your time will be spent leading the team and improving how we work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Helping shape our Products.&lt;/strong&gt; Share what you learn from customers with Product to help shape our proposition and priorities, and use what we learn to improve how we sell.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Putting AI and automation to work.&lt;/strong&gt; Experiment with tools, agents and workflows that help the team research prospects, prepare for conversations, follow up or learn from calls. Work with specialist teams to test ideas responsibly, understand their impact and help the team adopt what works.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Making good decisions with data.&lt;/strong&gt; Use pipeline, conversion, activation, productivity and quality data to understand where the team is doing well and where customers or opportunities are getting stuck. Keep the pipeline accurate and work with RevOps on reporting and forecasting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working as one team.&lt;/strong&gt; Bring frontline insight to RevOps, Product, Marketing and Operations. Help shape the tools, processes and customer journeys Sales needs, and work together to solve problems that affect your team and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Earning customers’ trust.&lt;/strong&gt; Build a culture that puts customers first. Coach your team to understand their needs, represent Monzo accurately and deliver good outcomes. Raise concerns early and work with Risk, Compliance and Legal when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🤩 We’d love to hear from you if…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve managed and developed a sales team. You can share examples of how you’ve coached individuals, given feedback and improved performance, including when conversations were difficult.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand selling to small and medium-sized businesses in a relatively high-volume environment. You can balance an efficient process with thoughtful, customer-focused conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a builder. You’ve spotted a problem in how a team sells, tried a better approach and helped people put it into practice. You’re comfortable making progress when the playbook is still being written.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve actively experimented with AI or automation at work and are keen to explore what agents and new workflows can do. You can tell us what you tried, the problem you were solving and what you learned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re happy to stay hands-on with customers. You enjoy sales conversations yourself and use what you learn to help others improve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You use data to understand performance. You can look at a funnel or pipeline, ask good questions and turn the answers into practical action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work well with people in different teams. You can explain what your team and customers need, share evidence and help colleagues find solutions together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care about doing the right thing for customers. You’re comfortable working within clear standards and learning what it takes to sell in a regulated environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You might have built your experience in financial services, technology or another business selling to businesses. We care more about what you’ve done and how you think than the exact path you took to get here.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You don’t need to tick every box. If this role excites you and you think you could make a difference, we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not ticking every box? That’s totally okay! Studies show that women and people of colour might hesitate to apply unless they meet every single requirement. At Monzo, we’re dedicated to creating a diverse and welcoming team. If you’re passionate about this role and keen to learn and grow with us, we encourage you to apply—even if you don’t have everything that’s listed just yet. Drop us your application, we’d love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🙌 What’s in it for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰 £60k – £80k base salary, plus on-target commission based on team performance. Total on-target earnings are approximately £100k – £135k&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📍 This role is based in our London office. You’ll work from the office at least 3 days a week to stay close to your team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⏰ We offer flexible working hours and trust you to work enough hours to do your job well, and at times that suit you and your team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 £1,000 learning budget each year to use on books, training courses and conferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏡 We’ll set you up to work from home; all employees are given MacBooks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;➕ Plus lots more! Read our &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/careers/&quot;&gt;full list of benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🌈 The application journey has 4 key steps&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30-minute introductory call with a recruiter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A full interview loop covering role-specific skills, behaviours and values&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A conversation with a member of the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Final interview with the hiring manager at our London office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ll share more details about the interview process and timing as you progress. Your schedule is important to us, so we’ll be as flexible as possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have some guidelines on using Artificial Intelligence (AI) to ace an application and interview at Monzo. You can &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/the-ultimate-guide-on-using-ai-to-ace-an-interview-at-monzo&quot;&gt;read them here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ll only close this role once we have enough applications for the next stage. Please submit your application as soon as possible to make sure you don’t miss out.&lt;/p&gt;
