&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Counsel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are looking for a driven and enthusiastic Commercial Counsel based in New York to join&lt;br&gt;the global Deal Desk within the Commercial Legal team at Adyen. As Commercial Counsel,&lt;br&gt;you will be responsible for negotiating customer-facing contract negotiations, primarily&lt;br&gt;focused on platform and franchise customers. You will also be responsible for drafting&lt;br&gt;comprehensive negotiation playbooks, training our commercial colleagues on how to sell our&lt;br&gt;agreements, advising on contract interpretation, early-stage customer disputes, and other&lt;br&gt;general commercial matters.&lt;br&gt;This is a role for a counsel who thrives in a fast-moving, complex environment, who is&lt;br&gt;commercially-minded, and who can leverage their sophisticated legal expertise and strong&lt;br&gt;communication skills into tangible, scalable value that accelerates Adyen’s global growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;● Provide strategic legal advice across various commercial functions, advising&lt;br&gt;stakeholders in our sales, account management, product, and regulatory teams&lt;br&gt;globally.&lt;br&gt;● Draft, review, and negotiate a wide variety of complex, multi-jurisdictional commercial&lt;br&gt;agreements for our payment, data and financial services products.&lt;br&gt;● Proactively problem solve for emerging legal and operational risks, providing risk-&lt;br&gt;based decisions on complex legal issues and proposing improvements and efficiencies&lt;br&gt;to mitigate future exposure.&lt;br&gt;● Advise on early-stage customer disputes, managing initial phases of legal conflicts,&lt;br&gt;and providing counsel on complex legal interpretations.&lt;br&gt;● Drive legal automation efforts to help scale our team and bring greater efficiency to&lt;br&gt;the contracting process.&lt;br&gt;● Work autonomously in a cross-functional manner.&lt;br&gt;● Build strong relationships with colleagues, leaders, and stakeholders across the&lt;br&gt;company.&lt;br&gt;● Participate in training our commercial colleagues across the globe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;● You have 5+ years of legal experience, in house or at a law firm.&lt;br&gt;● You have strong commercial contracting and/or other transactional experience.&lt;br&gt;● You can collaborate with other legal counsels based in jurisdictions across the US,&lt;br&gt;LATAM, EMEA, and APAC.&lt;br&gt;● You are a team player who likes to collaborate and include different people to sharpen&lt;br&gt;your ideas.&lt;br&gt;● You have solid people skills and will work well with a variety of internal and external&lt;br&gt;stakeholders and customers from varying disciplines and cultures.&lt;br&gt;● You can work autonomously and run things like your own business.&lt;br&gt;● You are curious, ask questions, and take ownership over your learning and professional&lt;br&gt;growth.&lt;br&gt;● You are self-motivated, driven, reliable, adaptable and detail-oriented.&lt;br&gt;● You have experience educating others on complex ideas, communicating them clearly,&lt;br&gt;and providing additional training when necessary.&lt;br&gt;● You have the ability to structure and prioritize your work in a high volume, fast-paced&lt;br&gt;environment and build and drive processes to completion.&lt;br&gt;● You are available to work from our New York office and travel to other offices&lt;br&gt;periodically.&lt;br&gt;● You are fluent in English, both written and spoken. Any additional language is a plus.&lt;/p&gt;
