&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Operational Incentive Manager, you own the accurate, timely calculation and operation of Adyen&#39;s compensation plans for the commercial teams. You are the person who knows how every plan works, runs it in the comps system and offline, resolves exceptions, and explains and defends the plan to the business. You also host enablement sessions so that sellers and managers understand how they are paid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a mid-level role: you work independently on day-to-day operations and own the process end to end, while larger plan design changes are decided with S&amp;amp;E, Regional leaders, HR, CCO, Rewards and Finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Plan Calculation and Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calculate and run payouts for the BDR, Sales, Sales Lead and AM plans each period, in the comps system and offline where needed (spreadsheets, reconciliations).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain plan setup in the comps system: claims, targets, rates, accelerators, thresholds, cap rules and eligibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile source data with Finance and HR, and fix data issues before payout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the payout cycle on time: validation, review, sign-off and hand-off to Payroll, with clear audit trails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep plan documents, calculation logic and process documentation current and auditable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the Point of Contact for Exceptions and Escalations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle questions and disputes on crediting, split deals, role and territory changes, leavers and joiners, and mid-period adjustments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess exceptions against the plan rules, recommend a decision, and route those that need approval to the right owners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Log exceptions and decisions so that similar cases are treated consistently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Defend and Interpret the Comps Plans&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explain the logic and intent of each plan to sellers, Sales Leads, Finance and HR, and hold the line when requests go against plan rules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze plan performance (attainment distribution, payout cost versus budget) and bring improvement ideas to plan design discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support annual plan design and rollout: modeling scenarios and testing changes before launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable the Business&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Host enablement sessions for new joiners, sales managers and the wider sales organization on how the plans work, how payouts are calculated and how to read statements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create clear materials (guides, FAQs, calculators) and keep them updated when plans change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect recurring questions and turn them into process or communication improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3 to 5 years of experience in sales compensation, incentive operations, sales operations, finance or a similar analytical role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of incentive models: quota-based and commission plans, accelerators and decelerators, SPIFFs, clawbacks, crediting and splits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience operating a comp or incentive management system (for example SPIFF, Salesforce-based tools) and the offline work around it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel or Google Sheets skills; comfortable with large datasets, lookups and reconciliations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail and a strong sense of ownership of accuracy and deadlines, especially under payout pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communicator who can explain complex plan mechanics simply, in writing and in front of a group.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident handling sensitive pay topics: you can say no, explain why, and stay constructive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a fast-growing, global or fintech/payments company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting multiple sales roles (BDR, sales, management, account management) with different plan structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with audit, SOX or similar controls on variable pay.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience facilitating training or enablement sessions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Mid-level Means Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You run the operation independently and do not need step-by-step direction on routine cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You escalate and recommend, rather than wait to be told, on unusual exceptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You contribute ideas to plan design but are not expected to own the plan strategy on your own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
