&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-End Case Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage periodic reviews for high-risk enterprise customers, from initial assessment through final remediation. This involves conducting in-depth due diligence, analyzing complex ownership structures, and adhering to all regulatory obligations and internal policies are met within strict timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Uphold Quality &amp;amp; Consistency:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain &quot;First-Time-Right&quot; accuracy, perform regular quality control checks for the team, upskill team members on quality standards, ensure accurate risk reasoning, follow SOPs strictly, and maintain high-quality decision-making across all casework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Peer Mentorship:&lt;/strong&gt; Coach peers, guide the team through complex cases, support upskilling team quality, and foster a culture of proactive risk management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Policy Alignment &amp;amp; Operational Excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead calibration sessions to translate Second Line compliance requirements into practical daily workflows, continuously refining and enhancing our standard operating procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional &amp;amp; Customer Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the primary liaison between Commercial teams and external customers, balancing effective risk mitigation with strategic business growth during complex discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Volume &amp;amp; SLA Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Efficiently navigate high operational volumes and strict regulatory deadlines while managing competing priorities and stakeholder expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AMLR &amp;amp; Product Partnership:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with team leads and compliance teams to ensure the scalable and correct execution of upcoming AMLR regulations, aligning with our forward-looking compliance and operational goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;: 6+ years experience in CDD, KYC, or EDD operations or equivalent Second Line Risk or Compliance role within a FinTech, Payment Service Provider, or Financial Institution. E&lt;em&gt;xperience coaching/mentoring team members is a plus.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Complex Risk &amp;amp; Regulatory Depth:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven mastery in evaluating complex risk scenarios beyond standard checklists. You bring deep experience navigating challenges such as layered corporate structures, offshore/nominee entities, UBO transparency, high-risk business models, scheme rules, and multi-jurisdictional AML/CFT standards (e.g. DNB, FCA, FinCEN). &lt;em&gt;Prior experience as a Quality Checker or QA auditor in 1st/2nd Line functions is a plus.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Forward-Looking Mindset:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Up-to-date knowledge of upcoming EU Anti-Money Laundering Regulation changes and perpetual KYC implementation, combined with proven ability to analyze how future regulatory directives and legislative decisions impact operational risk and compliance processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scalability &amp;amp; Data Rigor:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Analytical mindset proficient in leveraging data and analytics to identify trends, conduct root-cause analysis, and actively partner with cross-functional teams to build automated risk operations solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomous &amp;amp; Strong Team Mentality:&lt;/strong&gt; High autonomy, resilience, and clear written and verbal communication skills. Eager to share knowledge, coach colleagues, and collaborate seamlessly across operational, second line and commercial teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Diversity, Equity and Inclusion commitments&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our unique approach is a product of our diverse perspectives. This diversity of backgrounds and cultures is essential in helping us maintain our momentum. Our business and technical challenges are unique, and we need as many different voices as possible to join us in solving them - voices like yours. No matter who you are or where you’re from, we welcome you to be your true self at Adyen.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Studies show that women and members of underrepresented communities apply for jobs only if they meet 100% of the qualifications. Does this sound like you? If so, Adyen encourages you to reconsider and apply. We look forward to your application!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s next?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Ensuring a smooth and enjoyable candidate experience is critical for us. We aim to get back to you regarding your application within 5 business days. Our interview process tends to take about 4 weeks to complete, but may fluctuate depending on the role. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.adyen.com/how-we-hire&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Learn more about our hiring process here&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;. Don’t be afraid to let us know if you need more flexibility.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based out of our Amsterdam office. We are an office-first company and value in-person collaboration; we do not offer remote-only roles.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is Adyen&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Adyen provides payments, data, and financial products in a single solution for customers like Meta, Uber, H&amp;amp;M, and Microsoft - making us the financial technology platform of choice. At Adyen, everything we do is engineered for ambition.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;For our teams, we create an environment with opportunities for our people to succeed, backed by the culture and support to ensure they are enabled to truly own their careers. We are motivated individuals who tackle unique technical challenges at scale and solve them as a team. Together, we deliver innovative and ethical solutions that help businesses achieve their ambitions faster.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Credit Risk Operations owns Adyen&#39;s global arrears and collections flow for our financial products. When a merchant falls behind on repayment, we work to recover what is owed while keeping the relationship intact and staying fully compliant.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We sit at the intersection of Credit Risk, Product, Finance, Legal and our second-line Risk and Compliance teams. The team is growing quickly, so the processes, tooling and playbooks you help build now will shape how Adyen collects at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Collections Analyst, Commerical Credit in Chicago, you will own a portfolio of US merchants in arrears across Adyen&#39;s financial products: cash advances, capital loans, charge cards, overdrafts and hardware financing. You will resolve each case end to end, from first outreach to repayment plan, recovery or escalation. Alongside your caseload, you will help turn a fast-growing operation into a scalable, compliant and increasingly automated one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will run your own portfolio independently, within agreed playbooks and approval limits. You will escalate exceptions such as settlements, write-offs and legal action to senior colleagues, and take on more complex accounts as you grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a portfolio of merchant accounts in arrears and drive each case to resolution by email&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explain contractual obligations clearly, negotiate realistic repayment plans and follow through until they are met&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot breaches of agreement, such as licensing issues or unauthorized business activity, and agree next steps with Legal and Credit Risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate at the right moment and coordinate recoveries with Risk, Finance, Legal and Product so merchants get one consistent answer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor portfolio health, including delinquency rates, roll rates, promise-to-pay and cure rates, and flag emerging risks early&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep accurate, audit-ready records of every merchant interaction and case decision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure every recovery action complies with US federal and state collections, servicing and lending rules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Help design and improve collections tooling, automation and workflows so the operation scales without adding headcount at the same rate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements below. If you do, we encourage you to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in collections, account recovery or credit operations at a lender, bank, fintech or payments company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience managing a portfolio of overdue business or consumer credit accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of US collections and servicing regulations, and how to apply them day to day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence in difficult conversations: you balance empathy with firmness and keep the relationship intact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and spoken English, including explaining terms like breach of contract or default in plain language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organization: you track many accounts, deadlines and follow-ups without dropping detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with collections platforms or CRM tools, and with Excel or Google Sheets for basic reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A low-ego, high-accountability approach to working with Risk, Legal, Finance and Product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to leverage AI tools and automation to increase operational efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collecting on commercial credit products: merchant cash advances, working capital loans, charge cards, overdrafts or equipment financing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with FDCPA, UDAAP, state collection licensing rules and fair-lending expectations as they apply to business credit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience handling legal escalations, settlements, charge-offs or third-party agency placements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with data: SQL, Looker or similar tools to analyze delinquency trends and build reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of improving a collections process, building a playbook or helping automate a workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
