&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Partner Solution Engineer - Device Assurance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Partner Solution Engineer &amp;nbsp;within Hardware Partner Engineering, you will help to ensure that payment terminals supplied by our hardware partners meet Adyen&#39;s technical, reliability and quality expectations throughout their lifecycle.&lt;br&gt;You will own the system assurance capability for devices: translating product needs into clear technical requirements, defining how those requirements should be validated, and ensuring suppliers provide sufficient evidence to demonstrate compliance.&lt;br&gt;You will work closely with Product, SW Engineer, Partner Solutions Engineers, &amp;nbsp;OEMs and external testing labs to create a lightweight and scalable technical-assurance model across our hardware partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate product use cases and operational needs into clear, reusable device-level system requirements covering hardware, connectivity, power, diagnostics, environmental behaviour and reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain requirements throughout the device lifecycle, incorporating product changes, field learnings and reliability findings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define validation strategies, acceptance criteria and qualification approaches for new devices and significant changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define what evidence should be produced by hardware partners and external laboratories, and review test plans, results and technical evidence for completeness and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge gaps in supplier validation, technical claims, RCA and corrective actions, and ensure additional evidence or actions are provided where needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support technical assessment and qualification of new devices, suppliers and future RFPs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess the technical impact of lifecycle changes and ensure field failures, RCA and corrective actions feed back into requirements and validation expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across Product, Software Engineering, Partner Solutions Engineering, Integrity, Supply Chain, OEMs and external labs to provide clear technical recommendations, risks and evidence for product-readiness decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7–10+ years of relevant engineering experience in embedded systems, hardware products, systems engineering, product assurance or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience defining and maintaining system-level requirements and translating product use cases into clear technical expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with verification, validation and qualification, including test strategy, acceptance criteria and technical evidence review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong system-level understanding of embedded products across hardware, firmware/OS and software interactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working technically with hardware manufacturers, OEMs or external engineering suppliers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to critically assess supplier test results, technical claims, RCA and corrective actions and identify where evidence is insufficient.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong engineering judgement and stakeholder-management skills, able to introduce enough structure to make quality predictable without creating unnecessary processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive, pragmatic and comfortable operating independently with incomplete information in a fast-moving environment where processes are evolving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
