&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Senior Recruiter&lt;/strong&gt; to join our North America Talent Acquisition team in San Francisco.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Recruiter, you will serve as a strategic partner to business leaders—combining deep expertise in identifying complex enterprise talent with a track record of proactively sourcing hard-to-reach, passive candidates. Your primary focus will be owning G&amp;amp;A hiring across North America, but your versatility allows you to quickly master new markets as priorities shift. We want a recruiter who builds high-performing teams, challenges assumptions with market data, and empowers leaders to make better hiring decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Full-Cycle Recruiting Across G&amp;amp;A: Lead hiring across key G&amp;amp;A functions, including Finance, Legal, and compliance, with a focus on quality, urgency, and candidate experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive Sourcing: Build deep pipelines of passive talent rather than relying primarily on inbound candidates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market Intelligence: Map relevant talent markets and provide insight on competitor organizations, candidate availability, compensation, location, and market dynamics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trusted Advisor: Act as a trusted partner to hiring managers—knowing when to challenge, when to influence, and when to align and move.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-Driven Recruitment: Use funnel data and recruiting insights to identify issues early and recommend practical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Partnership: Partner across Recruiting, People, Compensation, and the broader business to solve hiring challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team Enablement: Contribute beyond your own requisitions by mentoring others, sharing market expertise, and improving how we work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience: You bring 8+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, preferably within high-growth technology, fintech, or payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Versatility: You have successfully recruited across multiple business domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder Management: You can quickly learn a new business, product, or talent segment, translate that into an effective strategy, and build credibility quickly with senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market Mapping &amp;amp; Data: You are an exceptional sourcer who uses data and market intelligence to shape strategy, influence stakeholders, and make better decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Adaptability: You communicate clearly and directly (even in difficult conversations), challenge constructively without friction, and remain adaptable and low-ego.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High Bar: You care deeply about candidate experience, maintain high professionalism, and are energized by ambiguity in fast-moving environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in our &lt;strong&gt;San Francisco office&lt;/strong&gt;. Adyen is an office-first company and values the speed, connection and collaboration that comes from working together in person.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
