&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Recruitment Business Partner (Japan market)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Senior Recruitment Business Partner to drive regional growth across APAC (Commercial, Operations &amp;amp; Staff), with a dedicated focus on the &lt;strong&gt;Japan market.&lt;/strong&gt; At Adyen, we empower you to implement your ideas, take ownership of your career, and continuously learn. You&#39;ll experience a fast-paced, open-minded work environment that fosters innovation and collaboration. As a Senior Recruitment Business Partner, you will collaborate closely with our APAC hiring teams to identify, attract, and hire top talent, playing a pivotal role in shaping the future of our growing organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As a senior member of the team, you will own the end-to-end recruitment strategy for Japan. Beyond this primary focus, you will leverage your regional expertise to oversee delivery and talent acquisition efforts across our broader APAC markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will make an impact sourcing &amp;amp; long-term pipeline for the best candidates in the market and help fill roles to build the APAC team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a primary talent advisor to leadership and HRBPs, directing recruitment strategies that elevate the quality of talent across APAC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Beyond filling roles, you ensure the quality of hire by translating recruitment data and market intelligence into actionable coaching for hiring managers, fostering a culture of data-informed decision-making.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will be responsible for the candidates’ experience from their first contact with Adyen to the offer management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As a global team member with the recruitment team, you share best practices and market intelligence to upskill the broader team beyond APAC&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring significant full-cycle recruiting experience, including at least 4+ years &lt;strong&gt;in-house&lt;/strong&gt; within fast-paced tech, SaaS, or global organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable operating in a high-ownership environment proactively sourcing and engaging talent across niche and competitive markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business fluency in &lt;strong&gt;Japanese (native or JLPT N1 equivalent)&lt;/strong&gt; is strongly preferred to effectively partner with local stakeholders and candidates in Japan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience living or working in Japan is a plus, as it provides the cultural context necessary to navigate the local talent market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You built talent pipelines from scratch, conducting market mapping, and influencing hiring decisions in competitive hiring environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You strategically collaborate with HRBPs, Rewards and the Business ensuring our APAC talent strategy is aligned with long-term business goals.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a wealth of experience in collecting Recruiting data and leading data informed conversations to support and influence hiring decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
